he\nMiddle Mountains themselves are the highest point in the\n                                                                        •   There must be one leader (Elder) chosen when the\nEmpire and their peaks are inhabited by a large number of\n                                                                            warband is first founded (if the leader is killed see\nOgres.\n                                                                            below)\nOstland’s isolation has greatly shaped its inhabitants and they\n                                                                        •   There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nare a poor but hardy folk. Each small village lives barely above\n                                                                            for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nsubsistence levels and is usually composed of one large\n                                                                            example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nextended family. The men of Ostand are tall and broad-\n                                                                            to four champions.\nshouldered while the women tend to either be tall and whippet\n                                                                        •   The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\nthin or short and stout. Married men are usually dirt farmers\n                                                                            be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nwho also gather roots, tubers and nuts in the forests, while\n                                                                            warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nunmarried men spend their lives as trappers and hunters. The\n                                                                            the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nworship of Taal, the god of Forests and Beasts, is very popular\n                                                                        •   A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\nin the region, although there is also some worship of Taal’s\n                                                                            weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nwife Ryha, and his brother Ulric in the the more westerly\n                                                                            up the space of two weapons.\nvillages.\n                                                                        •   Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\n                                                                            is shown before the name. For example, 0-1 Priest of\nWhile not warlike by nature, Ostlanders are never opposed to a\n                                                                            Ulric. The maximum number of Priests of Ulric in a\ngood honest drunken brawl and with their love of dark ales\n                                                                            warband is therefore 1.\nthese sorts of scraps are not uncommon. During the Great War\nagainst Chaos, Ostlanders rallied in great numbers to wield\nbow and spear in defence of their Kislevite neighbours. More\nthan any other part of the Empire, Ostland has tasted the lash\nof Chaos and their hatred of the evil ones knows no bounds.\n\n[Page 90]\nHeroes\n\n                          1 Elder                                                0~1 Priest of Taal\nCOST TO HIRE: 125 Gold Crowns.                                      COST TO HIRE: 50 Gold Crowns.\nIn Ostland, the oldest (or more often biggest) man in the           It is said that every priest of Taal is born during the darkest\nvillage is given the title ‘Elder’. His word is greatly respected   phase of the moon. Those who are accepted into the service\nand only at his urging would the manhood of an entire village       of Taal are loners by nature and spend their time wandering\npack up and travel to Mordheim to seek their fortune.               the untamed forests of the Northern Empire. It is unclear\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W     I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT      why the priests of the forest have begun to join bands of\n 4     4     4    4   3    2   4    3    8     8     7       7      Ostlanders in their delving into the ruined city of Mordheim\n                                                                    — for the servants of Taal keep their own counsel. Suffice to\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                              say that the Forest-God is clearly building a strong presence\nAn Elder starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close          both in and around the darkened ruins as more animals begin\nCombat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Special Weapons,                   to fill the surrounding forests.\nArmour, and Wargear from the Ostlander Equipment List.               M    WS    BS   S   T   W     I   A   LD   CL    WIL    INT\n                                                                     4     2     3   3   3    2   3    1    7    8      8      8\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Human), Leader                                                WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                    A Priest of Taal starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                     Close Combat Weapons, from the Ostlander Equipment List.\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does        SPECIAL RULES:\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.                            Race (Human), Champion, Priest (Cast Spells Prayers of\n                                                                    Taal), may never wear armour.\n                  Blood Brothers                                    STARTING SKILL:\nCOST TO HIRE: 80 Gold Crowns.                                       When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nOstland villages are usually composed of a single extended          Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nfamily. Everyone is everyone else's uncle, cousin or brother        not increase the warrior’s credit value.\n(and sometimes their own!). Rather than trying to keep all of\nthese relations straight, the most respected men in the village                          Youngbloods\n(aside from the Elder) are referred to simply as Blood-\nbrothers.                                                           COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W     I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT      These are young warriors who are still inexperienced, but\n 4     4     3    3   3    2    4   2    8     7     7       7      eager to win their spurs in the savage fighting in and around\n                                                                    the ruins of Mordheim.\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                               M    WS    BS   S   T   W     I   A   LD   CL    WIL    INT\nA Sergeant starts with no equipment. They may purchase               4     2     2   3   3    1   3    1    6    6      6      6\nClose Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Special Weapons,\nArmour, and Wargear from the Ostlander Equipment List.              WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                    A Youngblood starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                      Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Spceial weapons,\nRace (Human), Champion                                              Armour, and Wargear from the Ostlander Equipment List.\n\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                     SPECIAL RULES:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their          Race (Human ), Raw Recruit.\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.","equipment":["Axe","Club","Dagger","Great Axe","Great Hammer","Great Sword","Hammer or Mace","Spear","Staff","Sword","Heavy armour","Light armour","Bow","Blunderbuss","Handgun","Hochland long rifle","Pistol","Shield","Lantern","Rope and hook","Bottle of rotgut"],"displayName":"Ostland","warriors":[{"id":"elder","name":"Elder","type":"Leader","max":1,"cost":125,"profile":[4,4,4,4,3,2,4,3,8,8,7,7],"access":"Ostlander Equipment List"},{"id":"priest-of-taal","name":"Priest of Taal","type":"Champion","max":1,"cost":50,"profile":[4,2,3,3,3,2,3,1,7,8,8,8],"access":"Ostlander Equipment List"},{"id":"blood-brother","name":"Blood Brother","type":"Champion","max":2,"cost":80,"profile":[4,4,3,3,3,2,4,2,8,7,7,7],"access":"Ostlander Equipment List"},{"id":"youngblood","name":"Youngblood","type":"Raw Recruit","max":2,"cost":20,"profile":[4,2,2,3,3,1,3,1,6,6,6,6],"access":"Ostlander Equipment List"},{"id":"kin","name":"Kin","type":"Henchman","max":null,"cost":35,"profile":[4,3,3,3,3,1,3,1,7,7,7,7],"access":"Ostlander Equipment List"},{"id":"jaeger","name":"Jaeger","type":"Henchman","max":7,"cost":35,"profile":[4,3,3,3,3,1,3,1,7,7,7,7],"access":"Ostlander Equipment List"},{"id":"ruffian","name":"Ruffian","type":"Henchman","max":5,"cost":25,"profile":[4,2,2,3,3,1,2,1,6,7,6,6],"access":"Ostlander Equipment List"},{"id":"ogre","name":"Ogre","type":"Henchman","max":1,"cost":120,"profile":[6,3,2,4,4,3,3,2,7,5,7,4],"access":"Ostlander Equipment List"}]},{"id":"possessed","name":"Possessed","title":"Possessed Warbands","equipmentTitle":"The Possessed Equipment List","startPage":54,"equipmentPage":96,"text":"[Page 54]\nMain Gauche                                                 Ithilmar mail\nA stout, off-hand dagger forged for defence rather than     Ithilmar is a silvery metal which is as light as silk and\noffence, the main gauche—or \"left hand\"—is built to         stronger than steel. Elves are experts at fashioning\nturn aside blades in the chaos of close combat. Thicker     weapons and armour from ithilmar, and the Elven\nand more rugged than a standard dagger, it must             kingdom of Caledor is the only place in the world where\nwithstand the crushing force of incoming strikes.           this metal can be found.\nThough not meant to deal damage, in the hands of a\nskilled duellist, it becomes a lifeline—deflecting lethal   Armour Save: 5+ armour save.\nblows that would otherwise maim or kill. Mastery of the\nmain gauche demands precision, speed, and nerve.\n       Weapon             Range        Str   D     AP\n                                                                         Sigmarite armour\n    Main Gauche          Melee 1       S-1   1     +1       Sigmarite armour is a type of heavy plate armour that\n                                                            also bears the Seal of Sigmar.\nTraits: Parry, Training (4)\n                                                            Armour Save: Sigmarite armour grants a 5+ armour\n                                                            save.\n                Sword breaker                               Nullify Spell: The warrior gains the Magic Resistance\n                                                            (5) special rule.\nA rare and wickedly serrated dagger, the Swordbreaker\n                                                            Encumbered: due to the extra weight of this armour, the\nis crafted to catch and twist an opponent’s blade rather\n                                                            warrior’s Initiative is reduced by 1 and their movement\nthan simply deflect it. Its comb-like teeth can trap\n                                                            by 1’’ when making a Charge action.\nweapons mid-swing, giving a skilled fighter the chance\n                                                            (Priests of Sigmar, Witch Hunters, or Sister’s of Sigmar\nto wrench the enemy’s sword from their grasp. In the\n                                                            only.)\nright hands, the Swordbreaker turns defence into\nsudden, decisive control—perfect for duellists who\nfavor precision and technique..                                             Chaos armour\n        Weapon            Range      Str     D     AP\n                                                            Chaos Armour is a suit of strangely wrought and\n    Sword Breaker        Melee 2     S-1     1     +1\n                                                            unnatural metal. It is the mark of a Dark God's favour.\n                                                            While most suits of Chaos Armour are received as Gifts\nTraits: Disarm, Parry, Training (4)\n                                                            from an Infernal Patron, they can be acquired, though\n                                                            only from Chaos Dwarfs in an exclusive exchange for\n         Gromril plate armour                               many captives or perhaps some impossible deed to\n                                                            further their interests.\nKnown by other races as Silverstone or hammernought\n                                                            Armour Save: Chaos armour grants a 5+ save roll.\narmour, the metal the Dwarfs call gromril is the\n                                                            Gift of Chaos: Chaos armour becomes fused to the body\ntoughest and sturdiest in the world. Armour forged of\n                                                            of its wearer. It can never be removed.\npure gromril is highly coveted for its protective value\n                                                            Ensorcelled- The warrior wearing Chaos Armour can\nand such suits are treasured heirlooms, many of which\n                                                            still perform the action Cast Spell (X).\ndate back to the Golden Age.\n                                                            (Possessed Warbands only)\nGromril is the rarest and strongest metal known of in\nthe Old World. Only a very few Dwarf smiths know the\nsecret of forging gromril, and a suit of armour made                            Fur cloak\nfrom it fetches a huge price.\n                                                            Fur cloaks range from the wolf cloaks of the warriors of\n                                                            Ulric, to bear cloaks of Kislev warriors. These grim\nArmour Save: Gromril armour grants a 4+ save roll.\n                                                            warriors are famously contemptuous of missiles fired at\n                                                            them.\n\n                                                            Armour Save: A warrior wearing a Wolf Cloak will gain\n                                                            +1 to their armour saves against all shooting attacks, as\n                                                            long as they are not using a shield.\n\n[Page 55]\nMiscellaneous Equipment\nThis section covers all the strange and unusual equipment your warriors can find in the ruins or buy from the merchants and\npedlars in the settlements and villages around Mordheim.\nNote: A warrior can only own one item of each type. For example, a warrior cannot own two Lucky Charms.\nOnly Heroes may buy and carry the equipment described in this section. You may not give it to Henchmen unless the rules\nspecifically say so.\n\n             Aethyric repository                                                Blessed water\nAn Aethyric Repository is an object enchanted by a            The priests of Sigmar, Mórr and Shallya hold great power\nwizard and used to store his magical power. They can          over evil. A vial of pure water from a clear fountain,\ntake many forms, an enchanted skull, a wand, a staff or       blessed by one of these priests, is said to burn things of\nother arcane item. A Wizard with a Aethyric Repository        darkness and evil.\ncan focus the winds of magic and store Aethyric power         A warrior with Blessed Water can make a missile\nwithin it to be used later.                                   weapon attack with the following profile:\nIf a Wizard with a Aethyric Repository casts a spell or is\nthe target of a spell, place a token on their Warrior card      Weapon                 Range       Str      AP       D\nafter working out the effects of the spell. Once there is       Blessed Water            8          4       -6       1\nat least one token on the warrior’s card, they can\nattempt to use the Aethyric Repository whenever they          Traits: Balanced, Blessed,\ncast a spell.                                                 Blessed water only affects Undead and Daemonic\nTo trigger the Aethyric Repository, the warrior makes a       warriors. No armour saves are allowed. After using it,\nTAP AETHYRIC REPOSITORY (Basic) Action and                    remove from their Warrior card.\nrolls a D6. If the result is equal to or lower than the       Undead, Skaven or Possessed warbands (and any other\nnumber of tokens on their Warrior card, the Aethyric          evil race) may not use blessed water.\nRepository is triggered, otherwise there is no effect.\nWhen the Aethyric Repository is triggered, remove all\nAethyric Repository tokens from the warrior’s card and\n                                                                                Bodkin arrows\nimmediately use one of the warrior’s spells just as if they   A bodkin point is a type of arrowhead. A typical bodkin\nhad taken the Cast Spell (X) action. This action does not     is a square-section arrowhead tapering down the tip.\nrequire the warrior to make a Willpower check.                Bodkin point arrows were designed to punch though Mail\nIf there are ever six tokens on the warrior’s card, the       and Plate armour.\nAethyric Repository immediately explodes! Remove all          A warrior with Bodkin Arrows has an extra - 1AP.\nthe tokens and the Aethyric Repository from the               Bodkin arrows can only be used with bows; Bow, Short\nwarrior’s card and roll an Injury dice for the warrior.       Bow, Long Bow, Elf Bow.\n\n           Amulet of protection                                                  Chain cilice\nA common custom in the Old World is to wear amulets           The cilice is an “instrument of mortification” It is a chain\nto ward away harm. These take many shapes; a few              or strap with small spikes on it that point inwards worn\nbones from fallen comrades, evil idols, religious symbols,    by Priests and very devout followers around their thigh as\nwarpstone amulets or carved heads of ancient Dwarf            a form of penance The pain helps them to focused.\ngods. For the really desperate and gullible, such oddities    A warrior with a Chain Cilice may reroll any failed\ncan usually be purchased from pedlars and minor hedge         Willpower check. But each time it is used must make a\nwizards, but they are often fakes.                            Toughness check or gain a flesh wound.\nThe warrior gains the Magic Resistance (6) special rule.      (Priest or Sisters of Sigmar only.)\nIf the warrior already has the Magic Resistance special\nrule, then they can add +1 to it. For example, Magic\nResistance (5) would become Magic Resistance (4).\n\n[Page 56]\nConcealed blade                                                         Garlic\nIf the warrior is captured at the end of a battle, they can    Garlic is a common herb grown in most gardens of the\nattempt to escape. Roll a D6:                                  Empire, although hard to find in Mordheim. It is said to\n     • 1 or 2, they are unsuccessful.                          ward off Vampires and other denizens of the dark.\n     • 3 or 4, they can escape but are injured in the          A warrior with the Vampiric Special Rule must pass a\n         process – make a Lasting Injury roll for them.        Willpower check or it will be unable to charge a warrior\n     • 5 or 6, they escape.                                    carrying a clove of garlic.\nA warrior who escapes is no longer Captured, however,          Garlic lasts for the duration of one battle only.\ntheir Concealed Blade is lost and deleted from their\nWarrior card.\n                                                                             Impressive cloak\n                 Dispel scroll                                 Some rich warband warriors like to flaunt their wealth\n                                                               and purchase clothes made out of silk from distant\nA wizard with a Dispel Scroll may attempt to Dispel an         Cathay, or exotic furs, or something else eye-catching and\nenemy wizard’s successfully Cast Spell. An Engaged,            expensive.\nBroken or Seriously Injured wizard may not attempt to          Should this warrior make a Trade action in the post-\nDispel a Cast Spell (See Magic section above). Priests         battle sequence, they add an additional +1 modifier to\ncannot use Dispel Scrolls.                                     the dice roll to determine the rarity of the items on\nTo Dispel a successfully Cast Spells (X) action, a wizard      offer.\nmust roll 2D6 and can subtract -2 from the roll. If the        However, if the warrior is taken out of action, roll a D6.\ntotal is lower than the total rolled for the Willpower         On a roll of 1-2 the clothes are ruined and deleted from\ncheck made to successfully perform the action, the Cast        their Warrior card.\nSpell is Dispelled and fails as if the wizard making the\naction had failed their own Willpower check. If the total\nis equal to or higher than the total of the Willpower\n                                                                                  Holy tome\ncheck made to successfully perform the action, the             Books of prayers and descriptions of the holy deeds of\nDispel attempt fails and the Cast Spells (X) action is         religious heroes like Sigmar Heldenhammer are copied by\nresolved. There is no chance of a Magical Miscast when         hand in the scriptoriums of Sigmar and Ulric and given\nusing a Dispel Scroll.                                         or sold to the faithful. Of these tomes, the Testaments of\nOnce a Dispel Scroll has been used it crumbles to dust         Sigmar is the most common and well known, but other\nand is deleted from the Warrior’s card. A wizard can           texts such as the Scriptures of Sigmar are also sold to\nonly own one Dispel Scroll.                                    those who follow the faith. A holy man can recite his\n                                                               prayers from such a book, strengthening his faith and\n                   Elven cloak                                 belief.\n                                                               Any Priest with a holy tome can apply -1 to the 2D6 roll\nMade from the hair of Elven maidens and interwoven             when determining whether they can cast a Prayer\nwith living tree leaves, an Elven cloak is a wonder to         successfully or not.\nbehold. A warrior wearing such a cloak will blend into\nthe shadows, making it very difficult to shoot at them\nwith missile weapons. Elven cloaks rarely come up for\n                                                                              Hunting arrows\nsale but are sometimes recovered from dead warriors or         The best hunting arrows are made by the hunters of\noffered by Elves as rewards to men who have served them        Drakwald forest. They have sharp, barbed arrowheads\nin some way.                                                   which cause excruciating pain when they hit their target.\nIf the wearer of an Elven cloak did not move during            A skilled archer can severely injure his target with a\ntheir activation, ranged attacks made against them             single arrow.\nsuffer a -2 to hit until the start of their next activation.   A warrior using a short bow, bow, long bow or Elf bow\n                                                               may use these arrows. The weapon gains the Rending\n                                                               weapon trait.\n\n[Page 57]\nLantern                                               Mordheim map\nIn the gloomy dark of Mordheim, the light from a lantern    Some survivors of the cataclysm still remain in the many\nhelps boost the warrior’s morale.                           settlements around Mordheim and make a living by\nAll friendly warriors in 6” gain +1 Cool (to maximum        preparing maps of the city from memory. Many of these\nof 10). If a warrior with a Lantern is a sentry in a        maps are faked, and due to the ever-changing layout of\nscenario that uses the Sentries special rule, the D6 roll   the city due to buildings falling down, even real maps are\nto see whether a warrior is spotted has a +1 modifier (a    often crude and inaccurate.\nnatural 1 still fails)                                      A map can help a warband find their way through the\nA lantern counts as an off-hand weapon, the warrior may     confusing maze of streets and into areas with rich\nnot use an additional hand weapon in close combat. And      buildings to loot.\nit takes up the space of one weapon when equipping\nwarriors.                                                   When you buy a map, roll a D6:\n\n\n                 Lucky charm                                 D6\n                                                             1\n                                                                    Result\n                                               