worse.                                 Relic, this must be either the warband Leader or a\n                                                             Champion. This symbol of dedication and devotion\n\n              Religious symbol                               serves to inspire warband members to greater acts in\n                                                             battle. When the Leader or Champion carrying the relic\nIn this age of superstition and religious fanaticism holy    makes a group activation, they may activate one\nobjects are an important part of life. They take many        additional Readied warrior within 3\", meaning that the\nforms, from prayer beads to pendants of the Horned Rat.      Leader may activate three additional warriors whilst a\nAll are sold to those needing encouragement during           Champion may activate two additional warriors.\nbattle. Often worn on thong or chain around the neck, a\nwarrior only needs touch the symbol to reassert their                           War trophies\nfaith and courage.\nThe warrior may add +1 to Fear check.                        Trophies are a popular device and charm for warriors,\n                                                             these can range from taking body parts to taking trinkets\n                                                             and tokens from those the warrior has slain.\n                  Rope & hook                                The intent may be to demonstrate dominance over the\nA warrior using a rope & hook will find it much easier to    deceased (such as necklaces of severed ears, knuckle bones\nmove amongst the ruins of Mordheim.                          or teeth), to humiliate or intimidate the enemy (such as\nAn Active warrior with a Rope and Hook can perform           shrunken heads or skull cups). It is usually done to prove\nthe following actions:                                       the warrior’s body count in battle, or to boast their\nGrapnel (Double) – The warrior can move up to 12’’ in        prowess and achievements. This represents the warrior\na straight line, in any direction. This move can take        with the most, and the most impressive, war trophies in\nthem to a different level, as long as they do not move       your warband.\nthrough any terrain. This may also be used to move the       A warrior with War Trophies has +1 WS. May not be\nwarrior into base-to-base contact with another warrior,      used by warriors that are Immune to Psychology. There\nin which case they become Engaged, but do not                is only one warrior who can have the most war trophies,\nimmediately perform close combat attacks.                    therefore there is only one War Trophies per warband.\nAn Active warrior with a Rope and Hook can make the\nfollowing action while they are within 1’’ of the edge of               Superior blackpowder\na platform:\nDescend (Basic) – The warrior makes a move of up to          The warrior has acquired a powder horn of fine grained\n3’’ horizontally and up to 12’’ vertically. Any vertical     blackpowder, which is better quality than is normally\nmovement must be downwards, i.e. towards the                 available. However, it is also more volatile.\nground.                                                      The weapon gains the Hack and Rending weapon traits.\n                                                             But when rolling to hit, if a natural 1 is rolled then the\n                                                             weapon may have misfired. Make an INT check with a -\n                                                             2 penalty, if failed roll on the Blackpowder Weapon\n                                                             Misfires table (see Blackpowder weapon trait).\n                                                             There is enough Superior Blackpowder to last for one\n                                                             game.\n\n[Page 59]\nTome of magic                                                     War horn\nA grimoire is a tome of arcane knowledge, used by            The blaring sound of a war horn can be enough to stir\nwizards to study the magical arts. Usually, massive tomes    the hearts of any warband which it is attempting to\nbound in strange leather (sometimes Human skin or            bolster. It grants men courage and gives them the will to\nDaemon hide), they are offered for sale in the markets       fight on defiantly.\nand dark alleys of the settlements around Mordheim.          A warrior equipped with a War horn can perform the\nMany are fakes, or contain little useful information, but    following action Blow Horn (Basic):\na rare few contain something useful. However, studying       SOUND HORN (Basic) - Each friendly warrior that is\nthese books is not without risk, the wizard could lose his   currently subject to the Broken condition and within\nmind, or his life, or something far worse.                   12’’ can make a Leadership check if passed they\nA Wizard with a Tome of Magic can make an                    immediately recover from being Broken.\nIntelligence check with a-2 penalty, if passed they will     A warband may only own one War Horn. Signals\ngain an extra spell permanently. The wizard may              coming from two or more War Horns would just get\nrandomly generate this new spell from their own list of      confusing.\nspells or the Lesser Magic list. See the Magic section for\ndetails. After making the Intelligence check remove\nfrom their Warrior card.\n                                                                       Wyrdstone pendulum\nHowever, when making the Intelligence check, if the          Pendulums made of wyrdstone can reputedly be used to\nWizard rolled a double 6, then the grimoire they are         find even more of the magical stone.\nreading turns out to be a forbidden tome which takes a       In the post-battle sequence, a warrior equipped with a\ntoll on the readers sanity The wizard reduces his            Wyrdstone Pendulum can re-roll one dice in the\nWillpower by -1 permanently.                                 Exploration phase, as long as the warrior is not\n                                                             Captured or In Recovery.\n\n[Page 60]\nAnimals\nAnimals are not often offered for sale in Mordheim. The polluted grass and filthy water cause most animals to die quickly, and since\nhunger is commonplace, many have been butchered for food. However, some horses occasionally go on sale for wealthy leaders who\nenjoy commanding their subordinates from horseback.\n\nAnimals are purchased as Wargear and should be recorded on their owner’s Warrior card accordingly. However, where Animals\ndiffer to normal Wargear is that they will have their own Warrior card, which details their unique stats, skills, and weaponry.\nThey follow all of the normal rules for a warrior, with the following exceptions:\n\n    •    Whenever the warrior that owns the Animal is selected for a scenario, the Animal may also be deployed. This may take\n         the number of warriors in a starting crew above the number specified by the scenario.\n    •    Animals can only be activated as part of a Group Activation with their owner. Accordingly, the owner of an Animal gains\n         the following special rule:\n              - Group Activation (Animals): When a warrior with this special rule is activated, their controlling player must\n                  activate all Animals belonging to this warrior as well as part of a ‘Group Activation’:\n              - The controlling player selects and activates each warrior in this group activation as normal, fully resolving each\n                  activation before selecting and activating the next. Each warrior activates individually; groups do not activate\n                  simultaneously.\n              - If this warrior itself is activated as part of a Group Activation, this rule still applies, meaning any Animals this\n                  warrior owns are activated as described above when this warrior is itself activated as part of a Group Activation.\n    •    Animals must always end their activation within 6\" of their owner. If the Animal is more than 6\" away at the end of its\n         activation, it must pass a Nerve test or become Broken.\n    •    Should an Animal become Broken, it will run towards its owner when activated rather than for cover. When an Animal\n         makes a Running for Cover (Double) action, it runs towards its owner. It is only concerned with getting back within 6\" of\n         its owner.\n    •    An Animal that has become Broken automatically rallies if it ends an activation within 6\" of its owner (note that, during\n         Campaign play, Animals do not gain XP for rallying in this way).\n    •    If the owner is removed from the battlefield for any reason, the Animal is also removed from play.\n    •    If an Animal is removed from the battlefield for any reason, it is not counted for the purposes of Rout tests.\n    •    Animals suffer Lasting Injuries as a normal Henchmen.\n    •    Animals may not take any additional equipment. They may not use weapons other than those detailed on their profile.\n         They may never use Wargear.\n    •    Animals can be taken Captive, in which case the owning warrior’s warband can attempt to rescue them and the capturing\n         warband may sell them as if they were a normal warrior. Animals taken Captive cannot be put to work in any Territories.\n    •    A warrior can own up to 2 Animals.\n    •    Maximum of 5 Animals per warband.\n\n[Page 61]\npart in the game.\n                                                                       •    Any warrior with a Hatred to Daemons will also hate\n                                                                            the Wizard that owns the familiar.\nFamiliars are intelligent magical entities created to serve a          •    Wizards only ever have a single familiar.\nspellcaster. Wizards are often solitary, usually shunned by            •    Only warriors with the Wizard Special rule can own\nthose who can barely conceive of, much less understand, the                 a familiar.\npower these individuals wield. The nature of Wizards\nfamiliars can vary - some take a physical object and summon        WARRIOR FAMILIAR\na Aetheric Spirit directly into it, bringing it to life. Other     These familiars act as bodyguards and squires to their\nwizards create the familiar from their own imagination,            masters. This magical bodyguard usually takes the form of a\nliterally fashioning it via magic power. Others bind small         diminutive warrior in full plate armour or a tiny monstrous\nanimals and pets. to their will                                    creature. Despite their small stature they can carry full sized\n                                                                   swords and axes and are fully capable of using them.\nAll Wizard’s Familiars are treated as ordinary Equipment and       Special Rules: When the Wizard is engaged in close combat\nshould be recorded on their owner’s Warrior card                   the Warrior Familiar can make one WS6 attack with S5\naccordingly. All Wizard’s Familiars have the following rules:      Weapon Traits: Magical. Simply roll one extra hit dice the\n                                                                   Warrior Familiar, ideally of a different colour to those being\n    •    Wizard’s Familiars must be represented by a               used for the warrior, to represent the Familiar making a close\n         separate model that must stay within 2’’ of the           combat attack.\n         owning warrior. This is not a warband warrior or\n         friendly model; it is purely a marker representing        POWER FAMILIAR\n         the wizard’s Familiar and matters only for its own        A power familiar attracts raw magic power to it’s owner.\n         line of sight and targeting purposes. Nor will they       They are magical energy reservoirs who can assist their\n         give away their owner’s location as they are assumed      masters to cast spells and understand magic. They tend to be\n         to be aware enough of stealthy movement to                shy and retiring who seek safety at the slightest hint of\n         emulate it and remain very low and close when             danger.\n         needed.                                                   Special Rules: A wizard with a power familiar is allowed to\n    •    When the owner activates it, the Wizard’s Familiar        re-roll one D6 when performing the action Cast Spell (X).\n         will move with them, Wizard’s Familiars ignore all\n         terrain, and can never fall.                              SPELL FAMILIAR\n    •    Wizard’s Familiars cannot be targeted by shooting         A spell familiar memorises a spell on it’s master’s behalf,\n         or melee attacks and can never be Engaged in              offering its master a better choice of deadly spells to unleash\n         combat – they simply move away.                           in battle. Spell Familiars are usually curious and affectionate\n    •    Wizard’s Familiars may be caught by a Blast marker        creatures that enjoy being fussed over.\n         or Flame template. If a wizard’s Familiar is caught       Special Rules: The owner knows one more spell than he is\n         under a Blast marker or Flame template, the attacker      normally allowed. Roll on the Lesser Magic chart or the same\n         should roll a D6. On a 4-6, it is hit by the attack. On   chart the wizard uses.\n         a 1-3, it is able to move clear of the area of the\n         attack. Leave the model where it is and assume it has\n         bobbed around and returned to where it was. If a\n         wizard’s Familiar is hit in this way, the owning\n         player rolls a D6. On a 1, it is destroyed and should\n         be removed from the owning warrior’s Warrior\n         card. On a 2-6, it is taken Out of Action and plays\n         no further part in the game, but otherwise suffers no\n         long-term effects.\n    •    If a familiar is taken Out of Action the Aetheric\n         shock is so great it can cause the wizard to\n         temporarily lose his mind. The wizard suffers from\n         Stupidity for the remainder of the game.\n    •    If the owning Wizard leaves the table for any reason,\n         including being taken Out of Action, the Wizard’s\n         Familiar will accompany them and takes no further\n\n[Page 62]\nTrained Bear                                                               Wardog\nThe men of the Empire have used trained bears for                  The men of the Empire have always been experts at raising\nentertainment for many years; They are used as Dancing             ferocious bloodhounds to guard their cattle and holdings\nbears and even bear baiting. The poor animals are often            against roaming Goblins and Beastmen. A highly trained\ndressed up in human clothes sometimes with musical                 wardog is a dangerous opponent, trained to bite down on an\ninstruments tied to their paws. A great many bears were            opponent’s weapon hand, good at sniffing out enemy in\nbrought into the city for the festivities before the comet         hiding, and worth its weight in gold in Mordheim.\nstruck. After the destruction of Mordheim these beasts were\nsometimes found roaming the streets without their owners,           M    WS    BS   S    T   W    I   A   LD    CL   WIL    INT\nthey were rounded up and sold onto warband leaders. These           6    4     0    3    3   1    4   1   5     5    5      4\nanimals are extremely strong and tough, but somewhat\nunreliable due to their animalistic nature.                        Special Rules: War B