ch men have to lose if they pledge\ntheir souls to the dark gods of Chaos! In the aftermath of the      There are few sights as horrific as a cult warband. Deranged\ndestruction of Mordheim all manner of mutants have appeared         warriors smeared with blood and dirt wave jagged weapons\nwhilst many hitherto unblemished folk feel the stirring of          and chant blasphemous rites as they throw themselves upon\nstrange powers, the first awakenings of magical gifts destined      their foes. Many are hardly recognisable as human, their\nto bring them to a fiery death at the hands of the Witch            bodies are so scarred and disfigured. The stigmata of mutation\nHunters.                                                            is borne by most, but the most unsettling of all are the\n                                                                    Possessed themselves – melded flesh made of men, beasts, and\nNow a leader has appeared, a new Dark Emperor, who claims           metal driven by the implacable will of a Daemon.\nlordship of the City of the Damned. He is called the\nShadowlord, Master of the Possessed, and followers of the cults\nof Chaos gather from all over the Empire to pledge their souls      Possessed Warbands\nto him. Though none know whether he is man or Daemon all\n                                                                    The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nproclaim him their saviour and eagerly seek to do his bidding.\n                                                                    To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\nAs all students of the dark arts know, it is by the power of\n                                                                    must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nmagic that creatures such as Daemons and spirits are able to\n                                                                    gold crowns unspent are added to the 