it is               be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nclaimed) even offer human sacrifices in the name of their vile\nmasters. Of all the enemies of Sigmar they are the most               WARBAND COMPOSITION\nabhorrent!                                                            The warband must follow these rules when it is created, and\nThe destruction of Mordheim has fired the Witch Hunters               when new warriors are added to the warband.\nwith a new and irresistible sense of purpose. In the light of\nevents the Grand Theogonist has proclaimed Sigmar’s                       •    There must be one leader (Witch Hunter Captain)\npunishment on the City of the Damned. The Witch Hunters                        chosen when the warband is first founded (if the\nrejoice that their crusade against widespread corruption has                   leader is killed see below)\nbeen vindicated. Now they are ready to complete Sigmar’s holy             •    There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\npurpose by destroying his enemies within the ruins of the city                 for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nitself. The Grand Theogonist has commanded the Witch                           example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nHunters to go unto that place and recover the wyrdstone for                    to four champions.\nSigmar’s temple. Their crusade also pits them into the same               •    The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\narena as their old enemies the so-called Sisters of Sigmar –                   be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nthose loathsome Daemon-worshipping she-heretics whose                          warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nvery existence is a vile affront to the majesty of Sigmar.                     the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nWitch Hunters are charismatic rabble-rousers who can soon                 •    A warrior ca