eapon) and a warrior can only make 1 attack, he does\n                                                            not get an extra attack for his left arm!\n\n                 Tail Blade                                                Weeping blades\nTail blades are small bladed, barbed, or spiked weapons\n                                                            The adepts of Clan Eshin use weapons called Weeping\ndesigned to be worn or strapped to a Skaven’s tail. Tail\n                                                            Blades; a pair of murderous swords constructed with a\nblades that are used by more affluent Skaven are often\n                                                            small amount of warpstone in their structure. A\nornamental as well as deadly, etched with glyphs and\n                                                            Weeping Blade constantly sweats a deadly corrosive\nstudded with small crystal shards and bits of\n                                                            venom.\nWarpstone. In comparison, those used by Clanrats are\nalmost always homemade.\n                                                             Weapon                   Range           Str    AP       D\n                                                             Weeping Blades           Melee 2          S      -       1\n Weapon             Range         Str      AP     D\n Tail Blade         Melee 1        S       +1     1\n                                                            Traits: Paired, Parry, Poison, Training (4)\nTraits: Additional Attack- The warrior gains one\nadditional attack with the weapon in close combat.\nDoes not count as a weapon when equipping warriors\n                                                                                    Whip\n(they can still take 3 weapons).                            A whip is a thick leather or rope cord dealing negligible\n                                                            damage, but with it, you can entangle your foes.\n                                                            Coupled with the fact it cannot be parried the whip is a\n                                                            dangerous weapon in the hands of a skilled wielder. The\n                                                            Sisters of Sigmar use whips that have steel barbs that\n                                                            the Priestesses use with great expertise.\n\n                                                             Weapon              Range          Str         AP    D\n                                                             Whip                 3”             3          +1    1\n\n                                                            Traits: Knock back, Training (3), Entangle, Two-\n                                                            Handed, Versatile\n                                                            (Melee reach 4)\n\n[Page 49]\nBlackpowder Weapons\nBlackpowder weapons are only a very recent invention in the Warhammer world. They are often unreliable and temperamental, but\nthey do hit exceedingly hard, and armour offers almost no protection, as their lead bullets can penetrate even the strongest breastplate\nor shield. Most blackpowder weapons are bought from Dwarfs at great expense, though some of the forges of Nuln and Altdorf have\nstarted to experiment with making handguns.\n\n\n                   Blunderbus                                                  Dwarf Handgun\nA blunderbuss is a primitive blackpowder weapon,                  The handguns used by Dwarf Thunderers feature many\nwhich fires a hail of lead balls, rusty bolts, bent nails,        improvements over the cruder firearms used by other\nand other assorted scrap metal. It is a powerful, if              races, including wheel-lock firing mechanisms.\ninaccurate weapon, that takes such a long time to load\nthat most warriors discard it after the first shot.                Weapon                Range       Str         AP     D\n                                                                   Dwarf Handgun          24          4          -1     1\n Weapon               Range        Str      AP       D\n Blunderbus           Temp          3        -       1            Traits: Blackpowder, Penetrating, Reliable, Reload (2)\n\nTraits: Blackpowder, Template, Reload (2)\n                                                                                   Dwarf pistol\n                       Bomb                                       They are the ideal weapon to drop a charging Orc at\n                                                                  close range. The pistols used by Dwarfs feature many\nA bomb is a hollow shell of ceramic, or this metal filled         improvements over the cruder firearms used by other\nwith gunpowder, stopped with wax and armed with a                 races, including wheel-lock firing mechanisms.\nfuse. Bombs are crude and dangerous weapons best\nused with care.                                                    Weapon               Range        Str         AP     D\n                                                                   Dwarf Pistol           8           4          -1     1\n Weapon              Range         Str      AP       D\n Bomb                  8            3       -2       1            Traits: Blackpowder, Penetrating, Pistol, Reliable,\n                                                                  Reload (2)\nTraits: Balanced, Blast (3”), Knockback, Blackpowder\n(If a Misfire is rolled treat a result of 5 (Cough cough),\nas a result of 3 (Click) instead).\n                                                                             Cathay smoke bomb\n                                                                  Skaven smoke bombs are found among clan Eshin.\n               Duelling pistol                                    Using c