     direction. They may engage an enemy but do not count as\nSHIELDWALL                                                            charging and do not fight (free) this turn.\nThis warrior may perform the BRACE (Double) action during\ntheir activation:                                                     CRIMSON HAZE\nBRACE (Double) – Until the start of this warrior’s next               If this warrior is Engaged with one or more enemy warriors,\nactivation, this warrior increases their armour save by +2 to a       they automatically pass any Panic tests they are required to\nmaximum armour save of 2+ and cannot be moved from their              take.\ncurrent location by any skills such as Hurl or Overseer, or any\nweapon traits such as Knockback or Drag, nor can they be              FEROCIOUS ASSAULT\nPinned.                                                               When this warrior makes a Charge (Double) action, they gain\n                                                                      an additional D3 Attacks. However, all their hit rolls suffer a -1\nRELENTLESS                                                            modifier.\nDuring this warrior’s activation they may attempt to perform a\nthird action after completing their first two. Roll a D6. If the      KILLING BLOW\ndice roll is equal to or less than their Toughness then they          Before rolling to hit for the warrior’s close combat attacks, the\nperform the action. If the roll is greater than their Toughness,      controlling player can opt instead to make a single Killing\nor is a 6, their activation ends immediately. Whether or not          Blow attack. This attack cannot be made with a weapon that\nthey were successful, when their activation ends, this warrior is     has the Pistol trait. If the attack hits, the attack’s Strength and\nautomatically Pinned (this Pinning cannot be negated by skills        Damage are doubled and no Armour Save roll is allowed.\nsuch as Nerves of Steel).\n                                                                      MOMENTUM\nBEAT BACK                                                             For every unsaved wound this warrior inflicts on an enemy\nThe warrior lets out a roar of rage and throws off all those          warrior with a weapon with the Melee trait, increase their\nattacking them. Opponents are forced to jump back away from           Movement by 1\" for the duration of the warriors next\nthe wild sweeps of the warrior’s weapon. This warrior may             activation.\nperform the MAKE ROOM (Basic) action while they are\nActive and Engaged:\nMAKE ROOM (Basic) The warrior makes a Strength check, if\npassed, all warriors (friend or foe) in base contact with this\nwarrior are pushed D3” directly away from this warrior,\nstopping only if they come into contact with another warrior\nor an impassable terrain feature. If there are multiple enemies\nbeing pushed, the player controlling this warrior chooses in\nwhich order they are moved.\n\nWALK IT OFF\nShould this warrior perform two or more Move (Simple)\nactions during their activation, they can make a Toughness\ncheck at the end of their activation. If this check is passed, this\nwarrior may recover one lost Wound or discard a single Flesh\nWound.\n\n[Page 74]\nStarting a warband\nBefore the campaign or skirmish begins, each player must found a warband. When founding a campaign, players will have a\nmaximum budget of Gold Crowns to spend on warriors, weapons, and wargear chosen from the entries on the following pages.\nHow much this budget is will depend upon whether the warband is bring founded for Skirmish play or Campaign play. In either\ncase, this budget may not be exceeded. Any unspent Gold Crowns will be added to the warband’s Stash if the warband has been\nfounded for Campaign play. However, if a warband has been founded for Skirmish pay, any unspent Gold Crowns are simply lost.\n\nCAMPAIGN PLAY                                                       WEAPONS AND WARGEAR\nWhen founding a warband for Campaign play, the budget               The next step is to choose and purchase the weapons and\navailable is 1,000 Gold Crowns. Note, however, that should          wargear each warrior will be equipped with. Each warrior’s\nthey wish, a Games Master can increase or decrease this             entry in some warband lists includes a detailed list of the\nbudget.                                                             weapons and Wargear that warrior may purchase; others list\n                                                                    the types of weapons and Wargear a warrior may purchase\nSKIRMISH PLAY                                                       from a general warband list.\nWhen founding a warband for Skirmish play, the budget\navailable should be agreed upon by the players. This can be as      EQUIPPING A WARRIOR\nmuch or as little as they think appropriate, but as a general       All warriors can be equipped as follows:\noutline, a budget between 1,250 and 2,000 Gold Crowns is                 • A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\nrecommended.                                                                 weapons purchased from those listed in their entry.\n                                                                         • Weapons with the two-handed trait (marked with an\nWARRIOR NAMES, CATEGORIES AND TYPES                                          asterisk (*)) take up the space of two weapons.\nEach type of warrior available to a warband is of a named type;          • Any warrior may purchase Wargear that is listed in\nthis is the name given to that warrior’s rank within the                     their entry.\nparlance of their race or warband.                                       • If the warband is founded for Campaign play,\nVery often, the rules will refer to warriors by category (Leader,            warriors will be limited to equipment lists in their\nCha