                     Race (Human), Champion, Fearless\nCOST TO HIRE: 130 Gold Crowns.\nThe Possessed have committed the greatest of heresies: they                               Mutants\nhave given their bodies to Daemons. As a result, they are\nnightmarish creatures, a melding of flesh, metal and black       COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns.\nmagic. Inside them lives a supernatural thing of evil, a         Mutants are revered as the favoured ones of the Dark gods,\nDaemon from the dark reaches of the Realm of Chaos.              their physical disfigurements marking out the vileness of\nThe powerful spirit of a Daemon can meld several creatures       their soul. They come in many shapes and sizes, each more\ntogether, be they men or animals, into a multi-faceted horror.   bizarre than the next.\nThese monstrous Possessed are perhaps the most dangerous          M    WS    BS   S   T    W   I   A   LD   CL    WIL   INT\nof the creatures of Mordheim, and certainly the most              4     2    2    3   3    1   2   1   6     6     6      6\nloathsome and dreadful.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT    WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n 5     4     1    4   4   3    4   3    7     7     8      6     A Mutant starts with no equipment. They may purchase\n                                                                 Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           Wargear from the Possessed Equipment List.\nNone. Natural Weapons\n                                                                 SPECIAL RULES:\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   Race (Human), Raw Recruit.\nRace (Possessed) Champion, Daemonic, Mutation, Large\nTarget\n\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.\n\n[Page 97]\nHenchmen\n\n                         Brethren\nCOST TO HIRE: 35Gold Crowns\nBrethren are the crazed human followers of the cults of the\ndark gods, eager to descend into damnation. Their vile deeds\nand unspeakable acts have driven them to the brink of\ninsanity.\n M    WS    BS   S   T    W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\n 4     3     3   3   3    1   3   1    7     7     7      7\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Brethren starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nClose Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nWargear from the Possessed Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Human), Henchmen\n\n\n                  0~3 Beastmen\nCOST TO HIRE: 45Gold Crowns\nBeastmen are mutated monstrosities that infest the forests of\nthe Empire: massive horned creatures with an inhuman\nresistance to pain. The destruction of Mordheim brought\nmany Beastmen into the ruined city to prey upon the\nsurvivors. They readily ally with the Magisters of the\nPossessed warbands.\n M    WS    BS   S   T    W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\n 5     4     3   3   4    1   3   1    6     7     7      6\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Beastman starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nClose Combat Weapons, Darksouls Weapons, Armour, and\nWargear from the Possessed Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Beastman), Henchmen\n\n[Page 98]\nThe Possessed Equipment List\nCLOSE COMBAT WEAPONS                                                  DARKSOULS WEAPONS\nITEM                                PRICE                             ITEM                                PRICE\nAxe                                 15                                Flail                               30\nClub                                15                                Morning Star                        30\nDagger                              10\nFlaming Torch                       25                                SPECIAL WEAPONS\nGreat Axe                           50                                ITEM                                PRICE\nGreat Hammer                        50                                Morning Star                        30\nGreat Sword                         45                                Staff                               25\nHammer Or Mace                      20\nSpear                               15                                WARGEAR\nSword                               25                                ITEM                                PRICE\n                                                                      Lantern                             40\nMISSILE WEAPONS                                                       Rope And Hook                       30\nITEM                                    PRICE\nBow                                     15\nShort bow                               10\n\nARMOUR\nITEM                                PRICE\nLight Armour                        20\nHeavy Armour                        50\nShield                              20\n\n\n\n\n                                           Possessed skill access\nPossessed warband Warriors have access to the following skills:\n                Agility     Brawn         Combat      Cunning     Ferocity    Leadership   Shooting   Academic    Resilience   Savagery\nMagsiter                                  Secondary   Secondary   Primary     Primary                 Primary\nThe Possessed   Secondary   Secondary                             Secondary                                       Primary      Primary\nDarksoul                    Primary                               Primary     Secondary                           Secondary    Secondary\nMutants                     Secondary     Secondary               Primary\nBrethren                    Secondary     Primary     Secondary   Primary\nBeastmen                    Secondary                             Primary                                         Primary      Secondary\n\n[Page 99]\nRewards of the shadowlord\nWhen a Magister, Darksoul or Mutant from a Possessed warband has accumulated enough experience, instead of picking a skill,\nthey may roll on the Rewards table below. This represents the pilgrimage of the Mutant or Magister to the Pit, where he can\nbeseech a favour from the Shadowlord himself.\n\n\n2D      Result\n6\n2       Wrath of the Shadowlord! The warrior is mutated beyond recognition and vanishes into the ruins, joining the many\n        other horrors that roam Mordheim.\n3-6     Nothing Happens. The capricious Shadowlord ignores the pleas of his servant.\n\n7-8     Mutation. The warrior develops a severe mutation. Roll a D6. On a roll of 1 you lose a single point from one of your\n        warrior’s characteristics (chosen by you), due to atrophy, or some such degrading mutation. On a roll of 2 or more you\n        may choose which one of the mutations listed in the Cult of the Possessed Warbands section your warrior has been\n        rewarded with.\n9-10    Chaos Armour. The warrior’s body becomes encrusted with an arcane, all enveloping suit of armour. This confers am\n        armour save of 4+ but does not affect the model’s ability to cast spells or move in any way.\n11      Daemon Weapon. The warrior receives a weapon with a bound Daemon inside it. The weapon has the following profile:\n\n                        Weapon                  Range              Str               AP                D\n                        Daemon Weapon           Melee 3            S+1               -1                1\n\n        Traits: Accuracy (grants a +1 bonus on all to hit rolls when using it), Magical.\n        The user may choose the weapon’s form (a sword, an axe, etc), though it will not have any of the Weapon Traits normally\n        associated with common weapons of that type.\n12      Possessed! A Daemon takes over the soul and body of the warrior. The warrior immediately gains the following:\n            • +1 Weapon Skill, +1 Strength, +1 Attacks +1 Wounds.\n            • The warrior’s race is changed to Race (Possessed). The Maximum Characteristics are now those of the Possessed.\n            • The warrior loses D3 of his skills (chosen by the player).\n            • The warrior gains the Daemonic special rules.\n            • The warrior may no longer use weapons, armour, or equipment, except for Chaos Armour or Daemon weapons.\n\n[Page 100]\nWitch hunters\nThe Order of Templars of Sigmar, universally known as the             headgear which conceal their appearance from the overly\nWitch Hunters, is an organisation dedicated to the eradication        curious. Some wear chains about their throats to remind them\nof heretics, be they warlocks, witches, sorcerers, fortune-tellers,   of fallen comrades and old rivalries and also, so it is said, so\nnecromancers, worshippers of the dark gods, deviants,                 that the iron might serve as protection against witchcraft.\nmutants, blasphemers, sinners, utterers of profanities, servants      The followers of the Witch Hunters, the rabble that accompany\nof Daemons, or composers of corrupting music. Indeed, there           them to Mordheim, are a far more dire sight indeed – crazed\nare few who altogether escape the suspicions of the Witch             and self-mutilated men who have lost or surrendered all their\nHunters with the possible exception of other Witch Hunters.           worldly goods and, most likely, their reason as well.\nIt is wise to remember that the practice of magic in all its forms\nis deemed a most heinous crime in the Empire. Death by fire is\nthe proscribed punishment for this particular heresy. Many of\nthe Witch Hunters’ victims treacherously avoid their fate by          Witch hunter Warbands\nperishing under torture before making a full confession. In           The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nthese troubled times the Witch Hunters are kept busy as more          To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\nand more men turn to th