dows when compared to the dread Vampire Lords, the         has endured for centuries. They wear ancient rust-gnawed armour,\nimmortal servants of Vlad are still some of the most powerful          corroded by time and dusty with the years. These eerie, silent\ncreatures who fight in Mordheim. Most of them serve the undying        sentinels stand constant vigil on the crumbling battlements and at\ncount of Sylvania, but some have found the city to their liking, and   the iron-bound gates, never resting, eternally ready to defend their\nhave become independent.                                               Vampire masters.\n M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT                                         M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT\n 6     5      3    4   4    2    5   3     8     8      8      8        4      3     2    3    3   2    2    2    6     5      5       5\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                                 WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Dreg starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close               A Grave Guard starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nCombat Weapons, Vampire Weapons, Armour, and Wargear                   Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nfrom the Undead Equipment List.                                        Wargear from the Undead Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                         SPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Vampire), Leader, Undead, Vampiric.                              Race (Undead) Champion, Undead ,No deal, Wight Blades.\n\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                        STARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their               When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does           Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.                               not increase the warrior’s credit value.\n\n\n                  0~1 Necromancer                                                                  Dregs\nCOST TO HIRE: 60 Gold Crowns.                                          COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns.\nNecromancers are evil wizards, studying the corrupt art of             Dregs are very useful to their masters as they can be sent to buy\nNecromancy. Many of them are acolytes and servants of Vlad von         equipment, weapons and supplies from the settlements around\nCarstein, and follow the agents of their master to the city of the     Mordheim which would often not welcome Necromancers or where\nDamned. Others are recruited from amongst wizards and warlocks         Vampires would fall under the suspicion of the Witch Hunters.\nwho have come under the suspicion of the various agents of Sigmar      They can also do the bidding of their vampiric master during\nand have fled to Mordheim to avoid persecution.                        daylight, when the Vampires must rest in their coffins.\n M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT                                        M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT\n 4     3      3    3   3    2    3   1     7     8      8      8        4      2     2    3    3   1    2    1    6     6      6       6\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                                 WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Necromance starts with no equipment. They may purchase               A Dreg starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close\nNecromancer Weapons and Wargear from the Undead                        Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and Wargear\nEquipment List.                                                        from the Undead Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                         SPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Human), Champion, Wizard (Cast Spells                            Race (Human), Raw Recruit.\nNecromancy), Fearless.\n\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.","equipment":["Axe","Bastard Sword","Club","Dagger","Great Axe","Great Hammer","Great Sword","Halberd","Hammer or Mace","Rapier","Spear","Staff","Sword","Heavy armour","Light armour","Bow","Crossbow","Buckler","Shield","Lantern","Rope and hook"],"displayName":"Undead","warriors":[{"id":"vampire","name":"Vampire","type":"Leader","max":1,"cost":180,"profile":[6,5,3,4,4,2,5,3,8,8,8,8],"access":"Undead Equipment List"},{"id":"grave-guard","name":"Grave Guard","cost":100,"type":"Champion","max":null,"profile":[4,3,2,3,3,2,2,2,6,5,5,5],"access":"Primary: Brawn, Combat · Secondary: Ferocity, Leadership, Resilience","equipment":"Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, Wargear","rules":"Race (Undead), Champion, Undead, No Deal, Wight Blades"},{"id":"necromancer","name":"Necromancer","type":"Champion","max":1,"cost":60,"profile":[4,3,3,3,3,2,3,1,7,8,8,8],"access":"Undead Equipment List"},{"id":"dregs","name":"Dregs","type":"Raw Recruit","max":null,"cost":20,"profile":[4,2,2,3,3,1,2,1,6,6,6,6],"access":"Undead Equipment List"},{"id":"crypt-ghouls","name":"Crypt Ghouls","type":"Henchman","max":null,"cost":45,"profile":[4,3,2,3,4,1,3,2,6,5,6,5],"access":"Undead Equipment List"},{"id":"zombies","name":"Zombies","type":"Henchman","max":null,"cost":20,"profile":[4,2,0,3,3,1,1,1,5,5,5,5],"access":"Undead Equipment List"},{"id":"skeleton-warriors","name":"Skeleton Warriors","cost":35,"type":"Henchman","max":null,"profile":[4,2,2,3,3,1,2,1,5,5,5,5],"access":"","equipment":"Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, Wargear","rules":"Race (Undead), Henchmen, Undead, No Brain, Summoned"},{"id":"dire-wolves","name":"Dire Wolves","type":"Henchman","max":5,"cost":45,"profile":[9,3,0,3,3,1,3,1,5,5,5,3],"access":"Undead Equipment List"}]},{"id":"skaven","name":"Skaven","title":"Skaven Warbands","equipmentTitle":"Skaven Equipment List","startPage":62,"equipmentPage":113,"text":"[Page 62]\nTrained Bear                                                               Wardog\nThe men of the Empire have used trained bears for                  The men of the Empire have always been experts at raising\nentertainment for many years; They are used as Dancing             ferocious bloodhounds to guard their cattle and holdings\nbears and even bear baiting. The poor animals are often            against roaming Goblins and Beastmen. A highly trained\ndressed up in human clothes sometimes with musical                 wardog is a dangerous opponent, trained to bite down on an\ninstruments tied to their paws. A great many bears were            opponent’s weapon hand, good at sniffing out enemy in\nbrought into the city for the festivities before the comet         hiding, and worth its weight in gold in Mordheim.\nstruck. After the destruction of Mordheim these beasts were\nsometimes found roaming the streets without their owners,           M    WS    BS   S    T   W    I   A   LD    CL   WIL    INT\nthey were rounded up and sold onto warband leaders. These           6    4     0    3    3   1    4   1   5     5    5      4\nanimals are extremely strong and tough, but somewhat\nunreliable due to their animalistic nature.                        Special Rules: War Beast, Acute Senses\n\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A    LD   CL    WIL     INT     Skills: Disarm\n 6    3     0     5   4   2    2   2    6    6     6       3       (Only Human Warbands may hire)\n\nSpecial Rules: Fear, Stupidity, War Beast\n                                                                                        Giant Wolves\nSkills: Bull Charge, Bear Hug (use Headbutt Skill)                 Warbands may only purchase Giant Wolves if they have a\n(Only Human Warbands may hire)                                     Priest of Ulric. The wolves often act as guard dogs for the\n                                                                   priest, or they are used to scout ahead for danger.\n                      Dire Wolves                                   M    WS    BS   S    T    W   I   A   LD    CL   WIL    INT\n                                                                    9     4     0   3    3    1   3   1     3   4      4         4\nCOST TO HIRE: 45 Gold Crowns\nDire Wolves are slavering Undead hounds, the animated              SPECIAL RULES:\nremains of the giant wolves of the Worlds Edge Mountains.          Acute Senses, War Beasts\nTheir chilling howls can strike fear into the hearts of even the\nbravest warriors or most ruthless Dwarf mercenaries. They\nprowl the streets of Mordheim like shadows, and many men                                Giant Rats\nhave died with the cold jaws of a Dire Wolf around their\n                                                                   Cost to hire: 15 gold crowns\nneck.\n                                                                   Giant Rats are creations of the twisted genius of the Skaven.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A    LD    CL   WIL     INT\n                                                                   They are mutated monstrosities the size of dogs. They fight\n 9     3     0    3   3    1   3    1    5     5     5      3      alongside the Skaven, overpowering any opponents by sheer\n                                                                   weight of numbers.\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                      M    WS    BS   S    T    W   I   A   LD    CL   WIL    INT\nRace (Undead), War Beasts, Undead\n                                                                    6     2     0   3    3    1   3   1     4   5      5         4\n\nSkills: Bull Charge                                                SPECIAL RULES:\n                                                                   Race (Giant Rat) War Beasts\n                                                                   (Only Skaven Warbands may hire)\n\n[Page 63]\nPoisons, potions and drugs\nThe use of poison is almost universally abhorred, but in the ruthless and brutal battles fought in Mordheim, desperate warbands often\nresort to the use of envenomed blades. Poisons need to be ingested or injected into the victims bloodstream, by a bladed weapon or\narrow to have any effect.\nNote: rules for poisons, drugs and healing:\n     • Poisons can only be applied to any one-handed weapons with a blade, such as a Dagger, Sword, Eshin Fighting Claws,\n          Rapier, and Tail Blades. And spears, whips, and to most missile weapons (bows and crossbows).\n     • Poison may not be used with Blackpowder weapons or blunt weapons (maces, hammers, clubs etc) or Great Weapons.\n     • You can only poison a single weapon with one vial of poison.\n     • When you buy a vial of poison, there is always only enough to last the duration of one battle.\n     • Witch Hunters, Priests and Sisters of Sigmar will not use poisons.\n     • Unless stated these have no effect on any warrior with Undead or Daemonic trait.\n\n\n                Apothecary Kit                                   Intoxicated    Effect\nWhen a warrior with an Apothecary Kit assists a                  Markers\nfriendly warrior’s Recovery test, roll an extra injury dice      1              Feeling Good: -1 to ranged attack hit\nthen choose one to discard.                                                     rolls, +1 to the result of Cool checks\n                                                                 2              Getting Unsteady: -2 to ranged attack\n                                                                                hit rolls, +2 to the result of Cool\n                  Black Lotus                                                   checks. If the warrior makes two Move\nIn the deepest forests of the Southlands grows a plant that                     actions in a row, they must pass an\nis extremely poisonous. It is known as Black Lotus and is                       Initiative check after completing the\nmuch sought after by alchemists, assassins, wizards of the                      second action or become Prone.\nWestern Coast and bored wives.                                   3-4            Blind Drunk: -3 to ranged attack hit\n                                                                                rolls and -1 to melee attack hit rolls, +3\nIf the hit roll for a weapon coated Black Lotus is a                            to the result of Cool checks. The\nnatural 6, the wound roll is considered to automatically                        warrior suffers from Stupidity.\nsucceed (no wound roll needs to be made). Take                   5+             Wasted: The warrior passes out. The\narmour saves as normal.                                                         warrior goes Out of Action, but counts\n                                                                                as having the Out Cold result.\n\n               Bottle of Rotgut\n                                                                               Crimson Shade\nRotgut is a particularly foul spirit made in stills in many\nplaces in the Empire. People drink rotgut for one reason       Crimson Shade is the name given by Old Worlders to the\nonly; to get stinking drunk! But distillation is a tricky      leaves of the blood oak of Estalia. It is an extremely\nprocess, and the results are often unpredictable. Poor         addictive drug but grants its users inhuman quickness\nrotgut has a good chance of permanently blinding the           and strength.\ndrinker.\n                                                               Once per game, a warrior with Crimson Shade can use\nAt the start of the warrior’s activation (before other         it when they are activated. The warrior can perform a\nchecks such as Stupidity), if this warrior is not Engaged,     Smoke Pipe (Basic) action. The warrior gains +2\nthe warrior takes a swig from the bottle. The player can       Movement, +2 Initiative, and +1 Strength for the rest of\nmake a WP check to avoid this if they wish.                    the battle. Once used remove it from the warrior’s card.\nEvery time a warrior makes this action, place an\nIntoxicated marker on their card and remove one of             Side Effects: After the battle, roll 2D6. On a roll of 2-3,\ntheir Flesh Wounds (if they have any). Intoxicated             the model becomes addicted to Crimson Shade (make a\nmarkers remain until the end of the game. Lasts one            note on the warrior’s card) and the player must try to\nbattle.                                                        buy them a new batch before every battle from now on.\nThe effects of the booze are dependent on how many             If you fail to buy any, the warrior will leave your\nmarkers they have on their card:                               warband.\n\n[Page 64]\nEssence of Garlic\nOf all the Dwarf brewmasters, Josef Bugman is the most        Garlic is a common herb grown in most gardens of the\nfamous. His ale is known throughout the Old World, and        Empire, although hard to find in Mordheim. It is said to\nwidely regarded as the best.                                  ward off Vampires and other denizens of the dark.\n(Side note: if Mordheim is set 500 years before the current\ntimeline, that makes Josef Bugman over 500 years old!         Essence of Garlic only affect warriors with the Vampiric\nEither that or he is a time traveller.)                       special rule. If the hit roll for a weapon coated in\n                                                              Essence of Garlic is a natural 6, the wound roll is\nA warrior with a keg (a small keg) of Bugman’s Ale can        considered to automatically succeed (no wound roll\nperform the Take a Swig (Simple) action. Roll a D6, on a      needs to be made). Take armour saves as normal.\nroll of a 1 or 2 the keg runs out and is empty, remove\nfrom the warrior card. Every time a warrior makes this\naction, place an Intoxicated marker on their card and\n                                                                             Healing draught\nremove one of their Flesh Wounds (if they have any).          Various healing draughts are made Herbalists,\nIntoxicated markers remain until the end of the game.         Apothecaries and witches. They can vary in quality with\nThe effects of the booze are dependent on how many            some being not much better than flavoured water.\nmarkers they have on their card:                              Some races even have their own concoctions, Skaven for\n                                                              instance, have Skalm, a mixture of healing herbs and a\n Intoxicated    Effect                                        dash of Warpdust.\n Markers\n 1              A Good Buzz: -1 to ranged attack hit          A warrior with a healing draught, that is not Engaged,\n                rolls, +2 to the result of Cool checks.       can perform the action Swig (Simple). This restores D3\n 2              Seeing Double: -1 to ranged attack hit        wounds he has previously lost during the game. Once\n                rolls, +3 to the result of Cool checks.       used remove it from the warrior’s card.\n                When making ranged attack hit rolls\n                after choosing a target, randomise the\n                actual target of the attack between the\n                                                                                  Laudanum\n                intended target and any model (friend         A soothing tincture to inure one's mind against the\n                or foe) within 6\" of them.                    horrors of the dark. Laudanum is a mixture of opium\n 3+             Trollslayer Courage!: -2 to ranged            and alcohol, used as a pain killer and cure all, but also\n                attack hit rolls, gains the Fearless          