y something more expensive.\nrarely with their sanity intact.\nIn the dimly-lit chamber of the Drakenhof castle, on a throne\n                                                                    WARBAND COMPOSITION\nof black obsidian, sits Vlad von Carstein, the ruler of Sylvania.\n                                                                    An Undead warband must follow these rules when it is created,\nHe waits in shadows, having set himself apart from the politics\n                                                                    and when new warriors are added to the warband.\nand bickering of the Empire. For he holds a terrible secret: he,\nand all the ruling aristocracy of his province are Vampires,\n                                                                        •   There must be one leader (Vampire) chosen when the\nundying monsters from beyond the grave. Here he patiently\n                                                                            warband is first founded (if the leader is killed see\nwaits, drinking the blood of maidens from gold goblets.\n                                                                            below)\nFor many long years Vlad has gathered his strength and\n                                                                        •   There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nmustered his Undead legions in secrecy. One day soon he will\n                                                                            for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nmarch from the forests of Sylvania at the head of an army of\n                                                                            example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nrestless dead. The pieces of magic stone that lie scattered\n                                                                            to four champions.\namong the ruins of Mordheim can give the Count the power to\nchallenge the nobles of the Empire and enslave the men of the           •   The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\nOld World.                                                                  be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nWyrdstone holds enough captured magical energy to unleash a                 warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\ngreat spell of doom to rival that of Nagash the Black. If the               the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nCount is successful, he will raise all the dead between the             •   A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\nWorlds Edge Mountains and the borders of Stirland, and go to                weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nwar against the divided rulers of the Empire. His plans laid out,           up the space of two weapons.\nVlad sends his thralls, the immortal Vampires, to do his                •   Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\nbidding.                                                                    is shown before the name. For example, 0-1\nDuring dark, moonless nights, black coaches arrive at the gates             Necromancer. The maximum number of\nof Mordheim carrying coffins. Ghouls scuttle from their hiding              Necromancers in a warband is therefore 1.\nplaces to greet them, and corpses are stirred by a command\nwhich the living cannot hear. Following the commands of the\nVampire, they hunt for shards of wyrdstone.\nThe night belongs to the Undead, and in Mordheim it is always\nnight.\n\n[Page 109]\nHeroes\n                        1 Vampire                                                             Grave Guard\nCOST TO HIRE: 180 Gold Crowns.                                         COST TO HIRE: 100 Gold Crowns.\nVampires lead the Undead in their search for the magical stones that   Although their bodies have decayed, leaving only bones and tattered\nwill give their master the power to conquer the Empire. Although       flesh, Grave Guard are held together by evil magic so strong that it\nbut pale shadows when compared to the dread Vampire Lords, the         has endured for centuries. They wear ancient rust-gnawed armour,\nimmortal servants of Vlad are still some of the most powerful          corroded by time and dusty with the years. These eerie, silent\ncreatures who fight in Mordheim. Most of them serve the undying        sentinels stand constant vigil on the crumbling battlements and at\ncount of Sylvania, but some have found the city to their liking, and   the iron-bound gates, never resting, eternally ready to defend their\nhave become independent.                                               Vampire masters.\n M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT                                         M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT\n 6     5      3    4   4    2    5   3     8     8      8      8        4      3     2    3    3   2    2    2    6     5      5       5\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                                 WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Dreg starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close               A Grave Guard starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nCombat Weapons, Vampire Weapons, Armour, and Wargear                   Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nfrom the Undead Equipment List.                                        Wargear from the Undead Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                         SPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Vampire), Leader, Undead, Vampiric.                              Race (Undead) Champion, Undead ,No deal, Wight Blades.\n\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                        STARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their               When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does           Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit val