wound’ as normal to determine if it is a ‘critical hit’, but even a failed ‘to wound’ roll will still cause a wound if a 6 was rolled\nfirst ‘to hit’.\nSKELETON MINOR HERO:\nA note about Grave Guard. A Grave Guard is not actually learning new skills or truly gaining experience in the traditional sense,\ninstead it can be thought of as becoming more powerful as the Necromancer continues to practice their dark arts on them, dark\nrituals that increase their strength and power. Or perhaps some of the skills they had in life are starting to return. The inverse\ngoes for Lasting Injuries, the damage done to them weakens their magical bonds.\n\n[Page 112]\nSkaven\nUnbeknownst to man, for thousands of years he has shared his\nworld with another and altogether different race. There have        The Skaven of Clan Eshin are supremely adapted to their task.\nalways been signs for those who cared to see them: a scurrying      Masters of the art of bringing silent death to their foes, they are\nblack shadow, an inhuman scream from the sewer, scuttling           skilled in the use of poison and trained in the thousand secrets\nshapes at the back of the cellar. All these years these creatures   of the assassin. Since birth Skaven warriors practise martial\nhave worked away in secret, burrowing beneath the world of          crafts in the ruinous temples of the Horned Rat, their ever\nman, undermining his great cities, infiltrating his sewers and      hungering and hideous god. There are none better amongst\ncellars, and joining all up into a vast world spanning labyrinth    their verminous kind to gather up the treasure of Mordheim,\nof tunnels and nests. These creatures call themselves Skaven        but they must be silent, swift and efficient. Were rival Skaven\nand they are ratmen, the mutant spawn of an older age of            clans to discover the secret of Mordheim there would come not\nchaos and mutation.                                                 hundreds, not thousand