ight Runner starts with no equipment. They may\npurchase Greyseer Weapons and Wargear from the Skaven            purchase Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons,\nEquipment List.                                                  Armour, and Wargear from the Skaven Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   SPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Skaven), Champion, Wizard (Cast Spells Magic of the        Race (Skaven), Raw Recruit, Scurry Away! Strength in\nHorned Rat), Scurry Away! Strength in numbers                    numbers\n\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.","equipment":["Axe","Billhook","Club","Dagger","Halberd","Spear","Staff","Sword","Light armour","Sling","Cathay Smoke bombs","Shield","Rope and hook","Black lotus","Eshin Fighting Claws","Tail Blade","Weeping Blades","Warplock Musket"],"displayName":"Skaven","warriors":[{"id":"assassin-adept","name":"Assassin Adept","type":"Leader","max":1,"cost":135,"profile":[6,4,4,3,3,2,5,3,7,6,7,6],"access":"Skaven Equipment List"},{"id":"apprentice-greyseer","name":"Apprentice Greyseer","type":"Champion","max":1,"cost":50,"profile":[5,3,3,3,3,2,4,1,6,6,8,7],"access":"Skaven Equipment List"},{"id":"black-skaven","name":"Black Skaven","type":"Champion","max":2,"cost":75,"profile":[5,4,3,3,3,2,5,2,7,5,7,6],"access":"Skaven Equipment List"},{"id":"night-runners","name":"Night Runners","type":"Raw Recruit","max":null,"cost":15,"profile":[5,2,2,3,3,1,4,1,5,4,6,5],"access":"Skaven Equipment List"},{"id":"clan-rats","name":"Clan Rats","type":"Henchman","max":null,"cost":30,"profile":[5,3,3,3,3,1,4,1,6,5,7,6],"access":"Skaven Equipment List"},{"id":"rat-ogre","name":"Rat Ogre","type":"Henchman","max":1,"cost":120,"profile":[6,3,1,5,4,3,4,3,5,5,7,4],"access":"Skaven Equipment List"}]},{"id":"orcs","name":"Orc","title":"Orc Warbands","equipmentTitle":"Orc Equipment List","startPage":116,"equipmentPage":118,"text":"[Page 116]\nOrcs\nWhen the comet struck Mordheim, its fiery descent shattered          particularly ruthless one might just make a fortune from the\nnot only the city, but the fragile order of the Empire. As smoke     loot they collect and the trophies they take from fallen\nand sorcery choked the skies and the noble houses tore each          enemies—many of whom end up as dinner.\nother apart, the Greenskins saw only opportunity. Like wolves\ndrawn to a dying stag, they came – bands of brutal Orcs and          But don’t expect Orcs to go scurrying around for wyrdstone\nsneaky Goblins, lured by the promise of violence, loot, and          like some pointy-eared Elf. Given the choice, they'd much\nbossin' others about.                                                rather bash another warband over the head and take their\n                                                                     stash. Their goals are brutally simple: despoil, pillage, burn,\nThese aren’t great warhosts with banners and bellowing               and leg it before anyone gets organized.\nWarbosses. No, these are fractured mobs – scavengers,\noutcasts, and ambitious upstarts. Smaller Orc warbands, driven\nby hunger for power or gold, have slunk into Mordheim's ruins        Orc Warbands\nto carve out a name for themselves. Others arrived\n                                                                     The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\naccidentally, swept up in failed Waaaghs! or chased from their\n                                                                     To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\ntribes, only to find themselves in a city where the strong\n                                                                     must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nsurvive and the rest get eaten.\n                                                                     gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\n                                                                     be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nAmong the many savage races of the Warhammer world, none\nrelish the thrill of looting and pillaging more than the Orcs and\n                                                                     WARBAND COMPOSITION\nGoblins. For the average Orc, life is a constant fight—whether\n                                                                     An Orc warband must follow these rules when it is created,\nit’s cracking skulls within their own tribe or battering some\n                                                                     and when new warriors are added to the warband.\nunfortunate foe. So when Mordheim, a city ripe with violence,\nchaos, and treasure, erupted into ruin, it was only natural that\n                                                                         •    There must be one leader (Orc Boss) chosen when the\nthe Greenskins would be drawn to it like flies to a corpse.\n                                                                              warband is first founded (if the leader is killed see\n                                                                              below)\nMordheim is a paradise of anarchy for Greenskins. The\nbuildings are half-fallen and full of shadows. There’s loot lying        •    There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\naround, enemies hiding in every alley, and the local humies are               for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\ntoo busy stabbing each other to keep order. It’s a perfect                    example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nplayground for a mob of violent thugs with no sense of self-                  to four champions.\npreservation.                                                            •    The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\n                                                                              be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nWith the Empire teetering on the edge of civil war and                        warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nlawlessness reigning in the surrounding regions, it’s all too easy            the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nfor smaller bands of Greenskins to sneak into the shattered              •    A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\ncity. Though Orcs have no real use for wyrdstone—it can’t be                  weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\neaten (tastes funny) and it doesn’t explode like a proper                     up the space of two weapons.\nweapon—they’ve discovered that plenty of others do want it.              •    The maximum number of warriors is shown before\nSkaven, Undead, even desperate humans are willing to barter                   the name. For example, 0-1 Orc Shaman. The\nand bleed for a handful of the glowing shards. A cunning Orc                  maximum number of Orc Shamans in a warband is 1.\nBoss can trade wyrdstone for weapons, grub, slaves or gold. A\n\n[Page 117]\nOrc Special Rules\nSIZE MATTERS. Orc units do not take a Panic check when a\nGoblin warrior is Seriously Wounded or goes Out of Action\nwithin 3\" of them.\nWhen testing to see if an Orc Warband needs to take a Rout\ntest, each Goblin Warrior Seriously Injured or Out of Action\nonly counts as half a warrior (rounding up).\n\nFEAR ELVES. All Goblins dislike fighting Elves of any kind.\nElves are haughty, unnatural and 'stink funny', which is more\nthan enough to unnerve such a cowardly race. Elves cause Fear\nin Goblin warriors.\n\nANIMOSITY. Orcs and goblins enjoy nothing more than a\ngood scrap, Greenskins will fight anyone, even each other!\nAt the start of the Warrior’s Activation, make an Animosity\ncheck if there is at least one other friendly warrior within 12”\nwith the Animosity special rule, that is an eligible target (not\nSeriously Injured. Broken, or Engaged).\nThere is no need to take an Animosity check if:\n     • There are visible enemy warriors within 12”.                 Animosity Table\n     • There are Hated enemy warriors visible at any                D6 Result\n          distance.                                                 1    “I ’Erd Dat!” If the warrior is in charge reach, they will\n     • Warriors engaged in close combat don't test.                      immediately charge the nearest friendly Greenskin\n     • Warriors that are Broken or Seriously Injured don't               warrior that is not engaged in close combat and fight a\n          test.                                                          round of close combat against the warrior. Their\n                                                                         opponent will make Reaction attacks as usual. At the\nTo make an Animosity check, the warrior makes a LD check                 end of this round of combat, the warriors will\nand adds +2 to the warrior’s LD. Apply the following modifiers           immediately move 1\" apart and no longer count as being\nto the 2D6 dice roll:                                                    in close combat.\n     • +1 if a friendly warrior with Animosity is in the                 If there are no friendly Greenskin warriors within\n         warrior’s visibility arc and charge distance.                   charge reach, and the warrior is armed with a missile\n     • +1 if the friendly warrior with Animosity is a Goblin             weapon and in range, he immediately performs a Shoot\n         and an Orc is testing.                                          (Basic) action at the nearest Eligible friendly Greenskin\n     • -1 enemy warriors visible.                                        warrior.\n     • -1 Leader is in 12” (or is the Leader).                           If none of the above applies, the warrior behaves as if a\n                                                                         2-5 had been rolled on this chart.\nIf LD check is passed, then nothing happens, and the warrior        2-5 “Wud Yoo Say?” The warrior makes two Move\ncan make their tun as usual. If the LD check failed, then roll on        (Simple) actions towards the nearest friendly Greenskin\nthe Animosity table below.                                               warrior, halting within 1\" or as close as possible. The\n                                                                         two warriors then exchange jeers, insults and a great\n                                                                         deal of spittle. The warrior may not perform any other\n                                                                         actions this turn.\n                                                                    6    “I’ll Show Yer!” The warrior counts as having the\n                                                                         Sprint skill for this Activation turn only. The warrior\n                                                                         must move towards the nearest visible enemy warrior,\n                                                                         charging into combat if possible. If there are no enemy\n                                                                         warriors within sight, the warrior may use Sprint skill\n                                                                         however the player wishes.\n\n[Page 118]\nHeroes\n                       1 Orc boss                                                       0-1 Shaman\nCOST TO HIRE: 125 Gold Crowns.                                   COST TO HIRE: 60 Gold Crowns.\nAn Orc Boss is a brutal war-leader, feared by his Boyz and       Orc Shamans are conduits of raw Waaagh! energy---- blessed\nobeyed without question. He rules through raw strength,          or cursed by Gork and Mork with chaotic powers they barely\nsavage cunning, and sudden violence. Any challenge to his        comprehend. Their magic is violent, unpredictable, and\nauthority is settled with blood. He hurls his warband into       dangerous to friend and foe alike. Shunned by many, they\nbattle not for glory or honour, but for loot, carnage, and the   find purpose in warbands, where their madness is seen not as\nsheer joy of smashing things until they stop moving.             weakness, but as a sign of brutal divine favour.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A    LD    CL   WIL    INT     M    WS     BS    S   T   W     I   A    LD    CL    WIL     INT\n 4     4     4    3   4    2   3   3    8     8      7      5     4     3      3    3   4    2    2   1     7     8      8      6\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nAn Orc Boss starts with no equipment. They may purchase          A Shaman starts with no equipment. They may purchase Orc\nClose Combat Weapons, Special Weapons, Missile Weapons,          Shaman Weapons and Wargear from the Orc Equipment\nArmour, and Wargear from the Orc Equipment List.                 List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   SPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Orc), Leader, Animosity, Size Matters                      Race (Orc), Champion, Wizard (Power of da Waaargh!),\n                                                                 Animosity, Size Matters\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their         STARTING SKILL:\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does     When recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.                         Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\n                                                                 not increase the warrior’s credit value.\n\n\n                                                                                            Big uns\n                                                                 COST TO HIRE: 85 Gold Crowns.\n                                                                 In Orc society, strength decides all. Big ’Uns are hardened\n                                                                 killers, second only to the Boss. If he falls, they don’t argue----\n                                                                 they fight. No words, no plans---- just fists, blades, and blood.\n                                                                 The last one standing leads. It’s not about honour or loyalty.\n                                                                 It’s about who’s meanest, toughest, and still breathing.\n                                                                  M    WS     BS    S   T   W     I   A    LD    CL    WIL     INT\n                                                                  4     4      3    3   4    2    3   2     8     7      7      5\n\n\n                                                                 WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                 An Orc Big Un starts with no equipment. They may purchase\n                                                                 Close Combat Weapons, Special Weapons, Missile Weapons,\n                                                                 Armour, and Wargear from the Orc Equipment List.\n\n                                                                 SPECIAL RULES:\n                                                                 Race (Orc), Champion, Animosity, Size Matters\n\n                                                                 STARTING SKILL:\n                                                                 When recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their\n                                                                 Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\n                                                                 not increase the warrior’s credit value.","equipment":["Axe","Club","Dagger","Flail","Great Axe","Great Hammer","Great Sword","Hammer or Mace","Morning Star","Spear","Staff","Sword","Heavy armour","Light armour","Bow","Crossbow","Net","Short bow","Shield","Lantern","Rope and hook","Bottle of rotgut","Mad cap mushrooms","Orc Choppa"],"displayName":"Orcs","warriors":[{"id":"orc-boss","name":"Orc Boss","type":"Leader","max":1,"cost":125,"profile":[4,4,4,3,4,2,3,3,8,8,7,5],"access":"Orc Equipment List"},{"id":"shaman","name":"Shaman","type":"Champion","max":1,"cost":60,"profile":[4,3,3,3,4,2,2,1,7,8,8,6],"access":"Orc Equipment List"},{"id":"big-uns","name":"Big Uns","type":"Champion","max":2,"cost":85,"profile":[4,4,3,3,4,2,3,2,8,7,7,5],"access":"Orc Equipment List"},{"id":"orc-yoofs","name":"Orc Yoofs","type":"Raw Recruit","max":null,"cost":25,"profile":[4,2,2,3,4,1,2,1,6,6,6,4],"access":"Orc Equipment List"},{"id":"nasty-skulker","name":"Nasty Skulkers","type":"Champion","max":2,"cost":55,"profile":[4,3,4,3,3,2,4,2,6,5,5,5],"access":"Orc Equipment List"},{"id":"orc-boyz","name":"Orc Boyz","type":"Henchman","max":null,"cost":35,"profile":[4,3,3,3,4,1,2,1,7,7,7,5],"access":"Orc Equipment List"},{"id":"goblin-warriors","name":"Goblin Warriors","type":"Henchman","max":null,"cost":20,"profile":[4,2,3,3,3,1,3,1,5,5,5,5],"access":"Orc Equipment List"},{"id":"troll","name":"Troll","type":"Henchman","max":1,"cost":120,"profile":[6,3,1,5,4,3,1,3,4,6,6,4],"access":"Orc Equipment List"}]},{"id":"dwarfs","name":"Dwarf","title":"Dwarf Warbands","equipmentTitle":"Dwarf Clansman Equipment List","startPage":122,"equipmentPage":124,"text":"[Page 122]\nDwarf Clansmen\nMordheim was once home to many Dwarf tradesmen,                    each passing day, their thirst for revenge consuming thought\ncraftsmen, merchants, and stonemasons. Not only did the            and reason. Their desire for gold—always a powerful instinct—\nDwarfs supply stone from their mountain quarries, but they         twisted into greed for wyrdstone and the wealth and vengeance\nalso lent their expertise to the city's very foundations—helping   it could bring. They began to see enemies everywhere: those\ndesign its canals, fortifications, and even the intricate sewer    who might steal from them, who stood in the way of their\nsystems beneath its streets. As a result, Mordheim enjoyed         honour, or dared to claim what rightfully belonged to their\nprosperous and long-standing trade relations with the nearby       people. It wasn’t just goldlust—it was possessiveness.\nDwarfholds.                                                        Wyrdstone came to represent what was stolen, what was owed,\nWhen disaster struck and the city was destroyed, word of the       and what could never be restored. Those who tried to take it\ncalamity spread swiftly to the Dwarf settlements. Many among       became enemies.\nthem had kin in the city, and the question that burned in every    And so, the Dwarfs endure in the ruins of Mordheim. Once\nhearth-hall was the same: What had become of their brethren?       they came seeking the fallen. Now they fight for vengeance,\nFor Dwarfs are a people bound by blood and honour, and few         gold, and pride—unwilling or unable to leave the city that has\nties run deeper than those of clan and family.                     already claimed so much from them.\nThe Dwarf Lords, ever wary of entanglement in human affairs,\nrefused to dispatch official aid. Yet many granted their Thanes\nleave to muster and equip small bands of warriors and kin to       Dwarf Warbands\njourney into the ruins in search of survivors.\n                                                                   The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nBut when the warbands reached Mordheim, they found the\n                                                                   To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\ndevastation far worse than imagined. Their noble task swiftly\n                                                                   must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nshifted—from rescue to remembrance. The ruined streets and\n                                                                   gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\nshattered dwellings became tombs, and their grim duty was\n                                                                   be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nnow to recover the remains of their fallen, so their souls might\nrest in the halls of their ancestors.\n                                                                   WARBAND COMPOSITION\nAmong the human shantytowns clinging to the city’s outskirts,\n                                                                   The warband must follow these rules when it is created, and\nthey found Dwarfs who had survived—shattered in spirit,\n                                                                   when new warriors are added to the warband.\nhaunted by grief. Some had even taken the Slayer’s oath,\nchoosing a life of doom to atone for surviving when others had\n                                                                       •   There must be one leader (Thane) chosen when the\nperished. Others were stonemasons, brewers, traders, and\n                                                                           warband is first founded (if the leader is killed see\nminers who had worked in the surrounding lands. Many of\n                                                                           below)\nthese Dwarfs, still searching for their own lost kin, chose to\nband together under Dwarf Thanes, rather than entrust their            •   There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nfates to fickle and untrustworthy humans.                                  for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nOver time, their reasons for staying in Mordheim began to                  example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nshift. Some remained to avenge the deaths of loved ones.                   to four champions.\nOthers continued the search for lost heirlooms and sacred              •   The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\nrelics of their clans. A few still clung to the faint hope of              be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nfinding friends or family alive in the ruins. And more than a              warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nfew Thanes, ever pragmatic, began to see opportunity in the                the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nchaos—selling scavenged wyrdstone to desperate human                   •   A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\nsmugglers for a high price.                                                weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nThe Dwarfs thought themselves immune to corrupting power                   up the space of two weapons.\nof the wyrdstone. Other races such as short-lived men and              •   Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\nsybaritic Elves might fall under its sway, but not them. As with           is shown before the name. For example, 0-1 Engineer.\nso much else that gave Dwarfs pride, their seeming immunity                The maximum number of Engineers in a warband is\nplayed them false. The longer they remained in Mordheim, the               therefore 1.\nmore they changed. Their books of grudges grew heavier with\n\n[Page 123]\nDwarf skill access\nDwarf Clansmen have access to the following skills:\n             Agility     Brawn          Combat          Cunning      Ferocity      Leadership    Shooting     Academic     Resilience\nThane                    Secondary Secondary                         Primary       Primary                                 Primary\nEngineer                                                             Secondary     Secondary     Primary      Primary      Secondary\nLongbeards               Secondary Secondary                         Primary       Secondary                               Primary\nBeardlings                              Secondary                    Primary                                               Secondary\nClansman                 Secondary Secondary                         Primary                                               Primary\nThunderers                                              Secondary    Secondary                   Primary                   Primary\n\n\nDwarf Special Rules\nRACE (DWARF)\nAll Dwarfs have the following special rules:\n     • ANCESTRAL GRUDGE: All Dwarfs hate all Orcs and Goblins. See the psychology section of the Mordheim rules for\n        details on the effects of hatred.\n     • ELF GRUDGE: A Dwarf warband may never include any kind of Elf Hired Sword or Dramatis Personae.\n     • BURLY: Dwarfs never suffer any movement penalties for wearing armour (e.g. Encumbrance).\n     • EXPERT MINERS: When checking for wyrdstone in the Post Battle, add +1 to the number of pieces found.\n     • MAGIC RESISTANCE (6) All Dwarfs have a natural resistance to magic. Magic spells will not affect a Dwarf on a D6 roll\n        of 6+. The spell isn’t dispelled and may still affect other warriors nearby. Note, that if the Dwarfs are fighting alongside a\n        Wizard or Priest (either in the same warband, or as part of an allied force) for whatever reason, this bonus is lost — the\n        spell caster’s presence disrupts the Dwarfs’ resistance.\n\nBALLISTICS EXPERT\nWhen this warrior makes an Aim (Basic) action, make an Intelligence check for them. If the check is passed, they gain an\nadditional +1 modifier to their hit roll.\n\nGUNSMITH\nWhenever a Blackpowder weapon rolls a Misfire, and requires an Intelligence check, a warrior from their warband within 6” can\nuse this warrior’s Intelligence characteristic instead of their own.\n\n[Page 124]\nHeroes\n\n                           1 Thane                                                     0~1 Engineer\nCOST TO HIRE: 135 Gold Crowns.                                   COST TO HIRE: 115 Gold Crowns.\nDwarf Thanes are stoic clan leaders drawn to Mordheim by         In the wreckage of Mordheim, Dwarf Engineers cling to their\nduty and blood. Once seekers of lost kin and relics, they now    sacred duty: maintaining the warband’s blackpowder\nbattle through ruin and corruption—driven by honour,             weapons. Every rifle cleaned, every bomb primed, is a ritual\nvengeance, and a growing hunger for the wyrdstone that has       against chaos. They mutter curses at flawed craftsmanship,\ntwisted their purpose and bound them to the city.                their hands black with soot and spite. In battle, they unleash\n M    WS    BS   S    T     W   I   A   LD   CL   WIL     INT    iron vengeance—precise gunfire and brutal detonations.\n 3     5     4   3     4    2   3   3   10   10     9      7     Their weapons are not mere tools, but sacred instruments of\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           wrath, built to endure. Amid ash and ruin, the Engineer\nA Than starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close         ensures that failure dies before honour ever does.\nCombat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Special Weapons,                 M    WS    BS    S    T   W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\nArmour, and Wargear from the Dwarf Clansman Equipment             3     4     4    4    4   2   3   2    9     9     9       8\nList.\n                                                                 WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   A Beardling starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nRace (Dwarf), Leader                                             Close Combat Weapons, Engineer Weapons, Armour, and\n                                                                 Wargear from the Dwarf Clansman Equipment List.\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their         SPECIAL RULES:\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does     Race (Dwarf), Champion, Ballistics Expert, Gunsmith\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.\n                                                                 STARTING SKILL:\n                      Longbeards                                 When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\n                                                                 Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nCOST TO HIRE: 120 Gold Crowns.                                   not increase the warrior’s credit value.\nLongbeards are ancient warriors forged by centuries of battle,\nloss, and unyielding duty. In the ruins of Mordheim, they                              Beardlings\nmarch not for glory, but to honour oaths and bury grief\nbeneath steel. Their presence is heavy with memory; every        COST TO HIRE: 30 Gold Crowns.\nblow struck is penance, every command weighted with              Fresh-faced and eager, young Dwarfs follow their Thane into\nsorrow. They are the spine of the warband—stoic, bitter, and     Mordheim, chasing whispers of lost kin and glittering riches.\nbound to a world that no longer remembers what they’ve lost.     They do not yet grasp the weight of grief or the city’s hunger.\n M    WS    BS    S    T    W   I   A   LD   CL    WIL    INT    Mordheim teaches quickly. Dreams turn to silence, courage\n 3     5     3    3    4    2   3   2   10    9     9      7     to ashes. In time, even hope is buried beneath the stones.\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                            M    WS    BS    S    T   W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\nA Longbeard starts with no equipment. They may purchase           3     3     2    3    4   1   2   1    8     8     8       6\nClose Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Special Weapons,          WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nArmour, and Wargear from the Dwarf Clansman Equipment            A Beardling starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nList.                                                            Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   Wargear from the Dwarf Clansman Equipment List.\nRace (Dwarf), Champion, Stubborn\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                  SPECIAL RULES:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their       Race (Dwarf), Raw Recruit.\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.","equipment":["Axe","Club","Dagger","Great Axe","Great Hammer","Great Sword","Gromril Axe","Hammer or Mace","Pickaxe","Spear","Sword","Gromril plate","Heavy armour","Light armour","Crossbow","Dwarf crossbow","Throwing axe","Blunderbuss","Bomb","Dwarf Handgun","Dwarf Pistol","Handgun","Pistol","Shield","Lantern","Rope and hook"],"displayName":"Dwarf Clansmen","warriors":[{"id":"thane","name":"Thane","type":"Leader","max":1,"cost":135,"profile":[3,5,4,3,4,2,3,3,10,10,9,7],"access":"Dwarf Clansman Equipment List"},{"id":"engineer","name":"Engineer","type":"Champion","max":1,"cost":115,"profile":[3,4,4,4,4,2,3,2,9,9,9,8],"access":"Dwarf Clansman Equipment List"},{"id":"longbeards","name":"Longbeards","type":"Champion","max":2,"cost":120,"profile":[3,5,3,3,4,2,3,2,10,9,9,7],"access":"Dwarf Clansman Equipment List"},{"id":"beardlings","name":"Beardlings","type":"Raw Recruit","max":3,"cost":30,"profile":[3,3,2,3,4,1,2,1,8,8,8,6],"access":"Dwarf Clansman Equipment List"},{"id":"clansmen","name":"Clansmen","type":"Henchman","max":null,"cost":45,"profile":[3,4,3,3,4,1,2,1,9,9,9,7],"access":"Dwarf Clansman Equipment List"},{"id":"thunderers","name":"Thunderers","type":"Henchman","max":5,"cost":45,