ndom and added to the rest        Chaos warband dies then their successor will be entitled to\n         of the warband’s Warrior cards before any cards are        learn to use magic in their stead. The new leader gains the\n         drawn. This means that only one of this warrior’s          Wizard special rule and rolls for a prayer/spell from the\n         cards can be drawn for the battle, and that the            appropriate list.\n         controlling player cannot choose which of their\n         equipment sets they will be using."},{"page":76,"text":"Warband Rules\nIn this section we take a detailed look at each of the warbands\nand provide the information you need to recruit a warband of      SPLINTER GANGS\nthat type.                                                        Players may wish to found a splinter warband from a previous\nUse the lists that follow to recruit and equip your warband.      or present campaign. A splinter warband is formed when one\nYou have a maximum budget of Gold Crowns to spend. Each           of a warband’s Champions goes it alone and takes some of\nmodel and their equipment (if you choose to buy any) costs a      their favoured Henchmen with them to form the core of a new\nset amount of money. As you make your choices, subtract the       warband.\nmoney you have “spent” from your total until you have bought      Forming a splinter warband is easy – players simply choose\nall you can. Any unspent gold crowns are put into the             one Champion from a warband they have played in a previous\nwarband’s treasury and can be used later or hoarded to buy        campaign and hire them as the Leader in a new warband,\nsomething more expensive.                                         keeping all of their equipment, Advancements and permanent\n                                                                  injuries, and paying their Gold Crowns value to hire them.\nWhen founding a warband, players will have a maximum              This champion then simply has their type changed to Leader\nbudget of Gold Crowns to spend. How much this is will             and is treated as such in all regards.\ndepend upon whether they are founding a warband for               Further to this, players may wish to retain other old favourites.\nSkirmish or Campaign play. In either case, this budget may not    • Veterans can be recruited from an old warband into a new\nbe exceeded. Any unspent Gold Crowns will be added to the         one in this way, changing their type to Champion (bearing in\nwarband’s Stash if the warband has been founded for               mind limits to Champions)\nCampaign play. However, if a warband has been founded for         • Raw Recruits can be recruited also, changing their type to\nSkirmish play, any unspent Gold Crowns are simply lost.           Henchmen.\n                                                                  • Any favoured Henchmen can be hired again as Henchmen\nThe next step is to choose the warriors that make up the          into a new warband.\nwarband. The following Warband lists show the warriors\navailable to each warband. A warrior’s entry in their Warband     New warriors can be hired to fill out the ranks and help keep\nlist will detail the weapon types they may be armed with, as      the cost down.\nwell as listing any Wargear they have when added to the           One of the old Henchmen, or a new one, may be promoted to\nwarband. Whenever a warrior is added to a warband, weapons        Veteran as well, although they do not roll for a skill – note a\nand Wargear are purchased for them. If the warband is being       Raw Recruit may not be promoted to Henchmen to Veteran in\nfounded for a campaign, warriors will be limited to equipment     this way.\nselected from their Warband Equipment List, whereas warriors      All that must be remembered is that the splinter warband must\nin a warband founded for a Skirmish may also have access to       abide by the same warband composition rules as a freshly\nsome items of equipment from the Trading Post. In either case,    founded warband, and is limited to the same Gold Crowns as\na warrior may discard any Wargear they have in favour of          new warbands.\nsomething else purchased from the Warband Type Equipment\nlist (most commonly this will be armour). Wargear discarded\nwhen a warband is founded is placed in the warband’s Stash\nand may be given to other warriors.\n\nFinally, a blank Warrior card is completed for each warrior\nwhen they are added to the warband; the characteristics of the\nwarrior and any equipment they now have should be noted\ndown in the appropriate sections of the Warrior card. A\nwarband roster sheet is also completed for the warband as a\nwhole."},{"page":77,"text":"Reikland Mercenaries\nThis is a time of unremitting war, civil strife, violence and\nfamine. A time of orphan children and wanton slaughter. For         Reiklander Warbands\nwarriors these are good times! Since the discovery of\n                                                                    The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nwyrdstone, Mordheim has become a magnet for fighting men\n                                                                    To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\nfrom all over the Empire. Nobles, merchants, and the Temple\n                                                                    must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nof Sigmar itself offer rich rewards for shards of the mysterious\n                                                                    gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\nstone. Foremost amongst the patrons of mercenary warriors\n                                                                    be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nare the three most powerful contenders for the Emperor’s\nthrone: the Grand Prince of Reikland, the Count of\n                                                                    WARBAND COMPOSITION\nMiddenheim, and Lady Magritta of Marienburg – favourite of\n                                                                    The warband must follow these rules when it is created, and\nthe merchant guilds.\n                                                                    when new warriors are added to the warband.\nReikland lies at the heart of the Empire and its greatest city is\n                                                                        •   There must be one leader (Mercenary Captain)\nAltdorf, home of the Grand Theogonist and seat of the Temple\n                                                                            chosen when the warband is first founded (if the\nof Sigmar. Reiklanders are devout followers of Sigmar, the\n                                                                            leader is killed see below)\nfounder, first Emperor, and patron god of the Empire. The\n                                                                        •   There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nGrand Prince of Reikland (as Siegfried, the ruler of Reikland,\n                                                                            for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nstyles himself) is supported in his claim to the throne by the\n                                                                            example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nGrand Theogonist and opposed most strongly by the Count of\n                                                                            to four champions.\nMiddenheim and the Priests of Ulric.\n                                                                        •   The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\nThroughout the Empire Reiklanders are commonly supposed                     be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nto embody the discipline and loyalty of the professional                    warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nwarrior. Brave and well-versed in the arts of war, Reiklanders              the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\ndisdain fashionable clothing in favour of well-made and                 •   A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\npractical wargear. In battle they often wear coloured ribbons as            weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nmarks of identification or authority. They are justly proud of              up the space of two weapons.\ntheir dynamic and ambitious Grand Prince and contemptuous               •   Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\nof other claimants to the throne, especially the Count of                   is shown before the name. For example, 0-1 Priest of\nMiddenheim, Mannfred Todbringer, whom they sneeringly                       Ulric. The maximum number of Priests of Ulric in a\ncall the ‘lap-dog of Ulric’.                                                warband is therefore 1."},{"page":78,"text":"Heroes\n\n            1 Mercenary Captain                                                        Sergeants\nCOST TO HIRE: 125 Gold Crowns.                                   COST TO HIRE: 80 Gold Crowns.\nA Mercenary Captain is a tough professional warrior, a man       Some captains are merchants or nobles that are looking for a\nwho will fight for anyone or against anything so long as the     chance at making some extra money. The brighter captains\nprice is right. Mordheim offers such a man the chance to         hire the service of a veteran as his sergeant, and leave all the\nbecome rich beyond his dreams, though at great risk. But as      practical decision to him. A veteran can be recognised by his\nruthlessness and lack of mercy and pity are the hallmarks of a   many battle-scars and the cynicism that marks a soldier of the\nsuccessful Mercenary Captain, it is no wonder that they flock 