good profit in       year in the army. These ‘Youngbloods’ are by no means\nAverheim, the provincial capital, to merchants from Nuln, who     regarded as professional soldiers yet and have to make do with\ntransport it on barges down the river Aver. The mountains         more simple clothing.\ncontain several ancient Dwarf strongholds but Night Goblins\nor Skaven has overrun several of them, while others have been\nlost in violent volcanic eruptions.                               Averlander Warbands\n                                                                  The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nThe Black Fire Pass guards an important trade route between\n                                                                  To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\nthe Borderlands and the Empire, it divides the World Edge\n                                                                  must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nMountains from the Black Mountains. The route is an old\n                                                                  gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\nDwarf road and extends past Averheim and further north into\n                                                                  be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nthe Empire. Goods from the Black Fire pass are usually\nshipped along the Aver River to Nuln. The pass is the only\n                                                                  WARBAND COMPOSITION\nplace to cross the mountains, as the mountainsides are\n                                                                  The warband must follow these rules when it is created, and\nextremely steep and almost impossible to pass. Not to mention\n                                                                  when new warriors are added to the warband.\nthat the weather is notoriously unpredictable and few dare risk\nbeing caught in a snow blizzard or avalanche. As if things\n                                                                      •    There must be one leader (Mercenary Captain)\nweren’t bad enough the mountains are home to fierce tribes of\n                                                                           chosen when the warband is first founded (if the\nNight Goblins, Trolls, Skaven and legendary monsters. Some\n                                                                           leader is killed see below)\ndaring adventurers have made a living off stealing eggs from\n                                                                      •    There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nthe tallest peaks and selling them to the Imperial Zoo. These\n                                                                           for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nbeasts will be brought up to become mounts for famous\ngenerals.                                                                  example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\n                                                                           to four champions.\nAverland is a rich province and as a result exorbitant sums of        •    The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\nmoney are spent on the uniforms of the state soldiers.                     be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nSeasoned veterans prefer flamboyant uniforms to make them                  warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nstand out compared to the peasant, but also to reflect their               the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nseniority. This tradition has seeped down through the ranks to        •    A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\na point where even the militia and mercenary bands strive to               weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nhave as flamboyant clothing as they can afford. The Averlander             up the space of two weapons.\narmy is said to employ enough tailors to supply a small city!         •    Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\n                                                                           is shown before the name. For example, 0-1 Priest of\nOutsiders joke that the Averlanders are such great archers                 Ulric. The maximum number of Priests of Ulric in a\nbecause they do not want to get up close and personal as they              warband is therefore 1.\nrisk tearing or bloodying their clothes. Such remarks are\nhushed down in the presence of a veteran of the Black Fire Pass\nthough, or else the jester will soon find himself in the gutter"},{"page":86,"text":"Heroes\n\n                                                                           When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\n             1 Mercenary Captain                                           Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nCOST TO HIRE: 125 Gold Crowns.                                             not increase the warrior’s credit value.\nThe Captain of a mercenary warband is typically a middle aged\nveteran soldier of the Imperial army, most likely he was a sergeant or\nother petty officer. The survival of a mercenary warband relies more\n                                                                                               0~2 Bergjaeger\non the wit and experience of its captain, than on how good a warrior       COST TO HIRE: 80 Gold Crowns.\nhe is. It’s all too common that an inexperienced captain will lead his     The Bergjaeger are trappers and rangers from the mountains that\nmen into an ambush, or lead them on a long journey with no food            surround the Black Fire pass. They are experts at moving silently\nor supplies. Being a successful captain means that your men will           through terrain and are used as scouts. In addition, they make good\nfollow you to hell and back, and plenty of gold crowns and feasting.       use of animal traps to delay or divide a group of enemies. Bergjager\nA captain that fails in his duty to keep his men alive and well fed will   are not professional soldiers and rely more on stealth and cunning\nat best find himself deserted and worst end up with a knife in his         than a strong sword-arm to survive.\nback.\n                                                                             M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT\n  M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT\n                                                                             4     3     4     3   3    2     4   2     7     8      7       7\n  4     4     4     4   3     2    4   3     8      8      7       7\n\n                                                                           WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                           A Bergjager starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nA Mercenary Captain starts with no equipment. They may\n                                                                           Close Combat Weapons, Bergjager Equipment, Armour, and\npurchase Close Combat Weapons, Mountainguard\n                                                                           Wargear from the Averlander Equipment List.\nEquipment, Special weapons, Armour, and Wargear from the\n                                                                           SPECIAL RULES:\nAverlander Equipment List.\n                                                                           Race (Human), Champion,\nSPECIAL RULES:\n                                                                           STARTING SKILL:\nRace (Human), Leader\n                                                                           When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nSTARTING SKILL:\n                                                                           Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their\n                                                                           not increase the warrior’s credit value.\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.\n                                                                                                   Youngbloods\n                             Sergeant                                      COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns.\n                                                                           Although Empire armies are comprised of mature men there are\nCOST TO HIRE: 80 Gold Crowns.                                              plenty of jobs for youths as there is always a demand for extra help\nSome captains are merchants or nobles that are looking for a chance        in the kitchens or as fetchers. Some of these youths actually join a\nat making some extra money. The brighter captains hire the service         band of mercenaries or regiment in pursuit of a romantic dream of\nof a veteran as his sergeant, and leave all the practical decision to      fame and adventure. Some are herdsmen who hoped to find an\nhim. A veteran can be recognised by his many battle-scars and the          easier way of filling their belly than the hard and uncertain business\ncynicism that marks a soldier of the army.                                 of looking after animals, not to mention that its quite dull!\n  M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT                                            M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT\n  4     4      3    3    3    2    4    2    8      7      7       7         4     2     2     3   3    1     3   1     6     6      6       6\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                                     WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Sergeant starts with no equipment. They may purchase                     A Youngblood starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nClose Combat Weapons, Mountainguard Equipment, Special                     Close Combat Weapons, Mountainguard Equipment, Special\nweapons, Armour, and Wargear from the Averlander                           weapons, Armour, and Wargear from the Averlander\nEquipment List.                                                            Equipment List.\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                             SPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Human), Champion                                                     Race (Human ), Raw Recruit.\nSTARTING SKILL:"},{"page":87,"text":"Henchmen\n\n                                                                 Marksmen often own their own weapons, as the cost of a\n                 Mountainguard                                   handgun is as high as hiring the Marksman himself! Thus the\nCOST TO HIRE: 35 Gold Crowns                                     Marksmen are not forced to do as much hard labour as the\nThe Mountainguard is the famous garrison of the Black Fire       militia.\nPass that has repelled countless greenskin invasion attempts.     M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A    LD    CL   WIL     INT\nTheir traditional uniform is yellow and black and it’s a merit    4     3     3    3   3    1   3    1    7     7     7      7\nin the Averland armey to have served a few years at the\nmountain-pass. The Mountain guard train both with the            WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\ntraditional Imperial weapons, the halberd and the sword, and     A Marksman starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nwith the crossbow and bow. Veterans are often employed by        Close Combat Weapons, Marksman Equipment, Armour,\nmercenary warbands who know that their presence will             and Wargear from the Averlander Equipment List.\ncertainly boost their chances in the battles to come. Some of\nthese veterans advance to become sergeants or even captains      SPECIAL RULES:\nthemselves. There are a few warbands that consists solely of     Race (Human),Henchman\nMountainguard veterans, often from the same regiment or\nthe survivors of a great battle.\n M    WS    BS   S   T   W    I   A    LD   CL    WIL    INT\n                                                                              0~3 Halfling Scouts\n 4     4     3   3   3    1   3   1    7     7     7      7      COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns\n                                                                 Averland is neighbour to the Moot, the Halfling province. In\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           1707 the Orc Warlord Gorbad Ironclaw invaded through the\nA Mountainguard starts with no equipment. They may               Black Fire pass and the Moot was devastated. Ever since then\npurchase Close Combat Weapons, Mountainguard                     the Moot urge their gamekeepers to serve at least a few years\nEquipment, Armour, and Wargear from the Averlander               in the garrison that guard the pass. If another warlord tries to\nEquipment List.                                                  invade the Moot, they will meet the fierce resistance of the\n                                                                 Halflings in the mountain Pass..\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                    M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A    LD    CL   WIL     INT\nRace (Human),Henchman                                             3     2     4    2   2    1   5    1    6     7     8      7\n\n\n                     Marksmen                                    WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                 A Halfling Scout starts with no equipment. They may\nCOST TO HIRE: 35 Gold Crowns                                     purchase Close Combat Weapons, Scout Equipment,\nBeing a Marksmen is not as simple as picking up a bow and        Armour, and Wargear from the Averlander Equipment List.\ntry to hit your enemies. A Marksman has to train for years to\nmaster his chosen weapon, Imperial enlisters often visit         SPECIAL RULES:\narchery competitions to try and enlist a couple of expert        Race (Halfling), Henchman\narchers. Some Marksmen are trained with black powder\nweapons instead of the traditional bow or crossbow."},{"page":88,"text":"Averlander Equipment List\nBERGJAGER EQUIPMENT                                              SPECIAL WEAPONS\nITEM                               PRICE                         ITEM                           PRICE\nBow                                15                            Buckler                        10\nLong Bow                           20                            Duelling Pistol                35\nMan Trap                           15                            Hochland Long Rifle            90\nHunting Arrows                     10\n                                                                 ARMOUR\nCLOSE COMBAT WEAPONS                                             ITEM                           PRICE\nITEM                               PRICE                         Light Armour                   20\nAxe                                15                            Shield                         20\nClub                               15\nDagger                             10                            MOUNTAINGUARD WEAPONS\nHammer Or Mace                     20                            ITEM                  PRICE\nSword                              25                            Bow                   15\n                                                                 Crossbow              30\nHALFLING EQUIPMENT                                               Great Axe             50\nITEM                               PRICE                         Great Hammer          45\nShort Bow                          10                            Great Sword           45\nStaff                              25                            Halberd               30\n                                                                 Morning star          30\nMARKSMAN WEAPONS                                                 Pistol                20\nITEM                                PRICE                        Spear                 20\nBlunderbuss                         25                           Heavy Armour          50\nBow                                 15\nCrossbow                            30                           WARGEAR\nHandgun                             40                           ITEM                           PRICE\nLong Bow                            20                           Lantern                        35\nPistol                              20                           Rope And Hook                  30\n\n\n\n\n                                        Averlander skill access\nAverlander Warriors have access to the following skills:\n\n                       Agility       Brawn         Combat      Cunning     Ferocity    Leadership   Shooting    Academic\nMercenary Captain      Secondary                   Primary                 Primary     Primary      Secondary\nSergeant                             Secondary     Primary                 Secondary   Primary      Secondary\nBergjager              Secondary                               Primary     Secondary   Secondary    Primary\nYoungblood             Secondary                   Primary                 Secondary\nMountainguard          Secondary     Secondary     Primary                 Primary\nMarksman               Secondary                   Primary     Secondary                            Primary\nHalfling scout         Secondary                   Secondary   Primary                              Primary"},{"page":89,"text":"Ostlander Mercenaries\nMy only crime was to get in a brawl with some pig farmer\n\n                                                                    Ostlander Warbands\noutside of the Donkey's Nut Tavern - the next thing I knew a\ndozen of his brothers were after my blood!'\n-Udo Verkonnen, Freesword\n                                                                    The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\n                                                                    To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\nThe principality of Ostland is the most sparsely inhabited of all\n                                                                    must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nof the Empire's Electoral provinces. Its people have more ties\n                                                                    gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\nwith the land of Kislev to the north than they do with their\n                                                                    be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\ncountrymen to the south. This is because the Forest of\nShadows and the Middle Mountains form two natural barriers\n                                                                    WARBAND COMPOSITION\nbetween Ostland and the rest of the Empire. Within the Forest\n                                                                    The warband must follow these rules when it is created, and\nof Shadows are vast amounts of wild game but also darker\n                                                                    when new warriors are added to the warband.\ncreatures such as Chaos Beastmen and Forest Goblins. The\nMiddle Mountains themselves are the highest point in the\n                                                                        •   There must be one leader (Elder) chosen when the\nEmpire and their peaks are inhabited by a large number of\n                                                                            warband is first founded (if the leader is killed see\nOgres.\n                                                                            below)\nOstland’s isolation has greatly shaped its inhabitants and they\n                                                                        •   There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nare a poor but hardy folk. Each small village lives barely above\n                                                                            for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nsubsistence levels and is usually composed of one large\n                                                                            example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nextended family. The men of Ostand are tall and broad-\n                                                                            to four champions.\nshouldered while the women tend to either be tall and whippet\n                                                                        •   The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\nthin or short and stout. Married men are usually dirt farmers\n                                                                            be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nwho also gather roots, tubers and nuts in the forests, while\n                                                                            warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nunmarried men spend their lives as trappers and hunters. The\n                                                                            the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nworship of Taal, the god of Forests and Beasts, is very popular\n                                                                        •   A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\nin the region, although there is also some worship of Taal’s\n                                                                            weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nwife Ryha, and his brother Ulric in the the more westerly\n                                                                            up the space of two weapons.\nvillages.\n                                                                        •   Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\n                                                                            is shown before the name. For example, 0-1 Priest of\nWhile not warlike by nature, Ostlanders are never opposed to a\n                                                                            Ulric. The maximum number of Priests of Ulric in a\ngood honest drunken brawl and with their love of dark ales\n                                                                            warband is therefore 1.\nthese sorts of scraps are not uncommon. During the Great War\nagainst Chaos, Ostlanders rallied in great numbers to wield\nbow and spear in defence of their Kislevite neighbours. More\nthan any other part of the Empire, Ostland has tasted the lash\nof Chaos and their hatred of the evil ones knows no bounds."},{"page":90,"text":"Heroes\n\n                          1 Elder                                                0~1 Priest of Taal\nCOST TO HIRE: 125 Gold Crowns.                                      COST TO HIRE: 50 Gold Crowns.\nIn Ostland, the oldest (or more often biggest) man in the           It is said that every priest of Taal is born during the darkest\nvillage is given the title ‘Elder’. His word is greatly respected   phase of the moon. Those who are accepted into the service\nand only at his urging would the manhood of an entire village       of Taal are loners by nature and spend their time wandering\npack up and travel to Mordheim to seek their fortune.               the untamed forests of the Northern Empire. It is unclear\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W     I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT      why the priests of the forest have begun to join bands of\n 4     4     4    4   3    2   4    3    8     8     7       7      Ostlanders in their delving into the ruined city of Mordheim\n                                                                    — for the servants of Taal keep their own counsel. Suffice to\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                              say that the Forest-God is clearly building a strong presence\nAn Elder starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close          both in and around the darkened ruins as more animals begin\nCombat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Special Weapons,                   to fill the surrounding forests.\nArmour, and Wargear from the Ostlander Equipment List.               M    WS    BS   S   T   W     I   A   LD   CL    WIL    INT\n                                                                     4     2     3   3   3    2   3    1    7    8      8      8\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Human), Leader                                                WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                    A Priest of Taal starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                     Close Combat Weapons, from the Ostlander Equipment List.\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does        SPECIAL RULES:\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.                            Race (Human), Champion, Priest (Cast Spells Prayers of\n                                                                    Taal), may never wear armour.\n                  Blood Brothers                                    STARTING SKILL:\nCOST TO HIRE: 80 Gold Crowns.                                       When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nOstland villages are usually composed of a single extended          Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nfamily. Everyone is everyone else's uncle, cousin or brother        not increase the warrior’s credit value.\n(and sometimes their own!). Rather than trying to keep all of\nthese relations straight, the most respected men in the village                          Youngbloods\n(aside from the Elder) are referred to simply as Blood-\nbrothers.                                                           COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W     I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT      These are young warriors who are still inexperienced, but\n 4     4     3    3   3    2    4   2    8     7     7       7      eager to win their spurs in the savage fighting in and around\n                                                                    the ruins of Mordheim.\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                               M    WS    BS   S   T   W     I   A   LD   CL    WIL    INT\nA Sergeant starts with no equipment. They may purchase               4     2     2   3   3    1   3    1    6    6      6      6\nClose Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Special Weapons,\nArmour, and Wargear from the Ostlander Equipment List.              WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                    A Youngblood starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                      Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Spceial weapons,\nRace (Human), Champion                                              Armour, and Wargear from the Ostlander Equipment List.\n\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                     SPECIAL RULES:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their          Race (Human ), Raw Recruit.\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value."},{"page":91,"text":"Henchmen\n\n                              Kin                                                     0~5 Ruffians\nCOST TO HIRE: 35 Gold Crowns                                    COST TO HIRE: 25 Gold Crowns\nMost of the warriors in an Ostlander warband are brothers       Although every Ostlander loves his ale, a few men in every\nand cousins of the Elder. Many are marred men with children     village take this love to extremes. Never sober and rarely\nto support and the ruins of Mordheim are a lure that few        conscious, these buffoons stagger their way through the\npoor villagers can resist.                                      streets of Mordheim yelling slurred insults at whomever they\n M    WS    BS   S   T   W     I    A   LD   CL   WIL    INT    meet, committing petty acts of vandalism and generally\n 4     3     3   3   3    1    3    1   7    7     7      7     making a mess of things. This comic behaviour is often\n                                                                misconstrued into a false belief that they are harmless, a belief\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                          that many live to regret. Fuelled by vast quantities of booze\nA Kin starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close         these are very dangerous, unpredictable men indeed who will\nCombat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and Wargear            shove a broken bottle into your face as soon as laugh heartily\nfrom the Ostlander Equipment List.                              and burst into song!\n                                                                 M    WS    BS    S    T   W    I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   4     2     2    3    3   1    2   1    6     7     6       6\nRace (Human), Henchman\n                                                                WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                A Ruffian starts with a Bottle of Rotgut.\n                     0-7 Jaeger                                 They may purchase Close Combat Weapons, Armour, and\nCOST TO HIRE: 35 Gold Crowns                                    Wargear from the Ostlander Equipment List.\nSome Ostlander men choose not to marry but instead spend\ntheir time alone in the forests of the Old World. While these   SPECIAL RULES:\nrangers do not share the close family bonds of a typical        Race (Human), Henchman\nOstlander blood-kin they are well respected for their\nknowledge of the woods and their rugged determination.\nPoor Jaeger usually wield a simple home-made bow but it is                            0-1 Ogre\nevery jaeger’s dream to one day own a blackpowder weapon\n                                                                COST TO HIRE: 120 Gold Crowns\nand hunting rifle, especially double-barrelled versions, as\n                                                                More than anywhere in the Empire, Ogres are most\nthese are a sign of great prestige amongst the hunters of the\n                                                                commonplace within the hilly, pine forested landscape of\ndeep woods.\n                                                                Ostland. These brutish creatures are very much sought after\n M    WS    BS   S   T   W     I    A   LD   CL   WIL    INT\n                                                                by the rough mountain men of Ostland as muscle in the\n 4     3     3   3   3    1    3    1   7    7     7      7     warband. An Ogre’s strength is near legendary and their\n                                                                ability to sustain an awful lot of punishment during a fight\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                          makes these the perfect shock troops of any warband. Of\nA Jaeger starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close      course, an Ogre's appetite is nearly as well-renowned as their\nCombat Weapons, Jager Weapons, Armour, and Wargear              fighting abilities and so they are rather expensive to keep.\nfrom the Ostlander Equipment List.                               M    WS    BS    S    T   W    I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\n                                                                 6     3     2    4    4   3    3   2    7     5     7       4\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Human), Henchman\n                                                                WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                An Ogre starts with no equipment. They may purchase Ogre\n                                                                Equipment from the Ostlander Equipment List.\n\n                                                                SPECIAL RULES:\n                                                                Race (Ogre), Hired Sword, Fear, Large Target, Henchman"},{"page":92,"text":"Ostlander Equipment List\nCLOSE COMBAT WEAPONS                                              JAGER WEAPONS\nITEM                              PRICE                           ITEM                            PRICE\nAxe                               15                              Blunderbuss                     25\nClub                              15                              Bow                             15\nDagger                            10                              Handgun                         40\nHammer Or Mace                    20                              Pistol                          20\nSword                             25\nGreat Axe                         50                              OGRE EQUIPMENT\nGreat Hammer                      45                              ITEM                           PRICE\nGreat Sword                       45                              Axe                            15\nSpear                             20                              Club                           15\nStaff                             25                              Hammer Or Mace                 20\n                                                                  Sword                          25\nMISSILE WEAPONS                                                   Great Axe                      50\nITEM                                PRICE                         Great Hammer                   45\nBow                                 15                            Great Sword                    45\nPistol                              20                            Light Armour                   20\n\nARMOUR                                                            WARGEAR\nITEM                                PRICE                         ITEM                            PRICE\nLight Armour                        20                            Lantern                         35\nShield                              20                            Rope And Hook                   30\n                                                                  Bottle of Rotgut                15\nSPECIAL WEAPONS\nITEM                                PRICE\nHochland Long Rifle                 90\nHeavy Armour                        50\n\n\n\n\n                                         Ostlander skill access\nOstlander Warriors have access to the following skills:\n\n                 Agility      Brawn     Combat        Cunning     Ferocity    Leadership   Shooting    Academic   Resilience\nElder                         Primary   Secondary                 Primary     Primary      Secondary\nPriest of Taal                          Secondary     Secondary   Secondary   Primary                  Primary\nBlood                         Primary   Primary                   Secondary   Secondary                           Secondary\nBrother\nYoungblood       Secondary              Secondary                 Primary\nKin                           Primary   Secondary                 Secondary                Secondary\nJaeger                                                Secondary   Secondary                Primary\nRuffian                       Primary                             Secondary                                       Secondary\nOgre                          Primary                             Secondary                                       Secondary"},{"page":93,"text":"Cult of the possessed\nThere is never any shortage of men willing to risk their lives      nothing is too base for them! These degenerate humans are\nfor a chance of real power: men whose ambitions lie beyond          joined by other creatures as vile as they – things half-man half-\nthe scope of their birthright, or whose sorcerous skills or         beast that call themselves Gors, and which men refer to as\nphysical deformities place them in constant danger of               Beastmen.\npersecution. What do such men have to lose if they pledge\ntheir souls to the dark gods of Chaos! In the aftermath of the      There are few sights as horrific as a cult warband. Deranged\ndestruction of Mordheim all manner of mutants have appeared         warriors smeared with blood and dirt wave jagged weapons\nwhilst many hitherto unblemished folk feel the stirring of          and chant blasphemous rites as they throw themselves upon\nstrange powers, the first awakenings of magical gifts destined      their foes. Many are hardly recognisable as human, their\nto bring them to a fiery death at the hands of the Witch            bodies are so scarred and disfigured. The stigmata of mutation\nHunters.                                                            is borne by most, but the most unsettling of all are the\n                                                                    Possessed themselves – melded flesh made of men, beasts, and\nNow a leader has appeared, a new Dark Emperor, who claims           metal driven by the implacable will of a Daemon.\nlordship of the City of the Damned. He is called the\nShadowlord, Master of the Possessed, and followers of the cults\nof Chaos gather from all over the Empire to pledge their souls      Possessed Warbands\nto him. Though none know whether he is man or Daemon all\n                                                                    The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nproclaim him their saviour and eagerly seek to do his bidding.\n                                                                    To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\nAs all students of the dark arts know, it is by the power of\n                                                                    must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nmagic that creatures such as Daemons and spirits are able to\n                                                                    gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\nstalk the mortal world. The wyrdstone that proliferates in\n                                                                    be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nMordheim grants unnatural life to many vile things that by all\nnatural rights should never exist. The Possessed were once\n                                                                    WARBAND COMPOSITION\nmen but by surrendering themselves wholly to the dark gods\n                                                                    The warband must follow these rules when it is created, and\nthey have allowed Daemons to possess their bodies. Their\n                                                                    when new warriors are added to the warband.\nappearance is horrific – corrupted from within, their flesh is\ntwisted into a new and monstrous form.\n                                                                        •    There must be one leader (Magister) chosen when the\n                                                                             warband is first founded (if the leader is killed see\nWith the power of the Possessed behind them the followers of\n                                                                             below)\nthe Shadowlord have grown powerful in Mordheim. In the\n                                                                        •    There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nMassacre of Silver Street the Cult of the Possessed ambushed\n                                                                             for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nand destroyed a large force sent in to hunt them down. Now\n                                                                             example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nthe streets of Mordheim belong to the Shadowlord and his\n                                                                             to four champions.\nservants. The contaminated air does not affect them at all or,\n                                                                        •    The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\nmore likely, it nourishes their inner corruption. Men who\n                                                                             be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nventure into Mordheim alone are hunted down and sacrificed\n                                                                             warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nto the dark gods. All warbands of the Possessed gather\n                                                                             the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nwyrdstone for the Shadowlord who remains hidden in the Pit\n                                                                        •    A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\nwhere he is said to be guarded by titanic Possessed the size of\n                                                                             weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nhouses. A few shards of the precious stone are kept by the\n                                                                             up the space of two weapons.\nwarbands and used to create more of the Possessed.\n                                                                        •    Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\n                                                                             is shown before the name. For example, 0-1 Priest of\nThe leaders of cult warbands are called Magisters and each\n                                                                             Ulric. The maximum number of Priests of Ulric in a\nleads a group of cultists: minions of the dark gods of Chaos.\n                                                                             warband is therefore 1.\nThese are men whose hunger for power knows no bounds,\nwho willingly give their bodies over to possession. All take part\nin the blood sacrifices, dark rituals, and worship of Daemons –"},{"page":94,"text":"Mutations\nThose who dwell in Mordheim soon develop horrible mutations, and the Cult of the Possessed seem to be especially susceptible. In\naddition, Mordheim attracts mutants from all over the Empire, who are always quick to join the Chaos covens. Most mutations are\nsimply inconvenient or hideous, but some make their bearers extremely dangerous in combat.\n\nMUTATION\nA warrior with this special rule must purchase a Mutation when they are recruited. Possessed Warriors must take 2 Mutations.\nYou may not buy new mutations for a model after recruitment. A warrior may only have one Mutation and it is rare for a\nMutation to be duplicated within the same warband. The nature of Chaos is never consistent. To represent this, the first warrior to\ntake a Mutation pays the cost shown for it. The second warrior to take the same Mutation pays double the cost shown, the third\none to take the same Mutation pays triple the cost shown and so on.\n    • Mutations cannot be disarmed.\n    • Mutations do not count as a weapon when equipping warriors.\n\n\ndaemon soul                                                         blackblood\nCOST: 25 GOLD CROWNS.                                               COST: 30 GOLD CROWNS\nA Daemon lives within the warrior’s body. The warrior gains         If the warrior loses a wound in close combat, any warrior in\nthe special rule Magic Resistance (4+). Note, this doesn’t dispel   base contact (friend or foe) with the model suffers a Strength 3\nthe spell, which may still affect other warriors.                   hit from the spurting corrosive blood. Make armour saves as\n                                                                    normal.\ngreat claw\nCOST: 40 GOLD CROWNS.                                               spines\nOne of the warrior’s arms ends in a huge claw, this may be          COST: 35 GOLD CROWNS\nshaped like a crab claw, or another beast. He may carry no          Any model in base contact with the mutant suffers an\nweapon or shield in this arm, it counts as an additional hand       automatic Strength 1 hit at the beginning of each close combat\nweapon, the warrior can make close combat attacks with the          phase. The warrior cannot wear armour.\nfollowing weapon profile:\n                                                                    scorpion tail\n Weapon        Range        Str        D           AP\n                                                                    COST: 45 GOLD CROWNS\nGreat Claw      Melee       S+1        1           -1\n                                                                    The warrior has a long-barbed tail with a venomous tip. The\nTraits: Hack, Rending\n                                                                    warrior can make an extra close combat attack with following\n                                                                    weapon profile:\nbestial legs                                                        Weapon                 Range           Str      D        AP\nCOST: 10 GOLDCROWNS                                                 Scorpion Tail           Melee           4       1        -1\nThe warriors’ legs are like that of animal, most commonly a         Traits: Poison\ngoat with cloven hooves. The warrior gains +1 Movement to its\nbase profile.                                                       extra arm\n                                                                    COST: 45 GOLD CROWNS\ntentacle                                                            The warrior gains an additional +1 attack in close combat, just\nCOST: 25 GOLD CROWNS                                                like an additional weapon in the offhand.\nOne of the warrior’s arms is replaced with a tentacle. It counts    Alternatively, the warrior may carry a shield or a buckler in the\nas an additional hand weapon and the warrior can make               extra arm. Possessed cannot use weapon or armour but can\nattacks with the following profile:                                 still gain the extra attack.\n  Weapon         Range      Str       D         AP\n  Tentacle       Melee        S        1         -                  hideous appearance\nTraits: Disarm, Entangle\n                                                                    COST: 40 GOLD CROWNS\n                                                                    The warrior causes fear."},{"page":95,"text":"long tongue                                                        scaly skin\nCOST: 40 GOLD CROWNS                                               COST: 25 GOLD CROWNS\nThe warrior has very long tongue which it can flick out to         The warrior has a 6+ Armour Save. If the warrior is wearing\nattack enemies from a distance.                                    armour, then its save roll is improved by 1. For example, a\nWeapon                  Range          Str       D         AP      warrior with light armour and a Scaly Skin will have a saving\nLong Tongue               3”            3         1        +1      throw of 5+.\nTraits: Knock back, Entangle, Versatile\n                                                                   spiked tail\nhorns                                                              COST: 45 GOLD CROWNS\nCOST: 25 GOLD CROWNS                                               The warrior gains an extra close combat attack with the\nThe warrior has a huge pair of sharp horns growing from its        following weapon profile:\nhead. The warrior gains the skill Bull Charge.                     Weapon                 Range          Str        AP          D\n                                                                   Club                   Melee           S         +1          1\nsoporific musk                                                     Traits: Stun\n\nCOST: 20 GOLD CROWNS\nThe warrior exudes a heady and unnatural scent that ensnares       chameleon skin\nthe mind and slows the limbs.                                      COST: 30 GOLD CROWNS\nAny enemy warriors engaged in close combat must make a WP          Any enemy warriors making a ranged attack against this this\ncheck or have -1 to hit. Has no effect on Undead.                  warrior incurs an extra -1 to-hit penalty at long range. If the\n                                                                   warrior wears armour this ability is lost.\ngaping maw\nCOST: 20 GOLD CROWNS                                               bloated\nIf the warrior is Standing and Engaged, they can make the          COST: 45 GOLD CROWNS\nfollowing action:                                                  The warrior’s Wound characteristic is increased by +1 to its\nRETRACTABLE JAW (Basic) – One Engaged enemy warrior                base profile.\nmust make an Initiative Check. If failed the warrior suffers a\nhit with a Strength equal to this warrior's Strength +2 resolved   manifold eyes\nat Damage 2.\n                                                                   COST: 20 GOLD CROWNS\n                                                                   The mutant has eyes like that of a fly.\nsuckers                                                            The warrior has a 360 degree vision arc instead of 90 degrees.\nCOST: 20 GOLD CROWNS                                               Backstab trait has no effect on this warrior.\nThe warrior gains the Scale Sheer Surface skill.\n                                                                   acute senses\neyestalks                                                          COST: 20 GOLD CROWNS\nCOST: 10 GOLD CROWNS                                               The warrior has animal-like vision, hearing, or sense of smell.\nThe warrior has a 180 degree vision arc instead of 90 degrees      The warrior gains the Acute Senses special rule.\nand can make attacks within this arc.\n                                                                   double jointed\n                                                                   COST: 10 GOLD CROWNS\n                                                                   The warrior has no penalty for Turn to Face in close combat."},{"page":96,"text":"Heroes\n\n                      1 Magister                                                      Darksouls\nCOST TO HIRE: 110 Gold Crowns.                                   COST TO HIRE: 70 Gold Crowns\nMagisters lead the covens of the Possessed. They have been       Darksouls are men who have been driven insane by the\ngranted magical powers by their patron gods. They are            daemonic possession which became all too common after the\nfanatical followers of the Dark gods, utterly dedicated to       destruction of Mordheim. The Daemons have left the bodies\nbringing Chaos to the world.                                     of these men, but their minds have been scarred by the horror\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL   WIL     INT    of the experience.\n 4     4     3    3   3   2    3   2    8     8     8      8     Their insane strength makes Darksouls dangerous warriors.\n                                                                 The Cultists regard them as holy men, and let them work out\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           their unreasoning rage in battle. In their tortured minds the\nA Magister starts with no equipment. They have no                Darksouls believe themselves to be Daemons. They wear\nequipment restrictions.                                          leering daemonic masks and garb themselves in armour and\n                                                                 clothing resembling the scaled skin of Daemons.\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                    M    WS    BS   S   T    W   I   A   LD   CL    WIL   INT\nRace (Human), Leader, Wizard (Cast Spells Chaos Rituals)          4     3    2    4   3    2   4   2   7     7     6      6\n\n\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                  WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their         A Darksoul starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does     Close Combat Weapons, Darksouls Weapons, Armour, and\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.                         Wargear from the Possessed Equipment List.\n\n\n                 0-2 The Possessed                               SPECIAL RULES:\n                                                                 Race (Human), Champion, Fearless\nCOST TO HIRE: 130 Gold Crowns.\nThe Possessed have committed the greatest of heresies: they                               Mutants\nhave given their bodies to Daemons. As a result, they are\nnightmarish creatures, a melding of flesh, metal and black       COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns.\nmagic. Inside them lives a supernatural thing of evil, a         Mutants are revered as the favoured ones of the Dark gods,\nDaemon from the dark reaches of the Realm of Chaos.              their physical disfigurements marking out the vileness of\nThe powerful spirit of a Daemon can meld several creatures       their soul. They come in many shapes and sizes, each more\ntogether, be they men or animals, into a multi-faceted horror.   bizarre than the next.\nThese monstrous Possessed are perhaps the most dangerous          M    WS    BS   S   T    W   I   A   LD   CL    WIL   INT\nof the creatures of Mordheim, and certainly the most              4     2    2    3   3    1   2   1   6     6     6      6\nloathsome and dreadful.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT    WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n 5     4     1    4   4   3    4   3    7     7     8      6     A Mutant starts with no equipment. They may purchase\n                                                                 Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           Wargear from the Possessed Equipment List.\nNone. Natural Weapons\n                                                                 SPECIAL RULES:\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   Race (Human), Raw Recruit.\nRace (Possessed) Champion, Daemonic, Mutation, Large\nTarget\n\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value."},{"page":97,"text":"Henchmen\n\n                         Brethren\nCOST TO HIRE: 35Gold Crowns\nBrethren are the crazed human followers of the cults of the\ndark gods, eager to descend into damnation. Their vile deeds\nand unspeakable acts have driven them to the brink of\ninsanity.\n M    WS    BS   S   T    W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\n 4     3     3   3   3    1   3   1    7     7     7      7\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Brethren starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nClose Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nWargear from the Possessed Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Human), Henchmen\n\n\n                  0~3 Beastmen\nCOST TO HIRE: 45Gold Crowns\nBeastmen are mutated monstrosities that infest the forests of\nthe Empire: massive horned creatures with an inhuman\nresistance to pain. The destruction of Mordheim brought\nmany Beastmen into the ruined city to prey upon the\nsurvivors. They readily ally with the Magisters of the\nPossessed warbands.\n M    WS    BS   S   T    W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\n 5     4     3   3   4    1   3   1    6     7     7      6\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Beastman starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nClose Combat Weapons, Darksouls Weapons, Armour, and\nWargear from the Possessed Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Beastman), Henchmen"},{"page":98,"text":"The Possessed Equipment List\nCLOSE COMBAT WEAPONS                                                  DARKSOULS WEAPONS\nITEM                                PRICE                             ITEM                                PRICE\nAxe                                 15                                Flail                               30\nClub                                15                                Morning Star                        30\nDagger                              10\nFlaming Torch                       25                                SPECIAL WEAPONS\nGreat Axe                           50                                ITEM                                PRICE\nGreat Hammer                        50                                Morning Star                        30\nGreat Sword                         45                                Staff                               25\nHammer Or Mace                      20\nSpear                               15                                WARGEAR\nSword                               25                                ITEM                                PRICE\n                                                                      Lantern                             40\nMISSILE WEAPONS                                                       Rope And Hook                       30\nITEM                                    PRICE\nBow                                     15\nShort bow                               10\n\nARMOUR\nITEM                                PRICE\nLight Armour                        20\nHeavy Armour                        50\nShield                              20\n\n\n\n\n                                           Possessed skill access\nPossessed warband Warriors have access to the following skills:\n                Agility     Brawn         Combat      Cunning     Ferocity    Leadership   Shooting   Academic    Resilience   Savagery\nMagsiter                                  Secondary   Secondary   Primary     Primary                 Primary\nThe Possessed   Secondary   Secondary                             Secondary                                       Primary      Primary\nDarksoul                    Primary                               Primary     Secondary                           Secondary    Secondary\nMutants                     Secondary     Secondary               Primary\nBrethren                    Secondary     Primary     Secondary   Primary\nBeastmen                    Secondary                             Primary                                         Primary      Secondary"},{"page":99,"text":"Rewards of the shadowlord\nWhen a Magister, Darksoul or Mutant from a Possessed warband has accumulated enough experience, instead of picking a skill,\nthey may roll on the Rewards table below. This represents the pilgrimage of the Mutant or Magister to the Pit, where he can\nbeseech a favour from the Shadowlord himself.\n\n\n2D      Result\n6\n2       Wrath of the Shadowlord! The warrior is mutated beyond recognition and vanishes into the ruins, joining the many\n        other horrors that roam Mordheim.\n3-6     Nothing Happens. The capricious Shadowlord ignores the pleas of his servant.\n\n7-8     Mutation. The warrior develops a severe mutation. Roll a D6. On a roll of 1 you lose a single point from one of your\n        warrior’s characteristics (chosen by you), due to atrophy, or some such degrading mutation. On a roll of 2 or more you\n        may choose which one of the mutations listed in the Cult of the Possessed Warbands section your warrior has been\n        rewarded with.\n9-10    Chaos Armour. The warrior’s body becomes encrusted with an arcane, all enveloping suit of armour. This confers am\n        armour save of 4+ but does not affect the model’s ability to cast spells or move in any way.\n11      Daemon Weapon. The warrior receives a weapon with a bound Daemon inside it. The weapon has the following profile:\n\n                        Weapon                  Range              Str               AP                D\n                        Daemon Weapon           Melee 3            S+1               -1                1\n\n        Traits: Accuracy (grants a +1 bonus on all to hit rolls when using it), Magical.\n        The user may choose the weapon’s form (a sword, an axe, etc), though it will not have any of the Weapon Traits normally\n        associated with common weapons of that type.\n12      Possessed! A Daemon takes over the soul and body of the warrior. The warrior immediately gains the following:\n            • +1 Weapon Skill, +1 Strength, +1 Attacks +1 Wounds.\n            • The warrior’s race is changed to Race (Possessed). The Maximum Characteristics are now those of the Possessed.\n            • The warrior loses D3 of his skills (chosen by the player).\n            • The warrior gains the Daemonic special rules.\n            • The warrior may no longer use weapons, armour, or equipment, except for Chaos Armour or Daemon weapons."},{"page":100,"text":"Witch hunters\nThe Order of Templars of Sigmar, universally known as the             headgear which conceal their appearance from the overly\nWitch Hunters, is an organisation dedicated to the eradication        curious. Some wear chains about their throats to remind them\nof heretics, be they warlocks, witches, sorcerers, fortune-tellers,   of fallen comrades and old rivalries and also, so it is said, so\nnecromancers, worshippers of the dark gods, deviants,                 that the iron might serve as protection against witchcraft.\nmutants, blasphemers, sinners, utterers of profanities, servants      The followers of the Witch Hunters, the rabble that accompany\nof Daemons, or composers of corrupting music. Indeed, there           them to Mordheim, are a far more dire sight indeed – crazed\nare few who altogether escape the suspicions of the Witch             and self-mutilated men who have lost or surrendered all their\nHunters with the possible exception of other Witch Hunters.           worldly goods and, most likely, their reason as well.\nIt is wise to remember that the practice of magic in all its forms\nis deemed a most heinous crime in the Empire. Death by fire is\nthe proscribed punishment for this particular heresy. Many of\nthe Witch Hunters’ victims treacherously avoid their fate by          Witch hunter Warbands\nperishing under torture before making a full confession. In           The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nthese troubled times the Witch Hunters are kept busy as more          To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\nand more men turn to the dark arts. The most dangerous of all         must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nthese heretics are the followers of the Chaos gods. These             gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\ndepraved individuals practise Daemon worship and (it is               be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nclaimed) even offer human sacrifices in the name of their vile\nmasters. Of all the enemies of Sigmar they are the most               WARBAND COMPOSITION\nabhorrent!                                                            The warband must follow these rules when it is created, and\nThe destruction of Mordheim has fired the Witch Hunters               when new warriors are added to the warband.\nwith a new and irresistible sense of purpose. In the light of\nevents the Grand Theogonist has proclaimed Sigmar’s                       •    There must be one leader (Witch Hunter Captain)\npunishment on the City of the Damned. The Witch Hunters                        chosen when the warband is first founded (if the\nrejoice that their crusade against widespread corruption has                   leader is killed see below)\nbeen vindicated. Now they are ready to complete Sigmar’s holy             •    There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\npurpose by destroying his enemies within the ruins of the city                 for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nitself. The Grand Theogonist has commanded the Witch                           example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nHunters to go unto that place and recover the wyrdstone for                    to four champions.\nSigmar’s temple. Their crusade also pits them into the same               •    The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\narena as their old enemies the so-called Sisters of Sigmar –                   be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nthose loathsome Daemon-worshipping she-heretics whose                          warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nvery existence is a vile affront to the majesty of Sigmar.                     the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nWitch Hunters are charismatic rabble-rousers who can soon                 •    A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\nturn a crowd to their own ends. They are universally dreaded,\n                                                                               weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nfor everyone has something or someone to hide, and there are\n                                                                               up the space of two weapons.\ncountless individuals who would willingly and enthusiastically\n                                                                          •    Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\nhunt down and burn their own kin were a Witch Hunter to\n                                                                               is shown before the name. For example, 0-1 Priest of\ncommand them to do so. Bands of Witch Hunters are often\n                                                                               Ulric. The maximum number of Priests of Ulric in a\naccompanied by zealous citizens, Flagellants, and even holy\n                                                                               warband is therefore 1.\nPriests of Sigmar as well as the huge vicious warhounds which\nthe Witch Hunters employ to track and bring down fugitives.\nAs men accustomed to fighting Witch Hunters are well-armed\nand sturdy individuals. They favour hooded cloaks and"},{"page":101,"text":"Heroes\n\n           1 Witch Hunter captain                                           0-1 Priest of Sigmar\nCOST TO HIRE: 125 Gold Crowns.                                  COST TO HIRE: 55 Gold Crowns.\nDriven by fanaticism, Witch Hunter Captains are obsessed        Many powerful fighting men have come from the ranks of the\nwith cleansing Mordheim and bringing the justice of Sigmar      faithful. The Priests of Sigmar are no exception, and the\nto all. Carrying the edict of the Grand Theogonist himself,     military wing of the cult is feared and respected throughout\nthey have the divine right to judge and execute warlocks,       the Empire.\nwitches, Chaos worshippers… in fact all who dare to oppose      The Grand Theogonist himself has granted the Warrior-\nthem.                                                           Priests an edict to cleanse Mordheim of Chaos filth. With fire\n M    WS    BS    S    T   W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT   burning in their eyes, the Warrior- Priests stride into battle,\n 4     4     4    3    3   2   4   3    8     8     7      7    chanting aloud the Deus Sigmar, the praise of the patron god\n                                                                of the Empire.\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           M    WS    BS   S    T   W    I   A   LD    CL   WIL    INT\nA Witch Hunter Captain starts with no equipment. They may        4     3     3   3    3   2    3   1    7    8      8      8\npurchase Close Combat Weapons, Special Weapons, Armour,\nand Wargear from the Witch Hunter Equipment List.               WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                A Priest of Sigmar starts with no equipment. They may\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                  purchase Priest Weapons, Armour, and Wargear from the\nRace (Human), Leader                                            Witch Hunter Equipment List.\n\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their        SPECIAL RULES:\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does    Race (Human), Champion, Priest (Cast Spells Prayers of\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.                        Sigmar)\n\n\n                      Witch hunters                             STARTING SKILL:\n                                                                When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nCOST TO HIRE: 80 Gold Crowns.                                   Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nWitch Hunters are members of the grim Order of Witch            not increase the warrior’s credit value.\nHunters, dedicated to eradicating Chaos and all its minions.\nUsually they prowl the Old World individually trying and                             Interrogators\nexecuting the enemies of Sigmar, but the situation in\nMordheim requires them to band together.                        COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns.\n M    WS    BS    S    T   W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT   These are young Witch Hunters who are still inexperienced,\n 4     4     3    3    3   2   4   2    8     7     7      7    but eager to hunt down and burn their first witch.\n                                                                 M    WS    BS   S    T   W    I   A   LD    CL   WIL    INT\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           4     2     2   3    3   1    2   1    6    6      6      6\nA Witch Hunter starts with no equipment. They may\npurchase Close Combat Weapons, Special Weapons, Armour,         WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nand Wargear from the Witch Hunter Equipment List.               An Interrogator starts with no equipment. They may\n                                                                purchase Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons,\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                  Armour, and Wargear from the Witch Hunter Equipment\nRace (Human), Champion                                          List.\n\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                 SPECIAL RULES:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their      Race (Human), Raw Recruit.\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value."},{"page":102,"text":"Henchmen\n\n                 0-5 Flagellants                                                          Zealots\nCOST TO HIRE: 50 Gold Crowns                                     COST TO HIRE: 25 Gold Crowns\nFlagellants are fanatics and madmen obsessed with the end of     When a man loses his family, home and all he cared for,\nthe world. They are often men who have lost their families to    religion is often the last refuge left to him. Such men become\nwar or the ravages of nature and have also lost their minds.     wandering pilgrims, bitter and dangerous fanatics who are\nWith insane persistence, they travel the length and breadth of   prepared to avenge their loss at any cost. These men are\nthe Empire, preaching their view of the end of the world.        called Zealots.\nWith their rousing speeches, Witch Hunters can muster these      Zealots have forsaken their former lives and exist only to\ndangerous lunatics to fight in the streets of Mordheim, where    destroy evil and the minions of Chaos. Whilst they might\nno sane man dares tread.                                         have been peasants and craftsmen before, and thus may not\nFlagellants are extremely dangerous opponents in close           be as dangerous in a fight as seasoned mercenaries, their\ncombat, for they have the strength of madmen, and their          determination and fanaticism should not be underestimated.\nbodies have become inured to pain because of self-mutilation.    Witch Hunters find ready allies in their ranks, and many a\n M    WS    BS   S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL   WIL    INT      band of Zealots is led by Witch Hunters.\n 4     3     3   3   3    1   3   1    7     7     7      7       M    WS    BS   S   T    W    I   A   LD    CL   WIL    INT\n                                                                  4     2     2   3   3    1    3   1    7    7      6      6\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Flagellant starts with no equipment. They may purchase         WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nFlagellant Weapons from the Witch Hunter Equipment List.         A Zealot starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close\n                                                                 Combat Weapons, Zealot Weapons, Armour, and Wargear\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   from the Witch Hunter Equipment List.\nRace (Human), Henchmen, Fearless, Frenzy\n(Flagellants can never become the leader).                       SPECIAL RULES:\n                                                                 Race (Human), Henchmen"},{"page":103,"text":"Witch hunter Equipment List\nCLOSE COMBAT WEAPONS                                                   PRIEST WEAPONS\nITEM                                PRICE                              ITEM                                PRICE\nAxe                                 20                                 Aspergilla Morning Star             50\nClub                                15                                 Blessed Water                       20\nDagger                              10                                 Club                                15\nFlaming Torch                       20                                 Dagger                              10\nGreat Axe                           55                                 Flaming Torch                       25\nGreat Hammer                        50                                 Great Hammer                        45\nGreat Sword                         40                                 Hammer or Mace                      20\nHammer Or Mace                      20                                 Staff                               25\nSword                               25\n                                                                       ZEALOT WEAPONS\nMISSILE WEAPONS                                                        ITEM                                PRICE\nITEM                                    PRICE                          Bow                                 15\nCrossbow                                30                             Short bow                           10\n                                                                       Spear                               20\nARMOUR                                                                 Staff                               25\nITEM                                    PRICE\nLight Armour                            20                             SPECIAL WEAPONS\nShield                                  20                             ITEM                                PRICE\n                                                                       Buckler                             10\nFLAGELLANT WEAPONS                                                     Crossbow Pistol                     35\nITEM                                    PRICE                          Heavy Armour                        50\nClub                                    15                             Pistol                              25\nFlail                                   30\nGreat Axe                               55                             WARGEAR\nGreat Hammer                            50                             ITEM                                PRICE\nGreat Sword                             45                             Lantern                             35\nMorning Star                            30                             Rope And Hook                       30\n                                                                       Wardog                              15\n\n\n\n\n                                         Witch hunter skill access\nWitch Hunter Warriors have access to the following skills:\n\n                Agility     Brawn         Combat      Cunning     Ferocity    Leadership   Shooting    Academic   Resilience   Savagery\nWitch Hunter                              Primary     Secondary   Primary     Primary      Secondary\nCaptain\nPriest of                   Secondary     Secondary               Secondary   Primary                  Primary\nSigmar\nWitch Hunters               Secondary     Primary                 Primary     Secondary    Secondary\nInterrogators                             Secondary               Primary                  Secondary\nFlagellants                 Secondary                             Primary                                         Primary      Secondary\nZealots         Secondary                 Primary     Secondary   Primary"},{"page":104,"text":"The Sisters of Sigmar\nFor centuries the nobility of the Empire has sent its wayward         Sigmar’s Rock in the vaults of their convent where, shielded by\nor troublesome daughters to the Holy Convent of the Order of          a great depth of solid granite and guarded by the eternal\nMerciful Sisters of Sigmar in Mordheim to be initiated into the       prayers of the sisterhood, it will cause no harm to Sigmar’s\nonly order of priestesses dedicated to the Empire’s patron god.       people. It is a nigh hopeless task, for there are few Sisters and\nThe Sisters of Sigmar, as they are commonly called, have              countless shards of stone. Worse still, there are many who\ntraditionally travelled the Empire administering to the sick and      want the stone for themselves, to take it from Mordheim and\npoor, tending to the needs of orphans, curing the diseased and        spread its contagion amongst the cities of the Empire.\nmending broken bodies. As well as the healing arts, which they        The warbands of the sisterhood are led by tough Canonesses,\npractise with expert knowledge of herb-lore and prayer, their         each accompanied by a body of warrior sisters. The training\nadvice is frequently sought by those about to make an                 and harsh discipline of the convent includes mastery of martial\nimportant decision, for the Sisters of Sigmar are famed for           as well as ecclesiastic skills, for mastery of the body is but the\ntheir ability to predict the fickle course of fate.                   first step towards the mastery of the soul. Their favoured\nThough once much loved by the common people, the Sisters              weapon is the warhammer, the instrument of Sigmar, seen as\nhave seen their popularity wane in recent years. Rabble-              his holy symbol, alongside the twin-tailed comet.\nrousing Witch Hunters have denounced them as witches and\nheretics, so that even in the countryside they are attacked and\ndriven away by the very peasants they seek to help. Many of           Sisters Warbands\nSigmar’s priests wish to disband the order altogether, claiming\n                                                                      The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nthat women have no right to teach the holy word of Sigmar.\n                                                                      To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\nEven the Grand Theogonist, ostensibly the chief authority over\n                                                                      must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nthe order, has cooled towards the sisterhood, denying the\n                                                                      gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\nthrone to Magritta of Marienburg who was brought up by the\n                                                                      be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nSisters and said to be sympathetic to their cause. These days\nthe Sisters of Sigmar have retreated to their convent situated\n                                                                      WARBAND COMPOSITION\nhigh on the craggy island of Sigmar’s Rock in the river Stir in\n                                                                      The warband must follow these rules when it is created, and\nMordheim.\n                                                                      when new warriors are added to the warband.\nOf all the inhabitants of Mordheim only the Sisters of Sigmar\nwere prepared for its destruction. Seeress Cassandora foretold\n                                                                          •    There must be one leader (Canoness) chosen when\nof the disaster and at their nightly vigil the Maidens of Sigmar\n                                                                               the warband is first founded (if the leader is killed see\nheard the voice of Sigmar speaking in their dreaming minds.\n                                                                               below)\nThus they knew that they would be safe in their fortress high\n                                                                          •    There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nabove the city, raised as it is above the polluted vapours, if only\n                                                                               for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nthey were prepared to survive the fire of Sigmar’s Fury.\n                                                                               example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nWhile the rest of Mordheim fell under a spell of madness the\n                                                                               to four champions.\nSisters of Sigmar offered prayer after prayer, scourging\n                                                                          •    The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\nthemselves to drive out all thoughts of sin, fervently accepting\n                                                                               be equal to or higher than the total number of other\na punishing penitential regime to harden their minds against\n                                                                               warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nthe wantonness running rampant outside their walls. When\n                                                                               the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nthe blow finally came the Sisters gathered beneath the great\n                                                                          •    A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\ntemple dome of their convent which, well built and fortified as\n                                                                               weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nit was by the prayers of the Sisters, protected them from the\n                                                                               up the space of two weapons.\nfire and heat of their master’s ire.\n                                                                          •    Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\nThe Sisters believe they have a holy mission, a task that they\n                                                                               is shown before the name. For example, 0-1 Priest of\nhave been set by Sigmar himself and to which they must\n                                                                               Ulric. The maximum number of Priests of Ulric in a\nsubmit themselves body and soul. Their sacred duty is to\n                                                                               warband is therefore 1.\ngather up the shards of wyrdstone and hide it deep beneath"},{"page":105,"text":"Heroes\n                       1 Canoness                                                           0-1 Augur\nCOST TO HIRE: 95 Gold Crowns.                                     COST TO HIRE: 40 Gold Crowns.\nThe Canoness of Sigmar, of whom there is an inner circle of       The blind Augurs of the Sisterhood are blessed beyond their\ntwelve, are answerable to the High Matriarch of the temple.       comrades. By giving up their sight they have gained\nEach must lead a warband of Sisters in frequent searches of       something far more, second sight – a gift from their patron\nthe city in order to purge the ruins. Canoness are driven by a    god. Only a very few are marked this way, and they are\nzealous devotion to the Cult of Sigmar and a relentless           greatly revered by the Sisterhood. Unlike the rest of the\ndetermination to redeem the Sisterhood in His eyes.               priestesses, they shave their heads, save for a single long\n M    WS    BS    S    T   W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT     braid.\n 4     4     3    3    3   2   3   3    8     8     8      8       M    WS    BS    S   T    W   I   A    LD    CL   WIL     INT\n                                                                   4     2     2    3   3    2   3    1    7     8     8      8\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Canoness starts with no equipment. They may purchase            WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nClose Combat Weapons, Special Weapons, Armour, and                An Augur starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nWargear from the Sisters of Sigmar Equipment List.                Close Combat Weapons, Special Weapons, Armour, and\n                                                                  Wargear from the Sisters of Sigmar Equipment List.\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Human), Leader, Priest (Cast Spells Prayers of Sigmar)      SPECIAL RULES:\n                                                                  Race (Human), Champion, Blessed Sight, Wyrdstone Seeker\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their          STARTING SKILL:\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does      When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.                          Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\n                                                                  not increase the warrior’s credit value.\n                      Sister superior\n                                                                                            Novices\nCOST TO HIRE: 80 Gold Crowns.\nEach of the Sisters Superior is a long-serving priestess of the   COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns.\nCult of Sigmar, well versed in the rituals of the temple and an   By tradition, the Sisters draw their recruits only from the\nexample to the younger Sisters and Novices. The Sisters           most noble houses of the Empire, and families consider it a\nSuperior are entrusted with maintaining the faith and fervour     great honour to have their daughter accepted into the order.\nof the order. Any peril or foe that may lurk in the ruins of      Only maidens of noble lineage can be relied upon to have the\nMordheim is as nothing compared to the wrath of a Sister          devotion to duty and innate sense of honour. Few though the\nSuperior.                                                         recruits may be, they must endure several years as Novices\n M    WS    BS    S    T   W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT     during which time their devotion will be tested to the full. All\n 4     4     3    3    3   2   4   2    8     7     7      7      are eager to prove themselves worthy to be the handmaidens\n                                                                  of Sigmar.\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                             M    WS    BS    S   T    W   I   A    LD    CL   WIL     INT\nA Sister Superior starts with no equipment. They may               4     2     2    3   3    1   2    1    6     6     6      6\npurchase Close Combat Weapons, Special Weapons, Armour,\nand Wargear from the Sisters of Sigmar Equipment List.            WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                  A Novice starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                    Combat Weapons, Armour, and Wargear from the Sisters of\nRace (Human), Champion                                            Sigmar Equipment List.\n\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                   SPECIAL RULES:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their        Race (Human), Raw Recruit.\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value."},{"page":106,"text":"Henchmen\n\n                 Sigmarite sister                                                       Penitents\nCOST TO HIRE: 35 Gold Crowns                                      COST TO HIRE: 25 Gold Crowns\nSigmarite Sisters know that their entire order is shamed in the   After the destruction of Mordheim some of the citizens\neyes of their Lord Sigmar. Every one of them is sworn upon        sought refuge in the Sisters of Sigmar convent situated high\nHis altar to pacify the city and thereby redeem themselves.       on the craggy island of Sigmar’s Rock. Most were turned\nWhatever the perils and horrors that stand in their way, they     away, but some of the more devout women were given\nwill be overcome!                                                 sanctuary. Although they have fallen short of the Sisterhood’s\n M    WS    BS   S   T   W     I   A   LD   CL    WIL    INT      stringent codes of service, some have been given a second\n 4     3     3   3   3    1   3    1    7    7      7      7      chance to redeem themselves.\n                                                                  These women are banded together with others who have\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                            fallen from grace, and they are given the opportunity to wash\nA Sigmarite Sister starts with no equipment. They may             away their sins with the blood of the faithless. Whilst they\npurchase Close Combat Weapons, Armour, and Wargear                might have been peasants and craftsmen before, their\nfrom the Sisters of Sigmar Equipment List.                        determination and fanaticism should not be underestimated.\n                                                                  It may even be possible for a Penitent to redeem herself\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                    through deeds of great bravery and butchery.\nRace (Human), Henchmen                                             M    WS    BS   S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\n                                                                   4     2     2   3   3    1   3   1    7     7     6      6\n\n\n                                                                  WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                  A Penitent starts with no equipment. They may purchase\n                                                                  Penitent Weapons, Armour, and Wargear from the Sisters of\n                                                                  Sigmar Equipment List.\n\n                                                                  SPECIAL RULES:\n                                                                  Race (Human), Henchmen"},{"page":107,"text":"Sisters of Sigmar Equipment List\nCLOSE COMBAT WEAPONS                                                 SPECIAL WEAPONS\nITEM                               PRICE                             ITEM                               PRICE\nDagger                             10                                Aspergilla Morning Star            50\nFlail                              35                                Blessed Water                      20\nGreat Hammer                       50                                Buckler                            10\nHammer Or Mace                     20                                Heavy Armour                       50\n                                                                     Holy Tome                          140\nPENITENT WEAPONS                                                     Morning Star                       30\nITEM                                 PRICE                           Religious Symbol                   30\nAxe                                  20                              Sacred Relic                       45\nBow                                  15                              Sigmarite Warhammer                40\nClub                                 15                              Whip                               25\nDagger                               10\nHammer or Mace                       20                              ARMOUR\nShort bow                            10                              ITEM                              PRICE\nSling                                5                               Light Armour                      20\nSpear                                20                              Shield                            20\nStaff                                25\nSword                                25                              WARGEAR\n                                                                     ITEM                               PRICE\n                                                                     Lantern                            40\n                                                                     Rope And Hook                      30\n\n\n\n\n                                             Sisters skill access\nSisters of Sigmar Warriors have access to the following skills:\n\n                  Agility     Brawn         Combat       Cunning      Ferocity      Leadership   Shooting   Academic     Resilience\nCanoness                                    Secondary                 Primary       Primary                 Secondary    Primary\nAugur             Primary                   Primary      Secondary    Secondary                                          Secondary\nSister Superior               Secondary     Primary                   Primary       Secondary               Secondary\nNovices                       Secondary     Secondary                 Primary\nSigmarite                     Secondary     Primary                   Primary                                            Secondary\nSister\nPenitents         Secondary                 Primary      Secondary    Primary\n\n\nThe Sisters of Sigmar Special Rules\nBLESSED SIGHT: A warrior with this skill may re-roll any failed characteristic checks (climbing, resisting spells or any other\nreason), and any rolls they make when rolling to hit in close combat or shooting.\n\nWYRDSTONE SEEKER: In the Exploration Phase of the post-battle sequence, as long as the warrior is not Captured or In\nRecovery, you may roll two dice and pick either result."},{"page":108,"text":"The Undead\nCount Vlad von Carstein and his wife Isabella have ruled the\nprovince of Sylvania for as long as anyone can remember –           Undead Warbands\npeasants whisper of some dark secret, Witch Hunters revile\n                                                                    The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nthem, and the Priests of Sigmar shun their court. Indeed,\n                                                                    To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\nSylvania has the most dire reputation of all the provinces of the\n                                                                    must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nEmpire. Few men sent to spy on the rulers of Sylvania have\n                                                                    gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\never returned from those dark Sylvanian forests, and then\n                                                                    be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nrarely with their sanity intact.\nIn the dimly-lit chamber of the Drakenhof castle, on a throne\n                                                                    WARBAND COMPOSITION\nof black obsidian, sits Vlad von Carstein, the ruler of Sylvania.\n                                                                    An Undead warband must follow these rules when it is created,\nHe waits in shadows, having set himself apart from the politics\n                                                                    and when new warriors are added to the warband.\nand bickering of the Empire. For he holds a terrible secret: he,\nand all the ruling aristocracy of his province are Vampires,\n                                                                        •   There must be one leader (Vampire) chosen when the\nundying monsters from beyond the grave. Here he patiently\n                                                                            warband is first founded (if the leader is killed see\nwaits, drinking the blood of maidens from gold goblets.\n                                                                            below)\nFor many long years Vlad has gathered his strength and\n                                                                        •   There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nmustered his Undead legions in secrecy. One day soon he will\n                                                                            for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nmarch from the forests of Sylvania at the head of an army of\n                                                                            example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nrestless dead. The pieces of magic stone that lie scattered\n                                                                            to four champions.\namong the ruins of Mordheim can give the Count the power to\nchallenge the nobles of the Empire and enslave the men of the           •   The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\nOld World.                                                                  be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nWyrdstone holds enough captured magical energy to unleash a                 warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\ngreat spell of doom to rival that of Nagash the Black. If the               the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nCount is successful, he will raise all the dead between the             •   A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\nWorlds Edge Mountains and the borders of Stirland, and go to                weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nwar against the divided rulers of the Empire. His plans laid out,           up the space of two weapons.\nVlad sends his thralls, the immortal Vampires, to do his                •   Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\nbidding.                                                                    is shown before the name. For example, 0-1\nDuring dark, moonless nights, black coaches arrive at the gates             Necromancer. The maximum number of\nof Mordheim carrying coffins. Ghouls scuttle from their hiding              Necromancers in a warband is therefore 1.\nplaces to greet them, and corpses are stirred by a command\nwhich the living cannot hear. Following the commands of the\nVampire, they hunt for shards of wyrdstone.\nThe night belongs to the Undead, and in Mordheim it is always\nnight."},{"page":109,"text":"Heroes\n                        1 Vampire                                                             Grave Guard\nCOST TO HIRE: 180 Gold Crowns.                                         COST TO HIRE: 100 Gold Crowns.\nVampires lead the Undead in their search for the magical stones that   Although their bodies have decayed, leaving only bones and tattered\nwill give their master the power to conquer the Empire. Although       flesh, Grave Guard are held together by evil magic so strong that it\nbut pale shadows when compared to the dread Vampire Lords, the         has endured for centuries. They wear ancient rust-gnawed armour,\nimmortal servants of Vlad are still some of the most powerful          corroded by time and dusty with the years. These eerie, silent\ncreatures who fight in Mordheim. Most of them serve the undying        sentinels stand constant vigil on the crumbling battlements and at\ncount of Sylvania, but some have found the city to their liking, and   the iron-bound gates, never resting, eternally ready to defend their\nhave become independent.                                               Vampire masters.\n M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT                                         M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT\n 6     5      3    4   4    2    5   3     8     8      8      8        4      3     2    3    3   2    2    2    6     5      5       5\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                                 WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Dreg starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close               A Grave Guard starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nCombat Weapons, Vampire Weapons, Armour, and Wargear                   Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nfrom the Undead Equipment List.                                        Wargear from the Undead Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                         SPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Vampire), Leader, Undead, Vampiric.                              Race (Undead) Champion, Undead ,No deal, Wight Blades.\n\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                        STARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their               When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does           Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.                               not increase the warrior’s credit value.\n\n\n                  0~1 Necromancer                                                                  Dregs\nCOST TO HIRE: 60 Gold Crowns.                                          COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns.\nNecromancers are evil wizards, studying the corrupt art of             Dregs are very useful to their masters as they can be sent to buy\nNecromancy. Many of them are acolytes and servants of Vlad von         equipment, weapons and supplies from the settlements around\nCarstein, and follow the agents of their master to the city of the     Mordheim which would often not welcome Necromancers or where\nDamned. Others are recruited from amongst wizards and warlocks         Vampires would fall under the suspicion of the Witch Hunters.\nwho have come under the suspicion of the various agents of Sigmar      They can also do the bidding of their vampiric master during\nand have fled to Mordheim to avoid persecution.                        daylight, when the Vampires must rest in their coffins.\n M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT                                        M WS BS S T W I A LD CL WIL INT\n 4     3      3    3   3    2    3   1     7     8      8      8        4      2     2    3    3   1    2    1    6     6      6       6\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                                 WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Necromance starts with no equipment. They may purchase               A Dreg starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close\nNecromancer Weapons and Wargear from the Undead                        Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and Wargear\nEquipment List.                                                        from the Undead Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                         SPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Human), Champion, Wizard (Cast Spells                            Race (Human), Raw Recruit.\nNecromancy), Fearless.\n\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value."},{"page":110,"text":"Henchmen\n\n                     Crypt Ghouls                                                         Zombies\nCOST TO HIRE: 45 Gold Crowns                                    COST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns\nGhouls are the descendants of evil and insane men who ate       Zombies are the most common of the Undead: creatures\nthe flesh of the dead. When the lean and hungry times of        animated by the will of their Necromantic masters.\nfamine come upon the Old World, the most depraved and           Individually, a zombie is a clumsy and slow adversary, but in\ndestitute took to feasting on corpses to survive.               bulk they become a significant threat. Bludgeoning aside\nDriven by their unspeakable craving for the meat of their       enemy defences, they lash out with filthy fingernails and\nfellow men, these creatures have given up their human life      crude improvised weapons, heedless of their losses\nand dwell near graveyards, crypts and tombs, digging up the\nrotting corpses of the recently buried and consuming the cold\nflesh with their bare teeth and claws.\nThe destruction of Mordheim attracted many Ghoul clans           M    WS    BS    S   T    W   I   A    LD   CL    WIL    INT\nfrom the north, and now they have taken up permanent\nresidence in the crypts and cemeteries of the ruined city.       4     2     0    3   3    1   1   1    5     5      5      5\n M    WS    BS   S    T   W   I   A   LD   CL    WIL    INT\n 4     3    2    3    4   1   3   2    6    5     6      5      WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                Zombies may not have any weapons or armour and suffer no\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                          penalties for this.\nNone. Natural Weapons.\n                                                                SPECIAL RULES:\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                  Race (Undead), Henchmen, Undead, No brain,\nRace (Ghoul), Henchmen, Poisoned Attacks, Fear, Starving        Summonded, Undead Horde\n\n\n                                                                                 Skeleton Warriors\n                                                                COST TO HIRE: 35 Gold Crowns\n                                                                Beneath the mud lie the grave-stained bones of these bitter,\n                                                                ancient warriors. Long held beneath the earth, they are clad\n                                                                in their corroded armour, their lifeless hands still gripping\n                                                                the swords, axes, spears and shields they held in life. Provided\n                                                                their remains have not been blessed by the rites of Morr, a\n                                                                Necromancer or Vampire can use the coiling energies of\n                                                                Dark Magic to instil a semblance of life and a flicker of spirit\n                                                                into these dormant warriors.\n                                                                 M    WS    BS    S   T    W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\n                                                                 4     2     2    3   3    1   2   1    5     5      5      5\n\n\n                                                                WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                A Skeleton Warrior starts with no equipment. They may\n                                                                purchase Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons,\n                                                                Armour, and Wargear from the Undead Equipment List.\n\n                                                                SPECIAL RULES:\n                                                                Race (Undead) Henchmen, Undead, No Brain, Summoned"},{"page":111,"text":"Undead Equipment List\nCLOSE COMBAT WEAPONS                                                    MISSILE WEAPONS\nITEM                                PRICE                               ITEM                                    PRICE\nAxe                                 20                                  Bow                                     15\nClub                                15                                  Crossbow                                30\nDagger                              10\nGreat Axe                           55                                  VAMPIRE WEAPONS\nGreat Hammer                        50                                  ITEM                                    PRICE\nGreat Sword                         45                                  Buckler                                 10\nHalberd                             30                                  Bastard Sword                           35\nHammer Or Mace                      20                                  Rapier                                  35\nSpear                               15\nSword                               25                                  ARMOUR\n                                                                        ITEM                                    PRICE\nNECROMANCER WEAPONS                                                     Light Armour                            20\nITEM                                PRICE                               Heavy Armour                            50\nAxe                                 20                                  Shield                                  20\nClub                                15\nDagger                              10                                  WARGEAR\nHammer Or Mace                      20                                  ITEM                                    PRICE\nStaff                               20                                  Lantern                                 40\nSword                               25                                  Rope And Hook                           30\n                                                                        Dire Wolves                             45\n\n\n\n\n                                              Undead skill access\nUndead Warriors have access to the following skills:\n                 Agility       Brawn         Combat        Cunning       Ferocity      Leadership     Academic      Resilience   Savagery\nVampire          Primary                     Primary                     Secondary     Primary                                   Secondary\nNecromancer      Secondary                                 Primary       Secondary     Secondary      Primary\nGrave Guard                    Primary       Primary                     Secondary     Secondary                    Secondary\nDreg                           Secondary                   Primary       Secondary\nGhoul            Secondary                                 Primary       Primary                                                 Secondary\n\nUndead Special Rules\nNO BRAIN:\nA warrior with this trait cannot gain experience.\nSUMMONED:\nIf a 1-2 Memorable Death is rolled for a Summoned Warrior, you can Recruit a new one for half the price.\nUNDEAD HORDE:\nAt the end of the Choose Crew step of the pre-battle sequence, you can use the underdog bonuses to put 0-5 Zombies , while\npaying the cost.\nNO DEAL:\nGrave Guards may not search for rare items\nWIGHT BLADES:\nGrave Guards carry weapons laden with evil magic. All close combat ‘to hit’ rolls of a 6 will automatically wound. You may roll\n‘to wound’ as normal to determine if it is a ‘critical hit’, but even a failed ‘to wound’ roll will still cause a wound if a 6 was rolled\nfirst ‘to hit’.\nSKELETON MINOR HERO:\nA note about Grave Guard. A Grave Guard is not actually learning new skills or truly gaining experience in the traditional sense,\ninstead it can be thought of as becoming more powerful as the Necromancer continues to practice their dark arts on them, dark\nrituals that increase their strength and power. Or perhaps some of the skills they had in life are starting to return. The inverse\ngoes for Lasting Injuries, the damage done to them weakens their magical bonds."},{"page":112,"text":"Skaven\nUnbeknownst to man, for thousands of years he has shared his\nworld with another and altogether different race. There have        The Skaven of Clan Eshin are supremely adapted to their task.\nalways been signs for those who cared to see them: a scurrying      Masters of the art of bringing silent death to their foes, they are\nblack shadow, an inhuman scream from the sewer, scuttling           skilled in the use of poison and trained in the thousand secrets\nshapes at the back of the cellar. All these years these creatures   of the assassin. Since birth Skaven warriors practise martial\nhave worked away in secret, burrowing beneath the world of          crafts in the ruinous temples of the Horned Rat, their ever\nman, undermining his great cities, infiltrating his sewers and      hungering and hideous god. There are none better amongst\ncellars, and joining all up into a vast world spanning labyrinth    their verminous kind to gather up the treasure of Mordheim,\nof tunnels and nests. These creatures call themselves Skaven        but they must be silent, swift and efficient. Were rival Skaven\nand they are ratmen, the mutant spawn of an older age of            clans to discover the secret of Mordheim there would come not\nchaos and mutation.                                                 hundreds, not thousands, but millions upon millions to\n                                                                    contend for the wyrdstone in the City of the Damned.\nDoubtless one day the Skaven will be ready to emerge from\ntheir tunnels and wage open war upon mankind. For centuries\nthey have been content to feed upon his ruins, to seed plague       Skaven Warbands\nin his cities, and spread contagion amongst his lands. At least\n                                                                    The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nthey were content to wait and watch, for now everything has\n                                                                    To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\nsuddenly changed. Now the destruction of Mordheim has\n                                                                    must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\ncreated new opportunities in the secret war against mankind.\n                                                                    gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\n                                                                    be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nSince ancient times the Skaven have searched the world for the\nstones of power that men in their ignorance call wyrdstone but\n                                                                    WARBAND COMPOSITION\nwhich Skaven have long since known as warpstone, blackstone,\n                                                                    An Undead warband must follow these rules when it is created,\nor seerstone. It was as a result of gnawing upon this magic\n                                                                    and when new warriors are added to the warband.\nstone in ages past that commonplace rats began the slow\nprocess of mutation that spawned the Skaven race. Wyrdstone\n                                                                        •    There must be one leader (Assassin Adept) chosen\nis quite literally in their blood, for they feed upon it and make\n                                                                             when the warband is first founded (if the leader is\nuse of it in their foul sorceries. Until now the ratmen’s search\n                                                                             killed see below)\nfor wyrdstone has been difficult and time-consuming as the\nstone has grown increasingly rare, but now a new and                    •    There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nabundant source has appeared – a dark blessing from the skies!               for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\n                                                                             example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\n                                                                             to four champions.\nFor the Skaven of Clan Eshin, this is an especially opportune\ntime for such a thing to happen, for, just as the Empire is             •    The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\ndivided, so the Skaven race is divided amongst itself. Clan                  be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nfights clan the world over, each struggling for domination of                warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nthe Council of Thirteen whose masters rule the Skaven race.                  the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nMordheim’s secret is not yet revealed to all the clans, or else         •    A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\nthe City of the Damned would already be overrun with ratmen.                 weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nThe Nightmaster of Clan Eshin is keen to guard this secret, and              up the space of two weapons.\nfor this reason has not sent his multitudinous armies into              •    The maximum number of warriors is shown before\nMordheim. Instead, he has sent small warbands of Skaven                      the name. For example, 0-1 Necromancer. The\nskittering through secret tunnels into the city to gather up the             maximum number of Necromancers in a warband is\nshining stones and bring them back to the clan nests.                        1."},{"page":113,"text":"Heroes\n\n                 1 Assassin Adept                                                   Black Skaven\nCOST TO HIRE:135 Gold Crowns.                                    COST TO HIRE: 75 Gold Crowns.\nThe Nightmaster of Clan Eshin has sent the Assassin to           Black Skaven are the most powerful warriors of Clan Eshin:\ncollect precious wyrdstone. Success means many breeders,         black-furred killers trained in the martial arts of their clan. In\nwealth and a better position amongst the clan. Failure, on the   Mordheim they excel at ambushing and assassinating man-\nother hand, is best not contemplated…                            things.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT     M    WS     BS   S   T    W    I   A    LD    CL    WIL     INT\n 6     4     4    3   3   2    5   3    7     6     7      6      5     4     3    3    3    2   5    2    7     5      7      6\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nAn Assassin Adept starts with no equipment. They may             A Black Skaven starts with no equipment. They may purchase\npurchase Close Combat Weapons, Special Weapons, Missile          Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Special Weapons,\nWeapons, Armour, and Wargear from the Skaven Equipment           Armour, and Wargear from the Skaven Equipment List.\nList.\n                                                                 SPECIAL RULES:\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   Race (Skaven), Champion, Scurry Away! Strength in numbers\nRace (Skaven), Leader, Scurry Away! Strength in numbers\n                                                                 STARTING SKILL:\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                  When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their         Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does     not increase the warrior’s credit value.\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.\n                                                                                    Night Runners\n           0~1 Apprentice Greyseer\n                                                                 COST TO HIRE: 15 Gold Crowns.\nCOST TO HIRE: 50 Gold Crowns.                                    Night Runners are the young apprentices of Clan Eshin.\nAll potential Grey Seers are found at birth and sent to          Recently initiated into the secrets of the clan, they make up\nSkavenblight for training. Here, the survivors will become       for their lack of knowledge with their ambition and energy.\nGrey Seer Apprentices. After a period of tutelage, they are      The strongest amongst them are initiated into the secrets of\noften sent alone or with groups of agents to perform minor       the clan and begin their training to become Assassins. All the\nduties. Such things include raids, advising, and aiding in       Skaven of Clan Eshin dream of rising to the status of an\nrituals or rights.                                               Assassin one day.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT     M    WS     BS   S   T    W    I   A    LD    CL    WIL     INT\n 5     3     3    3   3   2    4   1    6     6     8      7      5     2     2    3    3    1   4    1    5     4      6      5\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nAn Apprentice Greyseer starts with no equipment. They may        A Night Runner starts with no equipment. They may\npurchase Greyseer Weapons and Wargear from the Skaven            purchase Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons,\nEquipment List.                                                  Armour, and Wargear from the Skaven Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   SPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Skaven), Champion, Wizard (Cast Spells Magic of the        Race (Skaven), Raw Recruit, Scurry Away! Strength in\nHorned Rat), Scurry Away! Strength in numbers                    numbers\n\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value."},{"page":114,"text":"Henchmen\n                      Clan Rats\nCost to hire: 30 gold crowns\nMost Skaven are Clanrats, hailing from one of the many\ncomplex Skaven clans that constantly bicker, politic,\nbackstab, and eventually war on each other. They generally\nact on the orders of higher-status Skaven, but are always\nlooking for a way to secure a better position, most often by\nbetrayal. They usually dress in mouldering leather or filthy\ncloth, with scraps of rusty and tarnished metal serving as\nmakeshift armour. Clanrats are often sent out as scouts or\nraiders to scavenge for goods, search for warpstone, or raid\nfor slaves.\n M    WS    BS   S    T   W    I   A   LD   CL    WIL     INT\n 5     3     3   3    3   1   4    1    6    5      7      6\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Clan Rat starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nClose Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nWargear from the Skaven Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Skaven),Scurry Away! Strength in numbers\n\n\n                     0~1 Rat Ogre\nCost to hire: 120 gold crowns\nRat Ogres are hulking brutes, bred in the dark caverns of the\nUnderempire by the demented ministerings of Clan Molder’s\npackmasters. They are stupid but are fearless and unrelenting\nin combat. Rarely encountered on their own, they tend to\naccompany Grey Seers, or other ranking Skaven, serving as a\nbodyguard.\n M    WS    BS   S    T   W    I   A   LD   CL    WIL     INT\n 6     3     1   5    4   3   4    3    5    5      7      4\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nNone. Natural weapons\n\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Rat Ogre), Fear, Monster, Large Target, Stupidity"},{"page":115,"text":"Skaven Equipment List\nCLOSE COMBAT WEAPONS                                               SPECIAL WEAPONS\nITEM                              PRICE                            ITEM                                PRICE\nAxe                               20                               Blow Pipe                           25\nBillhook                          30                               Cathay Smoke Bombs                  35\nClub                              15                               Eshin Fighting Claws                50\nDagger                            10                               Tail Blade                          30\nHalberd                           25                               Throwing Stars                      15\nSpear                             15                               Warp Lock Pistol                    40\nSword                             25                               Warplock Musket                     60\n                                                                   Weeping Blades                      60\nMISSILE WEAPONS\nITEM                                PRICE\nSling                               5                              ARMOUR\n                                                                   ITEM                                PRICE\nGREYSEER WEAPONS                                                   Light Armour                        20\nITEM                                PRICE                          Shield                              20\nAxe                                 20\nClub                                15                             WARGEAR\nDagger                              10                             ITEM                                PRICE\nSword                               25                             Black Lotus                         15\nStaff                               25                             Rope And Hook                       30\nWarp Lock Pistol                    60                             Giant Rat                           15\n\n\n\n\n                                          Skaven Skill Access\nSkaven Warriors have access to the following skills:\n\n                  Agility        Brawn         Combat        Cunning        Ferocity      Leadership      Shooting     Academic\nAssassin          Primary                      Primary       Primary        Secondary     Secondary\nAdept\nApprentice                                     Secondary     Primary        Secondary     Secondary                    Primary\nGreyseer\nBlack Skaven      Secondary                    Primary       Primary        Secondary     Secondary\nNight Runner      Secondary                    Secondary     Primary\nClan Rats         Secondary                    Primary       Secondary      Primary\n\n\n\nSkaven Special Rules\nSCURRY AWAY!\nThe Skaven embody the adage ‘he who runs away lives to fight another day!”. All Skaven warriors that are Broken add+1 to the\n2D6 roll when determining the distance they run.\n\nSTRENGTH IN NUMBERS\nSkaven are not brave by nature, but do take courage from being in large packs of their own kind. When a Skaven warrior makes a\nPanic check, apply -2 to the dice result (instead of the usual -1) for each friendly Skaven warrior (not hired swords) within 3\" of\nthem that is not Broken or Seriously Injured."},{"page":116,"text":"Orcs\nWhen the comet struck Mordheim, its fiery descent shattered          particularly ruthless one might just make a fortune from the\nnot only the city, but the fragile order of the Empire. As smoke     loot they collect and the trophies they take from fallen\nand sorcery choked the skies and the noble houses tore each          enemies—many of whom end up as dinner.\nother apart, the Greenskins saw only opportunity. Like wolves\ndrawn to a dying stag, they came – bands of brutal Orcs and          But don’t expect Orcs to go scurrying around for wyrdstone\nsneaky Goblins, lured by the promise of violence, loot, and          like some pointy-eared Elf. Given the choice, they'd much\nbossin' others about.                                                rather bash another warband over the head and take their\n                                                                     stash. Their goals are brutally simple: despoil, pillage, burn,\nThese aren’t great warhosts with banners and bellowing               and leg it before anyone gets organized.\nWarbosses. No, these are fractured mobs – scavengers,\noutcasts, and ambitious upstarts. Smaller Orc warbands, driven\nby hunger for power or gold, have slunk into Mordheim's ruins        Orc Warbands\nto carve out a name for themselves. Others arrived\n                                                                     The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\naccidentally, swept up in failed Waaaghs! or chased from their\n                                                                     To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\ntribes, only to find themselves in a city where the strong\n                                                                     must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nsurvive and the rest get eaten.\n                                                                     gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\n                                                                     be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nAmong the many savage races of the Warhammer world, none\nrelish the thrill of looting and pillaging more than the Orcs and\n                                                                     WARBAND COMPOSITION\nGoblins. For the average Orc, life is a constant fight—whether\n                                                                     An Orc warband must follow these rules when it is created,\nit’s cracking skulls within their own tribe or battering some\n                                                                     and when new warriors are added to the warband.\nunfortunate foe. So when Mordheim, a city ripe with violence,\nchaos, and treasure, erupted into ruin, it was only natural that\n                                                                         •    There must be one leader (Orc Boss) chosen when the\nthe Greenskins would be drawn to it like flies to a corpse.\n                                                                              warband is first founded (if the leader is killed see\n                                                                              below)\nMordheim is a paradise of anarchy for Greenskins. The\nbuildings are half-fallen and full of shadows. There’s loot lying        •    There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\naround, enemies hiding in every alley, and the local humies are               for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\ntoo busy stabbing each other to keep order. It’s a perfect                    example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nplayground for a mob of violent thugs with no sense of self-                  to four champions.\npreservation.                                                            •    The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\n                                                                              be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nWith the Empire teetering on the edge of civil war and                        warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nlawlessness reigning in the surrounding regions, it’s all too easy            the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nfor smaller bands of Greenskins to sneak into the shattered              •    A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\ncity. Though Orcs have no real use for wyrdstone—it can’t be                  weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\neaten (tastes funny) and it doesn’t explode like a proper                     up the space of two weapons.\nweapon—they’ve discovered that plenty of others do want it.              •    The maximum number of warriors is shown before\nSkaven, Undead, even desperate humans are willing to barter                   the name. For example, 0-1 Orc Shaman. The\nand bleed for a handful of the glowing shards. A cunning Orc                  maximum number of Orc Shamans in a warband is 1.\nBoss can trade wyrdstone for weapons, grub, slaves or gold. A"},{"page":117,"text":"Orc Special Rules\nSIZE MATTERS. Orc units do not take a Panic check when a\nGoblin warrior is Seriously Wounded or goes Out of Action\nwithin 3\" of them.\nWhen testing to see if an Orc Warband needs to take a Rout\ntest, each Goblin Warrior Seriously Injured or Out of Action\nonly counts as half a warrior (rounding up).\n\nFEAR ELVES. All Goblins dislike fighting Elves of any kind.\nElves are haughty, unnatural and 'stink funny', which is more\nthan enough to unnerve such a cowardly race. Elves cause Fear\nin Goblin warriors.\n\nANIMOSITY. Orcs and goblins enjoy nothing more than a\ngood scrap, Greenskins will fight anyone, even each other!\nAt the start of the Warrior’s Activation, make an Animosity\ncheck if there is at least one other friendly warrior within 12”\nwith the Animosity special rule, that is an eligible target (not\nSeriously Injured. Broken, or Engaged).\nThere is no need to take an Animosity check if:\n     • There are visible enemy warriors within 12”.                 Animosity Table\n     • There are Hated enemy warriors visible at any                D6 Result\n          distance.                                                 1    “I ’Erd Dat!” If the warrior is in charge reach, they will\n     • Warriors engaged in close combat don't test.                      immediately charge the nearest friendly Greenskin\n     • Warriors that are Broken or Seriously Injured don't               warrior that is not engaged in close combat and fight a\n          test.                                                          round of close combat against the warrior. Their\n                                                                         opponent will make Reaction attacks as usual. At the\nTo make an Animosity check, the warrior makes a LD check                 end of this round of combat, the warriors will\nand adds +2 to the warrior’s LD. Apply the following modifiers           immediately move 1\" apart and no longer count as being\nto the 2D6 dice roll:                                                    in close combat.\n     • +1 if a friendly warrior with Animosity is in the                 If there are no friendly Greenskin warriors within\n         warrior’s visibility arc and charge distance.                   charge reach, and the warrior is armed with a missile\n     • +1 if the friendly warrior with Animosity is a Goblin             weapon and in range, he immediately performs a Shoot\n         and an Orc is testing.                                          (Basic) action at the nearest Eligible friendly Greenskin\n     • -1 enemy warriors visible.                                        warrior.\n     • -1 Leader is in 12” (or is the Leader).                           If none of the above applies, the warrior behaves as if a\n                                                                         2-5 had been rolled on this chart.\nIf LD check is passed, then nothing happens, and the warrior        2-5 “Wud Yoo Say?” The warrior makes two Move\ncan make their tun as usual. If the LD check failed, then roll on        (Simple) actions towards the nearest friendly Greenskin\nthe Animosity table below.                                               warrior, halting within 1\" or as close as possible. The\n                                                                         two warriors then exchange jeers, insults and a great\n                                                                         deal of spittle. The warrior may not perform any other\n                                                                         actions this turn.\n                                                                    6    “I’ll Show Yer!” The warrior counts as having the\n                                                                         Sprint skill for this Activation turn only. The warrior\n                                                                         must move towards the nearest visible enemy warrior,\n                                                                         charging into combat if possible. If there are no enemy\n                                                                         warriors within sight, the warrior may use Sprint skill\n                                                                         however the player wishes."},{"page":118,"text":"Heroes\n                       1 Orc boss                                                       0-1 Shaman\nCOST TO HIRE: 125 Gold Crowns.                                   COST TO HIRE: 60 Gold Crowns.\nAn Orc Boss is a brutal war-leader, feared by his Boyz and       Orc Shamans are conduits of raw Waaagh! energy---- blessed\nobeyed without question. He rules through raw strength,          or cursed by Gork and Mork with chaotic powers they barely\nsavage cunning, and sudden violence. Any challenge to his        comprehend. Their magic is violent, unpredictable, and\nauthority is settled with blood. He hurls his warband into       dangerous to friend and foe alike. Shunned by many, they\nbattle not for glory or honour, but for loot, carnage, and the   find purpose in warbands, where their madness is seen not as\nsheer joy of smashing things until they stop moving.             weakness, but as a sign of brutal divine favour.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A    LD    CL   WIL    INT     M    WS     BS    S   T   W     I   A    LD    CL    WIL     INT\n 4     4     4    3   4    2   3   3    8     8      7      5     4     3      3    3   4    2    2   1     7     8      8      6\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nAn Orc Boss starts with no equipment. They may purchase          A Shaman starts with no equipment. They may purchase Orc\nClose Combat Weapons, Special Weapons, Missile Weapons,          Shaman Weapons and Wargear from the Orc Equipment\nArmour, and Wargear from the Orc Equipment List.                 List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   SPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Orc), Leader, Animosity, Size Matters                      Race (Orc), Champion, Wizard (Power of da Waaargh!),\n                                                                 Animosity, Size Matters\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their         STARTING SKILL:\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does     When recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.                         Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\n                                                                 not increase the warrior’s credit value.\n\n\n                                                                                            Big uns\n                                                                 COST TO HIRE: 85 Gold Crowns.\n                                                                 In Orc society, strength decides all. Big ’Uns are hardened\n                                                                 killers, second only to the Boss. If he falls, they don’t argue----\n                                                                 they fight. No words, no plans---- just fists, blades, and blood.\n                                                                 The last one standing leads. It’s not about honour or loyalty.\n                                                                 It’s about who’s meanest, toughest, and still breathing.\n                                                                  M    WS     BS    S   T   W     I   A    LD    CL    WIL     INT\n                                                                  4     4      3    3   4    2    3   2     8     7      7      5\n\n\n                                                                 WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n                                                                 An Orc Big Un starts with no equipment. They may purchase\n                                                                 Close Combat Weapons, Special Weapons, Missile Weapons,\n                                                                 Armour, and Wargear from the Orc Equipment List.\n\n                                                                 SPECIAL RULES:\n                                                                 Race (Orc), Champion, Animosity, Size Matters\n\n                                                                 STARTING SKILL:\n                                                                 When recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their\n                                                                 Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\n                                                                 not increase the warrior’s credit value."},{"page":119,"text":"0-2 Nasty skulkers                                                        Orc yoofs\nCOST TO HIRE: 55 Gold Crowns.                                    COST TO HIRE: 25 Gold Crowns.\nIn Mordheim’s choking gloom, Goblins are more than mere          Orc Yoofs are young, reckless brutes desperate to prove\nvermin---- they are predators cloaked in cowardice. They creep   themselves in the blood-soaked ruins of Mordheim. Hungry\nthrough rubble and ruin, slipping knives between ribs and        for glory and violence, they hurl themselves into battle with\nvanishing before the body falls. Treacherous by nature, they     wild enthusiasm, eager to earn scars and the respect of their\nexcel in ambush, sabotage, and cruel cunning. Orc Bosses         elders. Too dumb to fear death and too impatient to wait,\nsend them ahead not from trust, but necessity. In the city's     they charge headlong into the fray, driven by instinct, fury,\nfestering dark, it's the sly, the spiteful, and the small who    and the thrill of breaking skulls in a world already broken.\nstrike first---- and survive longest..                            M    WS    BS    S   T    W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT     4     2     2    3   4    1   2   1    6     6     6      4\n 4     3     4    3   3   2    4   2    6     5     5      5\n                                                                 WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           An Orc Yoof starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nA Nasty Skulker starts with no equipment. They may               Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\npurchase Close Combat Weapons, Goblin Weapons, Armour,           Wargear from the Orc Equipment List.\nand Wargear from the Orc Equipment List.\n                                                                 SPECIAL RULES:\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   Race (Orc), Raw Recruit, Animosity, Size Matters\nRace (Goblin), Champion, Animosity, Size Matters\n                                                                 STARTING SKILL:\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                  When recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their         Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does     not increase the warrior’s credit value.\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value."},{"page":120,"text":"Henchmen\n                          Orc boyz                                                     0-1 Troll\nCOST TO HIRE: 35 Gold Crowns.                                    COST TO HIRE: 120 Gold Crowns.\nOrc Boyz are savage and tough. They fear nothing that they       Trolls often latch on to Greenskin warbands, attracted by the\ncan get their bare hands on, though they are even more           rotten carcasses, bones and refuse on which they feast. Orcs\nignorant and superstitious than most other beings in the         may even try to encourage them by tossing them the odd\nWarhammer world. They form the core of any Orc warband.          Snotling.\nOrcs that use bows are known as Arrer Boyz. These are             M    WS    BS   S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL   WIL       INT\nviewed suspiciously by other Orcs, for archery is a bit           6     3     1   5   4    3   1   3    4     6     6        4\n'Gobliny'. As Arrer Boyz can prove their prowess in combat,\nsuch oddities can often be overlooked.                           WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\n M    WS    BS   S   T     W   I   A   LD    CL   WIL     INT    None. Natural weapons.\n 4     3     3   3    4    1   2   1    7     7     7      5\n                                                                 SPECIAL RULES:\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           Race (Troll), Fear, Large Target, Monster, Regeneration,\nAn Orc Boy starts with no equipment. They may purchase           Stupidity, Troll Vomit\nClose Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nWargear from the Orc Equipment List.                             TROLL VOMIT Instead of his normal attacks, a Troll can\n                                                                 regurgitate its highly corrosive digestive juices on an\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   unfortunate opponent. If the warrior is Standing and\nRace (Orc), Henchmen, Animosity, Size Matters                    Engaged, they can perform the action:\n                                                                 REGURGITATE (Basic) – The warrior makes a single attack\n                                                                 that automatically hits, Strength 5, D3 Damage with no\n                  Goblin warriors                                armour saves allowed. This action can only be performed\n                                                                 once per battle.\nCOST TO HIRE: 20 Gold Crowns.\nGoblins tend to be quite a cruel, sneaky, cowardly, and          In addition to the rules above, some types of Trolls have\nuntrustworthy lot who like to attack with superiors numbers      unique aspects and gain additional special rules. When\nand, if possible, from a distance. They steal or loot anything   purchasing a Troll, the player may choose to pay an\nthey can from anyone and destroy anything they can't carry       additional amount for one of the following:\njust for the fun of it.                                                 RIVER TROLL: (+30 Gold Crowns)\n M    WS    BS   S   T     W   I   A   LD    CL   WIL     INT           -River Strider: The warrior moves through water\n 4     2     3   3    3    1   3   1    5     5     5      5            terrain features with no move penalty.\n                                                                        -Stench: Warriors Engaged with the Troll suffer -1 to\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                                  hit.\nA Goblin warrior starts with no equipment. They may                     STONE TROLL: (+40 Gold Crowns)\npurchase Goblin Weapons, Armour, and Wargear from the                   -Magic Resistance (6+).\nOrc Equipment List.                                                     -Scaly Skin (armour save 5+).\n\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Goblin), Henchmen, Animosity, Size Matters, Fear\nElves\n\n\n\n\nThe only good Humie is a dead Humie. The only thing\nbetter ‘n a dead Humie iz a dyin’ Humie who tells yer\nwhere ter find ‘is mates."},{"page":121,"text":"Orc Equipment List\nCLOSE COMBAT WEAPONS                                               WARGEAR\nITEM                                 PRICE                         ITEM                                  PRICE\nAxe                                  20                            Mad Cap Mushrooms                     35\nClub                                 15                            Lantern                               40\nDagger                               10                            Rope And Hook                         30\nGreat Axe                            55\nGreat Hammer                         50                            SHAMAN WEAPONS\nGreat Sword                          45                            ITEM                                  PRICE\nHammer Or Mace                       20                            Axe                                   15\nSpear                                15                            Club                                  15\nSword                                20                            Dagger                                10\n                                                                   Hammer or Mace                        20\nGOBLIN WEAPONS                                                     Staff                                 25\nITEM                                 PRICE                         Sword                                 25\nShort bow                            10\nNet                                  15\nSpider Spittle                       40\n                                                                   “Ere now! Wot do you think you’re doin?”\nMISSILE WEAPONS                                                    “Nuffink, boss. Just having a bit of lunch is all.”\nITEM                                 PRICE                         “don’t give me that. Yer up to sumfink…” Looks around.\nBow                                  15                            “Where’s Ratgash? You ‘aven’t et ‘im, ‘ave ya?”\n                                                                   Shocked silence. “Et Ratgash? That’s disgustin’, boss! ‘E’s one of\nSPECIAL WEAPONS                                                    us Boyz!”\nITEM                                 PRICE                         Another Orc pipes up “And besides, ‘e’s all grease and fat, ‘im!\nBottle of Rotgut                     15                            Give us all inna… innagestion, ‘e would!”\nCrossbow                             30                            “Then ‘oo’s this then? And none of yer lies or I’ll give you\nFlail                                35                            sumfink a whole lot worse than innagestion!”\nHeavy Armour                         50                            “Er, Gutbag, boss. One of Maggot’s lot. But ‘e was dead when\nMorning Star                         30                            we found ‘im.”\nOrc Choppa                           25                            Pause. “Course ‘e claimed ‘e was just sleepin’ – but all that lot is\n                                                                   liars ain’t they?” The Orc Boyz nod vigorously.\nARMOUR                                                             “Well, that’s all right then. Carry on. And you’ll save me a leg if\nITEM                                 PRICE                         you know wot’s good for you!”\nLight Armour                         20\nShield                               20\n\n\n\n\n                                                    Orc skill access\nOrc Warriors have access to the following skills:\n\n                Agility    Brawn        Combat       Cunning   Ferocity    Leadership   Shooting    Academic     Resilience   Savagery\nOrc Boss                   Primary                             Secondary   Secondary                             Primary      Primary\nShaman                     Primary                             Secondary   Primary                  Secondary    Secondary\nBig Uns                    Primary                             Secondary   Secondary                             Secondary    Primary\nOrc Yoofs                  Primary                             Secondary                                         Secondary\nNasty Skulker   Primary                 Secondary    Primary   Secondary                Secondary\nOrc boyz                   Primary                             Secondary                                         Primary      Secondary\nGoblin          Primary                 Secondary    Primary                            Secondary\nWarriors"},{"page":122,"text":"Dwarf Clansmen\nMordheim was once home to many Dwarf tradesmen,                    each passing day, their thirst for revenge consuming thought\ncraftsmen, merchants, and stonemasons. Not only did the            and reason. Their desire for gold—always a powerful instinct—\nDwarfs supply stone from their mountain quarries, but they         twisted into greed for wyrdstone and the wealth and vengeance\nalso lent their expertise to the city's very foundations—helping   it could bring. They began to see enemies everywhere: those\ndesign its canals, fortifications, and even the intricate sewer    who might steal from them, who stood in the way of their\nsystems beneath its streets. As a result, Mordheim enjoyed         honour, or dared to claim what rightfully belonged to their\nprosperous and long-standing trade relations with the nearby       people. It wasn’t just goldlust—it was possessiveness.\nDwarfholds.                                                        Wyrdstone came to represent what was stolen, what was owed,\nWhen disaster struck and the city was destroyed, word of the       and what could never be restored. Those who tried to take it\ncalamity spread swiftly to the Dwarf settlements. Many among       became enemies.\nthem had kin in the city, and the question that burned in every    And so, the Dwarfs endure in the ruins of Mordheim. Once\nhearth-hall was the same: What had become of their brethren?       they came seeking the fallen. Now they fight for vengeance,\nFor Dwarfs are a people bound by blood and honour, and few         gold, and pride—unwilling or unable to leave the city that has\nties run deeper than those of clan and family.                     already claimed so much from them.\nThe Dwarf Lords, ever wary of entanglement in human affairs,\nrefused to dispatch official aid. Yet many granted their Thanes\nleave to muster and equip small bands of warriors and kin to       Dwarf Warbands\njourney into the ruins in search of survivors.\n                                                                   The following list is used to recruit and equip your warband.\nBut when the warbands reached Mordheim, they found the\n                                                                   To start with you have 1000 gold crowns (GCs) with which you\ndevastation far worse than imagined. Their noble task swiftly\n                                                                   must recruit at least three warriors including a leader. Any\nshifted—from rescue to remembrance. The ruined streets and\n                                                                   gold crowns unspent are added to the warband’s stash and can\nshattered dwellings became tombs, and their grim duty was\n                                                                   be used later or hoarded to buy something more expensive.\nnow to recover the remains of their fallen, so their souls might\nrest in the halls of their ancestors.\n                                                                   WARBAND COMPOSITION\nAmong the human shantytowns clinging to the city’s outskirts,\n                                                                   The warband must follow these rules when it is created, and\nthey found Dwarfs who had survived—shattered in spirit,\n                                                                   when new warriors are added to the warband.\nhaunted by grief. Some had even taken the Slayer’s oath,\nchoosing a life of doom to atone for surviving when others had\n                                                                       •   There must be one leader (Thane) chosen when the\nperished. Others were stonemasons, brewers, traders, and\n                                                                           warband is first founded (if the leader is killed see\nminers who had worked in the surrounding lands. Many of\n                                                                           below)\nthese Dwarfs, still searching for their own lost kin, chose to\nband together under Dwarf Thanes, rather than entrust their            •   There can be no more than two Champions, plus one\nfates to fickle and untrustworthy humans.                                  for every full 10 Reputation the warband has – for\nOver time, their reasons for staying in Mordheim began to                  example a warband with Reputation 24 could have up\nshift. Some remained to avenge the deaths of loved ones.                   to four champions.\nOthers continued the search for lost heirlooms and sacred              •   The total number of Henchmen in the warband must\nrelics of their clans. A few still clung to the faint hope of              be equal to or higher than the total number of other\nfinding friends or family alive in the ruins. And more than a              warriors (Leaders, Raw Recruits and Champions) in\nfew Thanes, ever pragmatic, began to see opportunity in the                the warband, not counting Hangers-on.\nchaos—selling scavenged wyrdstone to desperate human                   •   A warrior can be equipped with a maximum of three\nsmugglers for a high price.                                                weapons. Weapons with the Two-Handed Trait take\nThe Dwarfs thought themselves immune to corrupting power                   up the space of two weapons.\nof the wyrdstone. Other races such as short-lived men and              •   Some warrior types have a maximum amount which\nsybaritic Elves might fall under its sway, but not them. As with           is shown before the name. For example, 0-1 Engineer.\nso much else that gave Dwarfs pride, their seeming immunity                The maximum number of Engineers in a warband is\nplayed them false. The longer they remained in Mordheim, the               therefore 1.\nmore they changed. Their books of grudges grew heavier with"},{"page":123,"text":"Dwarf skill access\nDwarf Clansmen have access to the following skills:\n             Agility     Brawn          Combat          Cunning      Ferocity      Leadership    Shooting     Academic     Resilience\nThane                    Secondary Secondary                         Primary       Primary                                 Primary\nEngineer                                                             Secondary     Secondary     Primary      Primary      Secondary\nLongbeards               Secondary Secondary                         Primary       Secondary                               Primary\nBeardlings                              Secondary                    Primary                                               Secondary\nClansman                 Secondary Secondary                         Primary                                               Primary\nThunderers                                              Secondary    Secondary                   Primary                   Primary\n\n\nDwarf Special Rules\nRACE (DWARF)\nAll Dwarfs have the following special rules:\n     • ANCESTRAL GRUDGE: All Dwarfs hate all Orcs and Goblins. See the psychology section of the Mordheim rules for\n        details on the effects of hatred.\n     • ELF GRUDGE: A Dwarf warband may never include any kind of Elf Hired Sword or Dramatis Personae.\n     • BURLY: Dwarfs never suffer any movement penalties for wearing armour (e.g. Encumbrance).\n     • EXPERT MINERS: When checking for wyrdstone in the Post Battle, add +1 to the number of pieces found.\n     • MAGIC RESISTANCE (6) All Dwarfs have a natural resistance to magic. Magic spells will not affect a Dwarf on a D6 roll\n        of 6+. The spell isn’t dispelled and may still affect other warriors nearby. Note, that if the Dwarfs are fighting alongside a\n        Wizard or Priest (either in the same warband, or as part of an allied force) for whatever reason, this bonus is lost — the\n        spell caster’s presence disrupts the Dwarfs’ resistance.\n\nBALLISTICS EXPERT\nWhen this warrior makes an Aim (Basic) action, make an Intelligence check for them. If the check is passed, they gain an\nadditional +1 modifier to their hit roll.\n\nGUNSMITH\nWhenever a Blackpowder weapon rolls a Misfire, and requires an Intelligence check, a warrior from their warband within 6” can\nuse this warrior’s Intelligence characteristic instead of their own."},{"page":124,"text":"Heroes\n\n                           1 Thane                                                     0~1 Engineer\nCOST TO HIRE: 135 Gold Crowns.                                   COST TO HIRE: 115 Gold Crowns.\nDwarf Thanes are stoic clan leaders drawn to Mordheim by         In the wreckage of Mordheim, Dwarf Engineers cling to their\nduty and blood. Once seekers of lost kin and relics, they now    sacred duty: maintaining the warband’s blackpowder\nbattle through ruin and corruption—driven by honour,             weapons. Every rifle cleaned, every bomb primed, is a ritual\nvengeance, and a growing hunger for the wyrdstone that has       against chaos. They mutter curses at flawed craftsmanship,\ntwisted their purpose and bound them to the city.                their hands black with soot and spite. In battle, they unleash\n M    WS    BS   S    T     W   I   A   LD   CL   WIL     INT    iron vengeance—precise gunfire and brutal detonations.\n 3     5     4   3     4    2   3   3   10   10     9      7     Their weapons are not mere tools, but sacred instruments of\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                           wrath, built to endure. Amid ash and ruin, the Engineer\nA Than starts with no equipment. They may purchase Close         ensures that failure dies before honour ever does.\nCombat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Special Weapons,                 M    WS    BS    S    T   W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\nArmour, and Wargear from the Dwarf Clansman Equipment             3     4     4    4    4   2   3   2    9     9     9       8\nList.\n                                                                 WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   A Beardling starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nRace (Dwarf), Leader                                             Close Combat Weapons, Engineer Weapons, Armour, and\n                                                                 Wargear from the Dwarf Clansman Equipment List.\nSTARTING SKILL:\nWhen recruited, a Leader may choose one skill from their         SPECIAL RULES:\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does     Race (Dwarf), Champion, Ballistics Expert, Gunsmith\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value.\n                                                                 STARTING SKILL:\n                      Longbeards                                 When recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their\n                                                                 Primary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nCOST TO HIRE: 120 Gold Crowns.                                   not increase the warrior’s credit value.\nLongbeards are ancient warriors forged by centuries of battle,\nloss, and unyielding duty. In the ruins of Mordheim, they                              Beardlings\nmarch not for glory, but to honour oaths and bury grief\nbeneath steel. Their presence is heavy with memory; every        COST TO HIRE: 30 Gold Crowns.\nblow struck is penance, every command weighted with              Fresh-faced and eager, young Dwarfs follow their Thane into\nsorrow. They are the spine of the warband—stoic, bitter, and     Mordheim, chasing whispers of lost kin and glittering riches.\nbound to a world that no longer remembers what they’ve lost.     They do not yet grasp the weight of grief or the city’s hunger.\n M    WS    BS    S    T    W   I   A   LD   CL    WIL    INT    Mordheim teaches quickly. Dreams turn to silence, courage\n 3     5     3    3    4    2   3   2   10    9     9      7     to ashes. In time, even hope is buried beneath the stones.\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:                                            M    WS    BS    S    T   W   I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\nA Longbeard starts with no equipment. They may purchase           3     3     2    3    4   1   2   1    8     8     8       6\nClose Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Special Weapons,          WEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nArmour, and Wargear from the Dwarf Clansman Equipment            A Beardling starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nList.                                                            Close Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nSPECIAL RULES:                                                   Wargear from the Dwarf Clansman Equipment List.\nRace (Dwarf), Champion, Stubborn\nSTARTING SKILL:                                                  SPECIAL RULES:\nWhen recruited, a Champion may choose one skill from their       Race (Dwarf), Raw Recruit.\nPrimary skill sets. This skill does not cost any XP and does\nnot increase the warrior’s credit value."},{"page":125,"text":"Henchmen\n\n                      Clansmen\nCOST TO HIRE: 45 Gold Crowns\nThese are hardened Dwarf warriors—stoic, scarred, and\nunflinching. Veterans of countless battles, they are miners\nturned shieldbearers, brewers turned killers, tradesmen with\nbloodied hands. Forged by loss and purpose, they fight not\nfor glory, but for honour, vengeance, and what little can be\nsalvaged. In the Thane’s service, they hold the line with axe,\nhammer, and fire, unyielding amid the ruin, for they know\nskill is all that stands between survival and death.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\n 3     4     3    3   4   1    2   1    9     9     9      7\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Clansmen starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nClose Combat Weapons, Missile Weapons, Armour, and\nWargear from the Dwarf Clansman Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Dwarf), Henchmen\n\n\n                 0~5 Thunderers\nCOST TO HIRE: 45 Gold Crowns\nThunderers are masters of blackpowder—silent, watchful,\nand precise. Their handguns, forged by the Engineers’ Guild,\nare heirlooms of destruction: each one crafted with the care of\na thousand hammers. In Mordheim, they do not shout or\ncurse like men. They take position, adjust for wind and\ndistance, and wait. When the time comes, they fire once. That\nis enough. Smoke drifts. The enemy falls. There is no\ntriumph—only duty, and the silence that follows.\n M    WS    BS    S   T   W    I   A   LD    CL    WIL    INT\n 3     4     3    3   4   1    2   1    9     9     9      7\n\n\nWEAPONS AND EQUIPMENT:\nA Thunderer starts with no equipment. They may purchase\nClose Combat Weapons, Thunderer Weapons, Armour, and\nWargear from the Dwarf Clansman Equipment List.\n\nSPECIAL RULES:\nRace (Dwarf), Henchmen"},{"page":126,"text":"Dwarf Clansman Equipment List\nCLOSE COMBAT WEAPONS           MISSILE WEAPONS\nITEM                   PRICE   ITEM                   PRICE\nAxe                    15      Crossbow               30\nClub                   15\nDagger                 10      SPECIAL WEAPONS\nGreat Axe              50      ITEM                   PRICE\nGreat Hammer           50      Dwarf Crossbow         35\nGreat Sword            40      Dwarf Handgun          55\nHammer Or Mace         20      Dwarf Pistol           35\nPickaxe                35      Gromril Axe            35\nSpear                  15      Gromril Plate Armour   120\nSword                  25      Throwing Axes          15\n\nTHUNDERER WEAPONS              ARMOUR\nITEM                   PRICE   ITEM                   PRICE\nBlunderbuss            25      Light Armour           20\nHandgun                40      Heavy Armour           50\nPistol                 20      Shield                 20\n\nENGINEER WEAPONS               WARGEAR\nITEM                   PRICE   ITEM                   PRICE\nBomb                   25      Lantern                40\nDwarf Handgun          55      Rope And Hook          30\nDwarf Pistol           35"},{"page":127,"text":"Founding warbands\nBefore the campaign begins, each player must found a                ADVANCEMENTS\nwarband.                                                            The more Advancements a warrior has, the more expensive\n                                                                    any future Advancements will be. Leaders and Champions\nSTARTING GOLD CROWNS                                                start with one Advancement (a skill), which should be noted\nA warband has a starting budget of 1,000 gold crowns, and           on the warband roster.\nmust be created using any of the lists mentioned previously.\nThis budget can be spent on warriors (following the                 IN RECOVERY AND CAPTURED BY\nrestrictions in each Warband List) and equipment from that          When a warrior goes Out of Action, there is a chance that they\nwarband's Equipment List; any gold crowns that are not spent        will suffer a Lasting Injury. Many of these will cause them to go\nare added to the warband's Stash and stored away for later use.     Into Recovery and miss the next battle. When this is the case,\nA Warrior card must be completed for each warrior in the            their In Recovery-box is ticked. Similarly, warriors might be\nwarband, and a warband roster must be completed to record           Captured by an enemy warband – while this is the case, a note\nall of the warband's details.                                       is made in the Lasting Injury/Captured By box of the name of\n                                                                    the warband that has Captured them.\nWARBAND ATTRIBUTES\nIn a Campaign, warbands have a number of attributes, which          COMPLETING A WARBAND ROSTER\nare tracked on their roster. These attributes, and their starting   As well as filling in a Warrior card for each warrior in their\nvalues, are explained below:                                        warband, players will need to complete a warband roster. This\n                                                                    tracks additional Dominion Campaign related information,\nWARBAND RATING                                                      such as Territories held, Warband Rating, Reputation, Wealth\nThe Warband Rating is an indicator of how powerful the              and so on, as well as each warrior’s Experience and\nWarband is – the proficiency of its warriors, how well              Advancements.\nequipped it is, and so on. The Warband Rating is the total cost     The warband roster is made up of a number of elements: the\nof all of the warriors in the warband, including the cost of all    warband's name and Warband Type, its Warband Rating,\nalternative weapon sets a warrior has.                              Reputation and Wealth, the Territories it holds and its Stash,\n                                                                    containing. unspent gold crowns, surplus equipment (both\nREPUTATION                                                          weapons and Wargear), and so on. It also has a line for each\nReputation is the measure of a warband's standing and power         warrior in the warband, with space for their names, warrior\nin their area. It is separate from Warband Rating, which is a       type, Cost, Experience earned, the number of Advancements\nmeasure of the warband’s size and resources; a small warband        gained, and whether they are currently In Recovery or have\ncan build up quite an impressive reputation. A warband’s            suffered any injuries or been Captured.\nReputation starts at 1, and cannot drop below 1.\n                                                                    Note that although the number of rows is limited, there is no\n                                                                    upper limit on the number of warriors a warband can contain.\nWARRIOR CAMPAIGN ATTRIBUTES\n                                                                    Should a warband be lucky enough to have more warriors than\nIn a Campaign, each warrior in a warband has a number of\n                                                                    can be fitted onto one warband roster, simply use a second\nattributes that are track in their entry on the warband's roster:\n                                                                    warband roster for extra space.\n\nEXPERIENCE (XP)\nWarriors can spend Experience in order to purchase\nAdvancements – when they do so, the Experience total is\nreduced accordingly."},{"page":128,"text":"Gaining Experience\nDuring a game, a warrior can gain Experience in a number of ways. The standard ways in which Experience is gained are detailed\nhere. Experience is also gained by completing scenario objectives – these will be detailed in the scenario.\n\nACTION                                                                                                             XP GAINED\nAny action that directly caused an enemy warrior to go out of action *                                             D3\nIf the model taken out of action is a Leader or Champion (in addition to the first row)                            +1D3\nIf the model taken out of action is Dramatis Personae (in addition to the first row)                               +1D3\nA warrior Rallies and returns to the fight                                                                         D3\n\n* This could be a ranged or close combat attack, a Coup de Grace against a seriously injured warrior, or anything else, so long as\nthe enemy is taken Out of Action by the action itself and not later on in the game as the result of something else (for example if an\nattack leaves a warrior Seriously Injured and they later go Out of Action in the End phase), no Experience is gained. If an action\ncauses multiple enemies to be taken Out of Action – for example, if a warrior throws a bomb that takes out two enemies –\nExperience is gained for each.\n\n\nAdvance Rolls\nAt the start of a battle, during the pre-battle sequence, each player has the chance to purchase Advancements for their Leaders,\nChampions, Raw Recruit, and Veterans and any eligible Henchmen by spending Experience (XP) accrued. The XP cost of these\nAdvancements is shown in the table below. The warrior's card is updated accordingly with the Advancement taken, the warrior's\nXP is reduced by the amount spent to purchase the Advancement, the warrior’s total number of Advancements is increased by one\n(on the warband roster) and the warrior’s Gold Crown value is adjusted by the amount shown, which will in turn increase the\nWarband Rating.\nThe more experienced a warrior is, the more certain Advancements cost to purchase in terms of XP. The cost of each characteristic\nAdvancements of the same type taken is increased by 2 for each instance after the first. For example, a Champion may increase\ntheir Initiative by 1 for 5XP, but to increase it by 1 a second time will cost them 7XP.\nRaw Recruits however are particularly fast learners, and as result they suffer no such penalty on characteristic increases; they may\nincrease a characteristic any number of times (up to the Maximum Characteristics- see below) for the basic XP cost shown each\ntime.\n\nCost      Advancement – Leaders, Champions, Juves & Veterans                                                            Credits\n                                                                                                                        Increase\n3 XP      Improve the warrior's Willpower or Intelligence characteristic by 1.                                          +5 credits\n4 XP      Improve the warrior's Leadership or Cool characteristic by 1.                                                 +10 credits\n5 XP      Improve the warrior's Initiative characteristic by 1.                                                         +10 credits\n5 XP      Add 1'' to the warrior's Movement characteristic.                                                             +10 credits\n6 XP      Improve the warrior's Weapon Skill or Ballistic Skill characteristic by 1.                                    +20 credits\n6 XP      The warrior gains a random skill from one of their Primary skill sets.                                        +20 credits\n8 XP      Increase the warrior's Strength or Toughness characteristic by 1.                                             +30 credits\n9 XP      Pick a skill from one of the warrior's Primary skill sets.                                                    +20 credits\n9 XP      The warrior gains a random skill from one of their Secondary skill sets.                                      +35 credits\n12 XP     Increase the warrior's Wounds or Attacks characteristic by 1.                                                 +45 credits\n12 XP     Veterans only: Promote the warrior to Champion. They gain a random skill from one of their Primary            +40 credits\n          skill sets.\n15 XP     The warrior gains a random skill from ANY skill set.                                                          +50 credits"},{"page":129,"text":"Henchmen\nWhile Leaders, Champions and Raw Recruits are central to a warband’s narrative, Henchmen are its ‘supporting cast’. As such,\nthey spend Experience and gain Advancements in a simplified manner. If during the pre-battle sequence, a Henchmen has gained\n6 XP, the controlling player rolls 2D6 on the table below, updates the Henchmen’s Warrior card and their Gold Crowns value\naccordingly, and reduces their XP by 6. If the dice roll indicates an increase in a characteristic which has already been increased to\nits Maximum Characteristic, roll again until an appropriate characteristic is rolled.\n\n  2D6       Advancement – Henchmen (not including Veterans)                                                      Cost\n   2        The warrior becomes a Veteran.                                                                       0\n  3-4       Increase the warrior's Strength characteristic by 1.                                                 +30 gold crowns\n  5-6       Either add 1'' to the warrior's Movement characteristic, or increase their Initiative                +10 gold crowns\n            characteristic by 1\n    7       Improve the warrior's Weapon Skill or Ballistic Skill characteristic by 1.                           +20 gold crowns\n   8-9      Improve the warrior's Leadership or Cool characteristic by 1.                                        +10 gold crowns\n   10       Improve the warrior's Willpower or Intelligence characteristic by 1.                                 +5 gold crowns\n   11       Increase the warrior's Attack characteristic by 1.                                                   +45 gold crowns\n   12       The warrior becomes a Veteran.                                                                       0\n\nEditor’s note: You may want to halve the cost of gold crowns for both Advancement tables. If you do then for each subsequent\nadvancement for fighters other than those with the Fast Learners special rule, also add +10 credits to the credits increase as well as\nit being 2XP more expensive each time.\n\nVETERANS\nOne of the results on the table allows a Henchmen to become a Veteran. They are still a Henchmen for all rules purposes (for\nexample, which equipment they can carry), but they now spend Experience and gain Advancements in the same way as a Leader,\nChampion or Raw Recruit. Veterans have their own skill access as shown in their Warband List.\n\n\nMaximum characteristics\nCharacteristics for certain warriors may not be increased beyond the maximum limits shown on the following profiles. Each of a\nwarrior's characteristics has a maximum value.\nThe method for working out maximum characteristics, is to take the Base Profile for that race, then apply the following modifiers:\nM, S, T +1\nWS, BS, I, A +3\nW, LD, CL, WIL, INT +2\nSome creatures such as monsters never need to gain Ballistic Skill as they never use missile weapons.\n\n   Profile           M        WS          BS       S       T       W        I       A       LD         CL         WIL          INT\n  Beastman           5         7           6       4       5       3        6       4        9          9          8             8\n   Dwarf             4         7           6       4       5       3        5       4       10         10         10             9\n     Elf             6         7           7       4       4       3        9       4       10         10         10            10\n   Ghoul             5         6           2       4       5       3        6       4        8          7          8             7\n   Goblin            5         5           5       4       4       3        6       4        7          7          7             7\nGrave Guard          5         5           5       4       4       3        5       3        7          7          7             7\n   Halfling          4         5           7       3       3       3        8       4        8          8         10             9\n   Human             5         6           6       4       4       3        6       4        9          9          9             9\n    Ogre             7         6           5       5       5       5        6       5        9          7          9             6\n     Orc             5         6           6       4       5       3        5       4        9          9          9             7\n  Rat Ogre           7         6           1       6       5       5        7       6        7          7          9             6\n   Skaven            6         6           6       4       4       3        7       4        8          7          9             8\nThe Possessed        6         7           1       6       6       5        6       5        9          9         10             8\n    Troll            7         3           1       6       5       5        4       6        6          8          8             6\n  Vampire            6         8           5       6       6       4        9       5       10          9          9             9"},{"page":130,"text":"SKILLS\nSkills can be obtained by Leader, Champions, and Raw Recruits (as well as Henchmen who have become Veterans). The skills that\nare available are divided into eight sets: Agility, Brawn, Combat, Cunning, Ferocity, Leadership, Academic and Shooting.\n\nEach Warband Type fights in its own way, and this is reflected by the skill sets that are available to them. A warrior has different\nlevels of skill access depending upon their Warband Type and their type; for example, Goliath Champions can gain Brawn skills\nmore easily than Escher Raw Recruits. In each Warband Type list, and for certain other types of warrior (Animals and Brutes for\nexample) there is a section showing the skill sets available to those warriors. Warriors have Primary access to some skill sets, and\nSecondary access to others. Certain warriors can access skills from other sets, but to do so is more expensive in term of XP.\n\nRegardless of Warband Type, all Leaders and Champions have access to the Leadership skill set. This is treated as a Primary skill\nset for the Leaders and a Secondary skill set for Champions.\n\nGAINING A SKILL\nWhen a warrior gains a new skill, it will either be chosen or determined randomly depending upon how much XP has been spent\nto gain the skill on if the skill is Primary, Secondary or neither. Choosing a skill is simply a case of picking a skill from the sets\navailable that is desirable for the warrior. To determine a random skill, the player declares which set they are generating the skill\nfrom, and rolls a D6 on the table below (re-rolling if the warrior already has that skills).\n\n\n\nD6     AGILITY                         BRAWN                   COMBAT                   CUNNING                    FEROCITY\n1      Catfall                         Bull Charge             Combat Master            Backstab                   Berserk Charge\n2      Scale Sheer Surface             Strongman               Counter-Attack           Flee!                      Impetuous\n3      Dodge                           Crushing Blow           Disarm                   Evade                      Rightegous Fury\n4      Mighty Leap                     Headbutt                Parry                    Infiltrate                 Nerves of Steel\n5      Reaction Strike                 Hurl                    Step Aside               Lie Low                    True Grit\n6      Sprint                          Iron Jaw                Rain of Blows            Stalker                    Very Resilient\n\nD6     LEADERSHIP                      RESILIENCE              SAVAGERY                 ACADEMIC                   SHOOTING\n1      Commanding Presence             Fists Of Steel          Implacable               Identify Weakness          Fast Shot\n2      Inspirational                   Tenacious               Bloodlust                Streetwise                 Pistoleer\n3      Iron Will                       Shield wall             Crimson Haze             Trader                     Nimble\n4      Mentor                          Relentless              Ferocious Assault        Healer                     Marksman\n5      Overseer                        Beat Back               Killing Blow             Wyrdstone Hunter           Precision Shot\n6      Regroup                         Walk It Off             Momentum                 Haggle                     Trick Shot"},{"page":131,"text":"Lasting injuries\nWhen a warrior goes Out of Action, their opponent rolls two D6, one after the other (a D66 roll) and looks up the result on the\nLasting Injuries table. If an Injury roll results in more than one Out of Action result, a separate roll on the Lasting Injuries table\nand each result is applied.\n\nGOING INTO RECOVERY\nSome result cause a warrior to go into recovery. The warrior's In Recovery box on warband roster is checked, and the warrior must\nmiss both the post-battle sequence of the current game and the next battle in order to recover from their injuries. This means that\na Leader or Champion who has gone Into Recovery may not perform post-battle actions at this time. During the Wrap-up of the\nwarband’s next battle, the In Recovery box will be cleared, the warrior becomes available once again and Leaders and Champions\nmay perform post-battle actions.\n\nNote: that no matter how may Lasting Injury rolls are made, a warrior that goes Into Recovery will only miss one game rather than\nmultiple games.\n\nD66           Lasting Injury\n11            Lesson Learned. The warrior goes into Recovery but gains D3 Experience.\n12-26         Out Cold. The warrior misses the rest of the battle, but avoids any long-term injuries. The warrior recovers in time\n              to perform post-battle actions.\n31-45         Grievous Injury. The warrior goes into Recovery.\n46            Humiliated. The warrior goes into Recovery. In addition, their Leadership and Cool characteristics are each\n              decreased by 1.\n51            Head Injury. The warrior goes into Recovery. In addition, their Intelligence and Willpower characteristics are each\n              decreased by 1.\n52            Eye Injury. The warrior goes into Recovery. In addition, their Ballistic Skill characteristic is decreased by 1.\n53            Hand Injury. The warrior goes into Recovery. In addition, their Weapon Skill characteristic is decreased by 1.\n54            Hobbled. The warrior goes into Recovery. In addition, their Movement characteristic is decreased by 1.\n55            Spinal Injury. The warrior goes into Recovery. In addition, their Strength characteristic is decreased by 1.\n56            Enfeebled. The warrior goes into Recovery. In addition, their Toughness characteristic is decreased by 1.\n61-65         Critical Injury. The warrior is in critical condition – if their injuries are not successfully treated by a visit to the\n              Physician (see below) in the post-battle sequence, they will die.\n66            Memorable Death. The warrior is killed instantly – not even the most talented Physician can save them. If the injury\n              was caused by an Attack action, the attacker gains one additional Experience.\n\nDEAD WARRIORS\nFor dead warriors see Post Battle sequence 5a (below). Dead warriors are deleted from the roster. Their equipment (except for\narmour) is added to the warband’s Stash as long as their warband had at least one warrior on the battlefield at the end of the battle,\nor if the warrior was taken to the Doc but still died (either because the warband could not pay for their treatment or there were\ncomplications). Otherwise, the dead warrior’s equipment is lost.\n\nCHARACTERISTIC PENALTIES\nSome results on the Lasting Injuries table give a permanent penalty to a warrior's characteristic. Their Warrior Card must be\namended immediately – note that their gold crowns value does not change.\nThe warrior’s Maximum Characteristics is also reduced.\n\nMINIMUM CHARACTERISTICS\nA warrior's characteristics cannot be reduced beyond a certain level, as shown below. If one of a warrior's characteristics would be\nreduced below this level as the result of a Lasting Injury, the warrior goes into recovery, but suffers no additional penalty:\n        • Weapon Skill, Ballistic Skill and Initiative cannot be reduced to worse than 1\n        • Leadership, Cool, Willpower and Intelligence cannot be reduced to worse than 2\n        • Movement, Strength and Toughness cannot be reduced to less than 1."},{"page":132,"text":"SUCCUMBING TO INJURIES\nIf a warrior is Seriously Injured when the battle ends, roll a D6 for them during the Wrap-up. On a 3 or more, they survive without\nany further complications, but on a 1 or 2, they succumb to the injuries suffered during the battle and are treated as having gone\nOut of Action. A Lasting Injury roll is made for them, as described previously.\n\n\nBeing Captured\nIf only one warband has warriors on the battlefield at the end of the battle, there is a chance that they might Capture a fallen\nenemy. Roll 2d6 and add the number of opposing warriors who went Out of Action (including those who have succumbed to their\ninjuries, during the Warp-up). If the warband also includes a Bounty Hunter, add +1 to the result of the roll. If the result is 13 or\ngreater, an enemy warrior has been Captured.\n\n\nShuffle together the Warrior cards of any enemy warriors who went Out of Action (leaving those with the Fear or Terror rule), but\nnot those for any that suffered a Critical Injury or Memorable Death result, they are left where they fell! Draw one of these\nWarrior card at random – that warrior is Captured. Make a note in the Lasting Injury/Captured By box on the warband roster for\nthe Captured warrior, recording the name of the warband of the player who has Captured the warrior.\nWhilst a warrior is Captured, they are unavailable for battles and post-battle actions as if they were In Recovery – however, this\nlasts until they are freed (as follows) rather than for just one battle. The Capturing warband should make a note in the Stash\nsection of their warband roster of the name of the warrior they now hold Captive.\n\n\nCAPTURED WARRIORS\nOnce a warrior has been Captured, their warband has the chance to attempt to free them. The next time the same two warbands\nface each other, the Captured warrior's controlling player may declare that they will be attempting a Rescue Mission. This\nsupersedes the Determine Scenario steps of the pre-battle sequence – Instead, the Rescue Mission scenario is played.\n\nIf the warband does not wish to attempt the Rescue Mission scenario, and a different scenario is played, the warband holding the\nCaptive will sell them to slavers or kill them an collect their bounty (see below). This is worked out in the post-battle sequence of\nthat battle or any subsequent battle.\n\nAt any time during the campaign, regardless of whether a Rescue Mission has been attempted, the two warbands controlling\nplayers can come to an agreement to secure the Captive’s return. This could be a payment of gold crowns, a trade for another\nCaptive, or a valuable item of equipment or anything else – this is entirely up to the two players to decide and either warband is\nfree to decline an offer made by the other. If an agreement is reached, the Captured warrior is returned immediately and becomes\navailable to the warband once more.\n\n\nFleeing the battlefield\nIn a Campaign, it is often wise for a warband to quit a fight whilst they are still ahead. This is especially true in ambushes, and\nwhen smaller crews find themselves taking on larger and more dangerous ones! A warband’s controlling player can choose to\nautomatically fail any Rout test the warband is required to make.\n\nOnce a warband has routed (either voluntarily or by failing a Rout test), the controlling player can declare that the warband will\nflee the battlefield at the start of any Action phase. Any Active and Pinned warriors immediately flee the battlefield.. Engaged\nwarriors must attempt to break away from combat – make an Initiative check for each. If the check is passed, they flee the\nbattlefield. If the check is failed, they are Seriously Injured. Once the warband that has declared it will flee has only Seriously\n\n\nInjured warriors on     the battlefield, the battle ends. Roll to see if the Seriously Injured warriors succumb to their injuries during\nthe Wrap-up as usual."},{"page":133,"text":"Income\nAt the end of each battle, a warband may roll on the\nExploration chart. This is done as soon as a game is over so\n                                                                                    exploration procedure\nthat players can witness each other’s dice rolls. As you can see         1.   Roll 1D6 for each of your Heroes who survived the\nfrom the chart, a warband that is just starting out has little                battle and one extra dice if you won, plus any extra\nchance of finding the more obscure places in Mordheim.                        dice allowed by skills or equipment. Note, however,\nHowever, a warband will make more discoveries as it goes                      that you must pick a maximum of six dice out of all\nalong thanks to its better equipment and accumulated skills.                  the dice you roll, even if you are allowed to roll seven\n                                                                              dice or more.\nRoll a D6 for each Hero (Leader, Champion and Raw Recruit)               2.   Some things, such as skills and equipment, (like the\nin your warband who survives without going out of action.                     Mordheim Map) may allow you to re-roll dice.\nThis represents the warband’s efforts to unearth wyrdstone. Do           3.   If you rolled any natural doubles, triples, etc, you have\nnot roll for any Heroes who went out of action during the                     found an unusual location in Mordheim. Consult the\nbattle; they are taken back to the warband’s encampment to                    Exploration chart on the next page to see what you\nrecuperate instead. So, for example, if your warband includes                 find. Refer to the appropriate entry on the following\nfour Heroes who all survived the last battle, you can roll four               pages and follow the instructions given there.\ndice. If you won your last game, you may roll one extra dice.            4.   Add the results together and consult the chart on the\nAdd the results of the dice together and consult the                          next page to see how many shards of wyrdstone you\nExploration chart to see how many shards of wyrdstone your                    have found. Mark down the amount of wyrdstone on\nwarband has found.                                                            your warband’s roster sheet.\n\nDo not roll for Henchmen. This does not mean that they don’t         NUMBER OF WYRDSTONE SHARDS FOUND\nsearch the ruins, but instead represents the efforts of the                   DICE RESULT             SHARDS FOUND\nHeroes in coordinating the search parties. In addition, some\n                                                                                   1-5                     1\nHenchmen like Zombies or Warhounds (for obvious reasons)\n                                                                                   6-11                    2\nare not particularly useful when it comes to looking for\n                                                                                  12-17                    3\nwyrdstone.\n                                                                                  18-24                    4\n                                                                                  25-30                    5\nrolling multiples                                                                 31-35                    6\nAs well as finding shards of wyrdstone, the warband can come                       36+                     7\nacross unusual places or encounter inhabitants of the ruined\ncity. If you roll two or more of the same number while\nsearching, you have found an unusual building or encountered\nsomething out of ordinary. Consult the chart and refer to the\n                                                                     selling wyrdstone\nappropriate entry in the Exploration results. For example, you       Wyrdstone is tremendously valuable and is in constant\nmight roll two 3’s or three 5’s, in which case you should refer      demand by Imperial nobles. This means that finding buyers for\nto the chart. Choose the most numerous multiples if you score        your warband’s wyrdstone is not difficult. You do not have to\nmore than one set of multiples. So, if you rolled a double 3 and     sell all your wyrdstone immediately after the battle – you may\na triple 5, only look up the triple 5 on the Exploration chart. In   want to hoard it and sell it later, as selling wyrdstone in smaller\nthe case of two doubles or triples look up the highest result.       quantities will increase demand and raise the price.\nFor example, if you rolled double 1 and double 3, look up the\ndouble 3 result.                                                     Unfortunately, the demands of running a warband often mean\n                                                                     that you will have to sell most of your wyrdstone as soon as\nAny money or loot you find in these locations is added straight      you find it. The warband must spend a large portion of its\nto the warband’s treasury. Any shards of wyrdstone you find          income on basic necessities such as food, drink, repair of\ncan be sold as normal.                                               weapons, and new arrows and ammunition, as well as\n                                                                     celebrating! A warband leader is also expected to share any\n                                                                     profits made by selling wyrdstone between his men which\n                                                                     means that the more money the warband makes from such\n                                                                     sales, the bigger the share for the men."},{"page":134,"text":"The more models there are in the warband, the more it costs to        Vindication in the temple at Sigmar’s Rock, the more aid they\nmaintain and the higher the level of any profits made that must       will receive from the temple.\nbe shared between the men. The number indicated on the\nfollowing chart is the profit in gold crowns earned after             Thus, all gold crowns in the possession of a Sisters of Sigmar\ndeducting the warband’s maintenance costs. The profit is              warband represent the resources that the High Matriarch will\nadded to warband’s stash.                                             put at their disposal. It does not represent money in a literal\n                                                                      sense, so you may like to think of it as faith, piety, dedication,\n                                Number of warriors in warband         etc.\n                          1-3   4-6  7-9     10-12     13-15    16+\n                     1     45    40   35       30        30      25\n                                                                      Skaven and Undead\nNo. of Shards Sold\n\n\n\n\n                     2     60    55   50       45        50      35\n                     3     75    70   65       60        55      50   Neither of these warbands puts much value on gold, but they\n                     4     90    80   70       65        60      55   send all the wyrdstone they find to their superiors and receive\n                     5    110   100   90       80        70      65   aid and resources in return. Skaven use their own currency for\n                     6    120   110  100       90        80      70   trading, while the Undead are somewhat beyond petty\n                     7    145   130  120      110       100      90   concepts of wealth. For Skaven, the gold crowns in the\n                     8+   155   140  130      120       110     100   warband’s stash represent the warp tokens which the Skaven\n                                                                      use for currency, while for the Undead it represents the favour\n                                                                      they enjoy in the eyes of their master, Vlad von Carstein of\nSisters of Sigmar and income                                          Sylvania.\nWorldly possessions mean little to the Sisters, but their holy\nmission to purify Mordheim of the influence of Chaos requires\nsupplies and weaponry, and these are much in demand. Thus\n                                                                      spending income\nthe warbands of the Sisterhood compete with each other to             You can spend any accumulated money on weapons, armour,\ngain the best weapons and equipment from the temple’s                 hiring new warriors, buying new equipment or simply save the\narmoury. To measure their success, the more wyrdstone the             money for a bigger purchase. See the Trading section for\nSisters bring to be kept under lock and key in the Vault of           details.\n\n\n                                                    Exploration chart\nDOUBLES                                                               FOUR OF A KIND\n11                                     Well                           1111                            Gunsmith\n22                                     Shop                           2222                            Shrine\n33                                     Corpse                         3333                            Townhouse\n44                                     Straggler                      4444                            Armourer\n55                                     Overturned Cart                5555                            Graveyard\n66                                     Ruined Hovels                  6666                            Catacombs\n\nTRIPLES                                                               FIVE OF A KIND\n111                                    Tavern                         11111                           Moneylender’s House\n222                                    Smithy                         22222                           Alchemist’s Laboratory\n333                                    Prisoners                      33333                           Gem Cutter\n444                                    Fletcher                       44444                           Merchant’s House\n555                                    Market Hall                    55555                           Shattered Building\n666                                    Returning a Favour             66666                           Entrance to the Catacombs\n\n                                                                      SIX OF A KIND\n                                                                      111111                          The Pit\n                                                                      222222                          Hidden Treasure\n                                                                      333333                          Dwarf Smithy\n                                                                      444444                          Slaughtered Warband\n                                                                      555555                          Fighting Arena\n                                                                      666666                          Noble’s Villa"},{"page":135,"text":"Doubles\n(1 1) Well                                                           (4 4) Straggler\nThe public wells, of which there were several in Mordheim, were      Your warband encounters one of the survivors of Mordheim,\ncovered by rooves raised up on pillars and adorned with              who has lost his sanity along with all his worldly possessions.\ncarvings and fountains. The city was proud of its water system.      Skaven and Orc warbands can sell the straggler to slavers (or\nUnfortunately, like all the other wells, this one is in a parlous    eat him) and gain D6x5 gc.\nstate and undoubtedly polluted with wyrdstone.                       Possessed warbands can sacrifice the unfortunate individual\nChoose one of your Heroes and roll a D6. If the result is equal      for the glory of the Chaos gods. The leader of the warband will\nto or lower than his Toughness, he finds one shard of                gain +1D3 Experience.\nwyrdstone at the bottom of the well. If he fails, the Hero           Undead warbands can kill the man and gain a Skeleton\nswallows tainted water and must miss the next game through           Warrior with no equipment for no cost.\nsickness.                                                            Any other warband can interrogate the man and gain insight\n                                                                     into the city. Next time you roll on the Exploration chart, roll\n(2 2) Shop                                                           one dice more than is usually allowed, and discard any one\nThe Merchants Guild shop has been thoroughly ransacked. Even         dice. (For example, if you have three Heroes, roll four dice and\nso, there are still items scattered around the single, long room,    pick any three).\nmingled in with the rubble. Some are useful, such as cast iron\npots and pans and rolls of fine cloth. All manner of smaller items   (5 5) Overturned Cart\nare lying about – the sort of frippery which no longer has a use     Stuck in a ruined gateway is an overturned wagon – the covered\nin a devastated city with few inhabitants.                           type that nobles travel in from the city to their estates in the\nAfter a thorough search you find loot worth D6x5 gc. If you          country. Since anyone important fled a long time ago, what is it\nroll a 1 you will also find a Lucky Charm (see the Equipment         doing here? The horses have broken their traces, or did someone\nsection).                                                            cut them free? Roll a D6 to see what you find:\n                                                                               D6 Result\n(3 3) Corpse                                                                   1-2      Mordheim Map (see Equipment)\nYou find a still-warm corpse. A chipped dagger sticks out of his               3-4      A purse with 2D6x5 gc\nback. Surprisingly, his possessions have not been looted.                      5-6 J    A jewelled sword (worth 50gc) and jewelled\nYou gain a Dagger, in addition, to see what you find when you                  dagger (20gc).\nsearch the corpse, roll a D6:\n         D6 Result                                                   (6 6) Ruined Hovels\n         1         D6x5 gc                                           The street consists of ruined hovels, which are leaning over at\n         2         Club                                              alarming angles. Not much worth looting here.\n         3         Axe                                               You find loot worth D6x5 gc amidst the ruins.\n         4         Spear\n         5         Sword\n         6         Suit of light armour"},{"page":136,"text":"Triples\n(1 1 1) Tavern                                                        Undead warbands can callously kill the prisoners and gain a\nThe ruin of a tavern is recognisable by its sign still hanging on     Skeleton Warrior with no equipment at no cost.\nthe wall. The upper part of the building is ruined, but the cellars   Skaven and Orcs can sell the prisoners into slavery for 3D6x10\nare cut into rock and are still full of barrels. There are broken     gc.\nflagons and tankards everywhere.                                      Other warbands can escort the prisoners out of the city. For\nYou could easily sell the barrels for a good price. Unfortunately     their trouble, they are rewarded with 2D6x5 gc. In addition,\nyour men are also interested in the contents! The warband’s           one of the prisoners decides he wishes to join the warband.\nleader must take a Leadership check. If he passes, the warband        You gain a Henchmen of your choice from your Warband List.\ngains 4D6x5 gc worth of wines and ales which can be sold              They start with no equipment.\nimmediately.\nIf he fails, the men drink most of the alcohol despite their          (4 4 4) Fletcher\nleader’s threats and curses. You have D6x5 gc worth of alcohol        This hovel was once the workshop of a fletcher – a maker of\nleft when the warband reaches their encampment.                       bows and arrows. There are bundles of yew staves and willow\nUndead, Witch Hunter and Sisters of Sigmar warbands                   rods everywhere.\nautomatically pass this check, as they are not tempted by such        Roll a D6 to see what you find:\nworldly things as alcohol.                                                      D6 Result\n                                                                                1. D3 Bows\n(2 2 2) Smithy                                                                  2. D3 Long Bows\nThe furnace and toppled anvil make it obvious what work was                     3. Quiver Of Bodkin Arrows\ndone here. Most of the iron and the tools have been looted long                 4. Quiver Of Hunting Arrows\nago. Coal and slag litter the floor but there may still be weapons              5. D3 Crossbows\nto be found among the debris.                                                   6. Heavy Crossbow\nRoll a D6 to determine what you find inside:\n         D6 Result                                                    (5 5 5) Market Hall\n         1        Sword                                               The market hall was raised up on pillars, with the timbered corn\n         2        Bastard Sword                                       exchange above the open market place. The upper storey has\n         3        Morning Star                                        been badly damaged, but the covered market still offers a good\n         4        Halberd                                             deal of shelter. The remains of the last market day are still lying\n         5        Great Axe                                           around on the cobbles. Most of this is broken pottery and iron\n         6        2D6x5 gc worth of scrap metal (add the              pots.\n                  value to your treasury).                            You find several items worth 2D6x10 gc in total.\n\n(3 3 3) Prisoners                                                     (6 6 6) Returning a Favour\nA muffled sound comes from one of the buildings. Inside you           As you are returning to your encampment, you meet one of your\nfind a group of finely dressed people who have been locked in a       old acquaintances. He has come to repay an old favour or debt.\ncellar. Perhaps they are prisoners taken by cultists, ready to be     You gain the services of any one Hired Sword (choose from\nsacrificed during Geheimnisnacht.                                     those available to your warband) for the duration of the next\nPossessed warbands can sacrifice the victims (undoubtedly             battle, free of charge. After the battle he will depart, or you may\nfinishing the job of the captors). They gain 2D3 Experience           continue to pay for his upkeep as normal. See the Hired\nwhich is distributed amongst the Heroes of the warband.               Swords section."},{"page":137,"text":"Four of a kind\n(1 1 1 1) Gunsmith                                                  ruined and the forge has been smashed. Rooting about in the\nYou find the workshop of a Dwarf gunsmith. Its doors have been      soot, you find various half-finished items of armour.\nbroken down and the rooms raided, but some of the iron              Roll a D6 to see what you find:\nstrongboxes have survived intact.                                        D6 Result\nRoll a D6 to see what you find:                                          1. D3 Shields\n     D6 Result                                                           2. D3 Bucklers\n     1. Blunderbuss                                                      3. D3 Suits Of Light Armour\n     2. Brace Of Pistols (Pair)                                          4. D3 Suits Of Heavy Armour\n     3. Brace Of Duelling Pistols (Pair)                                 5. Suit Of Full Plate Armour\n     4. D3 Handguns                                                      6. Suit Of Ithilmar Armour\n     5. D3 Flasks Of Superior Blackpowder\n     6. Bomb                                                        (5 5 5 5) Graveyard\n                                                                    You find an old graveyard, crammed with sepulchres that are\n(2 2 2 2) Shrine                                                    overgrown with ivy. The monuments to the dead are grotesque\nYour warband stumbles across a ruined shrine, which is so badly     and decorated with sculpted gargoyles. The ironwork has been\ndamaged that it is difficult to tell which god was once             ripped from some of the tombs, and stones have toppled off. It\nworshipped within its walls. A few images remain on the painted     looks as if some of the crypts have already been broken into by\nplaster walls but they have been defaced by heretics. Fragments     tomb robbers.\nof smashed statues lie among the ruins. Some items appear to be     Any warband apart from Witch Hunters and Sisters of Sigmar\ncovered in gold leaf, most of which has been torn off.              may loot the crypts and graves and gains D6x5 gc worth of\nYour warband may strip the shrine and gain 3D6x5 gc worth           loot.\nof loot.                                                            If you loot the graveyard, the next time you play against Sisters\nSisters of Sigmar or Witch Hunter warbands may save some of         of Sigmar or Witch Hunters, the entire enemy warband will\nthe shrine’s holy relics. They will gain 2D6x5 gc from their        hate all the models in your warband. Make a note of this on\npatrons, and a blessing from the gods. One of their weapons         your warband roster sheet.\n(chosen by the player) will gain the weapon trait Blessed.          Witch Hunters and Sisters of Sigmar will seal the graves. They\n                                                                    are rewarded for their piety by D6 Experience points\n(3 3 3 3) Townhouse                                                 distributed amongst the Heroes of the warband.\nThis three-storey house was once part of a tenement block\noverlooking a narrow alleyway. The street is now in ruins, but      (6 6 6 6) Catacombs\nthis house remains largely intact. Exploring it you find that the   You find an entrance to the catacombs and tunnels below\ngarret leans over so far that you can step out of the window into   Mordheim.\nthe attic of the house opposite.                                    You can use the new tunnels you found in the next battle you\nYour warband finds 3D6x5 gc worth of loot.                          play. Position up to three warriors (not any warrior with Large\n                                                                    Target special rule) anywhere on the battlefield at ground level.\n(4 4 4 4) Armourer                                                  They are set up at the end of the player’s first turn and cannot\nA breastplate hanging from a pole drew your attention to this       be placed within 8\" of any enemy models. This represents the\nplace, obviously too high up to be easily looted. The workshop is   warriors making their way through the tunnels, infiltrating\n                                                                    enemy lines and emerging suddenly from below ground."},{"page":138,"text":"Five of a kind\n(1 1 1 1 1) Moneylender’s House\nA grand mansion, that is strongly built from stone, has survived    (4 4 4 4 4) Merchant’s House\nthe cataclysm remarkably well. A carved coat of arms adorns the     The merchant’s house stands by the waterfront. It has a vaulted\nlintel above the doorway although it has been defaced by raiders    stone undercroft which is still stacked with barrels and bales of\nand the symbols are now unrecognisable. The door itself, has        cloth. The foodstuffs have been looted or eaten long ago and\nbeen smashed open with axes and hangs open on its hinges.           huge rats infest the rotting bales. Up the stairs are the dwelling\nInside, hidden amongst the debris, you find D6x50 gc to add to      quarters, solidly built of timber, although badly damaged you\nyour treasury.                                                      think you can still get up to them but you’ll need to tread with\n                                                                    care!\n(2 2 2 2 2) Alchemist’s Laboratory                                  Inside you find several valuable objects which can be sold for\nA narrow stairway leads down into a crypt-like dwelling which       2D6x25 gc. If you roll a double, instead of finding money you\nwas once an alchemist’s workshop. The sign still hangs from one     find the Symbol of the Order of Freetraders. A Hero in\nhinge above the entrance. It looks as if this was a very old        possession of this gains the Haggle skill.\nbuilding which has remained in use for centuries although it did\nnot survive the comet’s destruction too well. The stone floor has   (5 5 5 5 5) Shattered Building\nstrange symbols on it and there are charts and astrological         The comet destroyed this building almost completely, making it\nsymbols painted onto the walls.                                     unsafe for all but the most daring to explore. But places such as\nIn the ruins you find loot worth 3D6x5 gc and a battered old        this are the best for searching for wyrdstone shards.\nnotebook. One of your Heroes may study the Alchemist’s              You find D3 shards of wyrdstone amongst the ruins. In\nnotebook, the gains Academic skills as a Primary Skill set.         addition, the warband leader makes a Leadership check. If\n                                                                    passed a wardog that was guarding the building joins the\n(3 3 3 3 3) Gem Cutter                                              warband (Human warbands only).\nThe houses in the jewellers’ quarter have all been well and truly\nlooted long ago. Even the rubble has been picked over many          (6 6 6 6 6) Entrance to the Catacombs\ntimes for fragments of gold and gems. But still, some small but     You find a well-hidden entrance to the dark catacombs which\nvaluable items may have been overlooked.                            extend for miles beneath the city of Mordheim. Although the\nRoll a D6 to see what you find:                                     entrance looks foreboding the tunnels will take hours off your\nD6 Result                                                           searches of the city.\n     1. Gold Jewellery worth 2D6x5                                  You can use these tunnels to explore Mordheim more\n     2. Onyx worth D3x25 gc                                         efficiently. From now on, you may re-roll one dice when you\n     3. Amethysts worth D6x25 gc                                    roll on the Exploration chart. Make a note of this in your\n     4. Emeralds worth 100 gc                                       warband’s roster sheet. Second and subsequent catacomb\n     5. Sapphires worth 250 gc                                      entrances you find do not grant you any additional re-rolls,\n     6. Rubies D6x50 gc                                             although you may find further re-rolls from other sources.\nIf your warband does not sell the gems, one of your Heroes\nmay keep them and displays them proudly. The warrior gains\nOpulent Jewellery (see Equipment section)."},{"page":139,"text":"Six of a kind\n(1 1 1 1 1 1) The Pit                                                After giving the dead their final rites (Sisters of Sigmar or\nYou have come within sight of the Pit, the huge crater created by    Witch Hunters), eating them (Skaven or Undead) or looting\nthe comet. A black cloud still rises from it but you can see         them (anyone else!) you find the following items. Roll for every\nglowing wyrdstone everywhere. This is the domain of the              item separately (apart from the gold coins and daggers) to see\nShadow Lord, the lord of the Possessed, and no-one is welcome        if you find it. For example, on a roll of 4+ you will find the\nhere – even his own followers!                                       suits of light armour.\nYou may choose to send one of your Heroes to search for any                     Item                        D6 Result Needed\nwyrdstone hidden here. Roll a D6. On a roll of 1 the Hero is                    3D6x25 gc                             Auto\ndevoured by the daemonic guardians of the Pit and never seen                    D3 Daggers                            Auto\nagain. On a roll of 2 or more he returns with D6+1 shards of                    D3 Shields                            2+\nwyrdstone.                                                                      D3 Swords                             3+\n                                                                                D3 Axes                               3+\n(2 2 2 2 2 2) Hidden Treasure                                                   D3 Bows                               4+\nIn the depths of Mordheim, you come across a hidden chest,                      D3 Suits of Light Armour              4+\nbearing the coat-of-arms of one of the noble families of the town.              Mordheim Map                          4+\nWhen you open the chest you find the following items. Roll for                  D3 Halberds                           5+\nevery item on the list separately (apart from the gold crowns)                  Suit of Heavy Armour                  5+\nto see whether you have found it. For example, on a roll of a 4+\nyou find the wyrdstone.                                              (5 5 5 5 5 5) Fighting Arena\n          Items                       D6 Result Needed               During better times, Mordheim was famous for its duellists and\n          5D6x20 gc                            Auto                  pit warriors. You have found one of the areas used to train these\n          D3 Pieces of wyrdstone               4+                    warriors. The place is filled with training equipment and\n          D3 Gems worth 25 gc each             4+                    practice weapons.\n          Sacred Relic                         5+                    You find a training manual, which you can either sell for 100\n          Suit of Full Plate Armour            5+                    gc or let one of your Heroes read. The Warrior gains Combat\n          Elven Cloak                          5+                    skills as a Primary Skill set, and their WS is increased by +1.\n          Holy tome                            5+                    This can be above their normal Maximum Characteristics (for\n          Magical artefact                     5+                    example, a Human who has the book would now have a\n                                                                     maximum Weapon Skill of 7).\n(3 3 3 3 3 3) Dwarf Smithy\nYou find a solidly built stone workshop. A runic inscription         (6 6 6 6 6 6) Noble’s Villa\nindicates that this may have been a Dwarf smithy.                    You find a fine house which is partially ruined. It has been\nRoll a D6 to see what you find:                                      thoroughly ransacked and all the furniture has been stripped of\nD6 Result                                                            its fine fabrics. Shards of broken pottery of the finest quality are\n     1. Dwarf Handgun                                                scattered over the floor.\n     2. D3 Great Hammers                                             Roll a D6 to see what you find:\n     3. D3 Suits of Heavy Armour                                                D6        Result\n     4. Gromril Axe                                                             1-2       D6x50 gc worth of items and money to add\n     5. Gromril Great axe                                                                 to your treasury.\n     6. Gromril Plate Armour                                                    3-4       2D3 vials of Crimson Shade.\n                                                                                5-6       A hidden magical artefact carefully\n(4 4 4 4 4 4) Slaughtered Warband                                                         concealed in a hidden cellar or behind a\nYou find the remains of an entire warband. Broken bodies lay                              secret door. Roll on the Magical Artefacts\nscattered among the ruins, torn apart by some monstrous                                   table.\ncreature. You see a huge shape, which looks like an immense\nPossessed creature, shambling away."},{"page":140,"text":"Magical artefacts table\nRoll a D66 and use this table to determine which item you find when a result in the Exploration chart indicates that you have found a\nmagical artefact. In a campaign none of these items can appear more than once, so if you find a magic item which is already in\nsomeone else’s possession roll again – even if the warrior carrying it has been killed.\nIf you do not wish to keep these amazing and rare magical artefacts, then you may sell them for 2D6x5 gold crowns.\n\n\n11-12. CLOAK OF MIST AND SHADOWS\nThis cloak endows the wearer with ethereal form, like that of a\nspirit or ghost. Free from the bond of his material body, the        21-22 ASRAI LONGBOW OF SEEKING\nwarrior is free to move through solid matter like a ghost.           This magnificent long bow was a gift to Count Steinhardt from\nThis item can only be used by warriors that are not riding a         the Elf lords of the Forest of Shadows.\nmount. The warrior can perform the following action:                 The warrior may make attacks with the following weapon\nTURN ETHEREAL (Basic) The warrior turns Ethereal (place a            profile:\nmarker on the warrior’s card a reminder) and treats all terrain\nas open terrain for the purposes of movement. The warrior can        Weapon                  Range          Str         AP      D\npass through walls and other obstructions but may not end            Elf Bow                    36           3          -1      1\ntheir movement inside passable terrain. The warrior is also          Traits: Accuracy, Penetrating, Magical, Rending\nnever slowed by any special rule, spell or item that would                • Shooting attacks made with this weapon do not suffer\notherwise reduce their movement or stop them moving                           To Hit penalties.\ncompletely.                                                               • If any Dwarf is an eligible target, the arrows will\nThe warrior cannot make any shooting attacks, cast magic                      always deviate from their intended target, the Dwarf\nspells or close combat attacks while ethereal. Conversely,                    becomes the priority target.\nEthereal warriors can only be wounded by spells, magical                  • Cannot be used to shoot at Elves. The arrows\nattacks and magic weapons or effects. The warrior can perform                 automatically miss.\nthe same action to turn back and cease being Ethereal.\n                                                                     22-24 THE HELM OF IRON AND BLOOD\n13-14 THE COUNT OF VENTIMIGLIA’S MISERICORDIA                        Nearly six hundred years ago, a band of Khorne’s Chaos\nThis dagger was used by the notorious Tilean gentleman-pirate        warriors began a crusade of death and despair, starting in the\nknown as the ‘Black Corsair’. It is claimed that he found it in      far eastern reaches of Ostland and ravaging all the way down to\nancient Elven ruins and legend also has it that the dagger’s blade   the dark woods of Sylanvia. This helmet belonged to Vulknar,\ncannot be damaged in any way.                                        the leader of the warband. The helmet has since been worn by\nThe warrior may make attacks with the following weapon               many champions of Khorne through the ages, the Helm of Iron\nprofile:                                                             and Blood always survives and shows up I some obscure and\nWeapon                  Range            Str         AP         D    forgotten location years later. Those that don it are overcome\nMisericordia            Melee             S           -         1    with the overwhelming desire to spill blood.\nTraits: Back Stab, Magical, Pulverise, Rending                       A warrior wearing this gains Frenzy. The warrior always\n                                                                     counts as being Frenzied and cannot lose this from being\n15-16 ATT’LA’S PLATE MAIL                                            seriously injured or broken.\nThis armour was given as a present by the Dwarf Lord Kurgan          The warrior gains +1 to his Strength in close combat.\nto the warlord Att’la in the time of Sigmar Heldenhammer.            The warrior can never leave close combat voluntarily but can\nAtt’la’s Plate Mail is a suit of Gromril Plate Armour with the       still be Broken.\nfollowing abilities:                                                 The warrior will always perform a Coup de Grace if possible.\nRune of Stone: Armour Save 3+.                                       If there are any seriously injured models within the warrior’s\nRune of Spell Breaking: The Hero wearing this armour has             charge range at the beginning of their turn, they will charge\nMagic Resistance (4+).                                               and perform a Coup de Grace, even if they are members of his\nRune of Fortitude: The Hero has an extra wound. Note that            own warband!\nthis may take his total Wounds above his race’s maximum.             Once given to a warrior it bonds to their skin and cannot be\n                                                                     given to another warrior."},{"page":141,"text":"25-26 ALL-SEEING EYE OF NUMAS                                         41-42 THE CURSED BOOK\nThis jewel was recovered from the ruins of Numas far in the           This tome was written by the mad Necromancer Har’ak Iman,\nsouth. It gives its wielder horrific nightmares that predict his      said to be the most depraved man to have ever lived. His vileness\nfuture.                                                               radiates from the book, draining life and energy from all living\nIf a warrior with the All-Seeing Eye of Numas is a sentry in a        beings.\nscenario that uses the Sentries special rule, they can attempt to     All warriors (friend or foe) in 3” suffer a -1 to hit penalty. Has\nspot attacker even if they are not within their vision arc. In        no effect on Undead and Daemonic warriors.\naddition, the D6 roll to see whether a warrior is spotted has a\n+1 modifier (a natural 1 still fails)                                 43-44 DWARF BATTLE AXE\nThe warrior rolls two dice when rolling on the Exploration            The Axe is empowered by Dwarfen magic, enabling the wielder\nChart.                                                                to employ it with dazzling effect. As producing these weapons\nThe warrior gains the Dodge skill. If the warrior already has         requires a great investment of time and skill, Dwarfs present\nthe Dodge skill, then the chance of dodging is increased to a         these weapons as gifts to individual humans who have done the\n5+.                                                                   Dwarf people a great service. Each Axe is unique in appearance,\nAll animals (Warbeasts, such as wardogs, horses, etc) will be         though all are forged of a gromril alloy and feature the makers\naffected by frenzy when fighting against the bearer of the All-       rune proudly on the handle.\nseeing Eye.                                                           The warrior can make attacks with following weapon profile:\n                                                                      Weapon                    Range           Str       AP        D\n31-32 NIGHTSHROUD                                                     Axe                       Melee            S          -       1\nEnsorcelled in pitch darkness in the heart of Castle Drachenfels,     Traits: Cleave, Magical\nthe Nightshroud owes more to the otherworld than to reality.          Rune of Fury which grants the warrior +1 Attack dice in close\nOriginally fashioned from the death-raiments of King                  combat.\nPharatohep, the Nightshroud has since been soaked in the blood        Rune of Cleaving +1 Strength in close combat.\nof sorcerers and witches. The aura of gloom that clings to it is so\nstrong it can physically manifest, lashing out with shadowy           45-46 RING OF VOLANS\ntendrils that grapple with all those who would strike the wearer.     Volans was the greatest of the human pupils of Teclis, the\nThe Nightshroud confers a 6+ armour save. If the warrior              founder of the Colleges of Magic. A warriors who possesses the\nalready has an armour save it adds + 1 to the saving throw.           Ring of Volans is able , for a small time at least, to harness a tiny\nFurthermore, enemy models in base contact with the wearer             fraction of one of the eight Winds of Magic Many wizards have\nlose all Strength bonuses conferred from normal weapons,              made imitations of this magic artefact, so this is likely a copy or\nskills and magical weapons, and have the Always Strikes Last          the original.\nspecial rule. (Wizards can wear the Nightshroud and still cast        The Ring of Volans contains one random spell from the Lesser\nspells.)                                                              Magic table. Any warrior with this item can perform the action\n                                                                      Cast Spells (X) and cast the spell as usual. If a Magical Miscast\n33-34 HELM OF THE DAMNED                                              is rolled, don’t roll on the Magical Miscast table, instead the\nCarved with images of the screaming faces of tortured souls, this     warrior is Pinned.\ncorrupt artefact constantly emits a chilling wail. The bearer\ndraws revitalising power from the spirits imprisoned within the       51-52 AMULET OF THRICE BLESSED COPPER\nhelmet, but at times their eternal wailing overpowers his mind.       After killers failed to assassinate the Emperor in 1499 IC, a\nThe warrior has a 4+ ward save. The wearer is subject to              merchant from distant Cathay presented the monarch with\nStupidity, even if the warrior is normally immune to                  amulet. It was a small disk of copper carved with strange sigils.\npsychology.                                                           While the Emperor gratefully accepted the item, he had no love\n                                                                      for magic or anything of the sort, and so, he promptly had the\n35-36 THE CURSED SHIELD OF MOUSILLON                                  merchant executed and ordered the amulet destroyed. The\nBretonnian legends speak in contempt of these accursed shields        guard tasked with the duty kept it instead. It changed hands\nwhich carry the symbol of the Black Grail and were used by the        many times, finally resurfacing briefly during the Great War\nUnholy Knights at the Battle of Mousillon.                            Against Chaos, when an Empire captain who, after a failed\nThe Cursed Shield counts as a normal shield, in addition one          poisoning by a cultist, noticed its change of colour when it came\nEngaged enemy warrior loses 1 Attack. (to a minimum of 1              close to the poisoned wine. It was lost again shortly after the\nattack). All Bretonnian Knights and Characters hate the               captain was stabbed to death on the following night.\nwarrior carrying the shield.                                          All close combat attacks made against a warrior with this\n                                                                      amulet suffer -1 Strength. The warrior wearing this is also\n                                                                      immune to poisons."},{"page":142,"text":"53-54 BOOTS OF BOVVA                                                61-62 SHADOW SHROUD PENDANT\nBovva was the apprentice of Rathnugg the most famous book           Some wyrdstone contaminated veins of ore develop strange\nmaker of all time. Charged with Cobbling a set of footwear          property of absorbing light, thus a radius of shadowy darkness\nsuitable for a Count, Bovva worked hard to produce the finest       forms around the metal.\nboots of his career. He worked for two weeks, striving for both     Shooting attacks against the warrior suffer an extra -1 to hit\ncomfort and durability, believing he had achieved his life’s work   penalty.\nupon finishing. But when the Elector Count of Stirland saw the\npair, he was unimpressed, believing Bovva was making a fool of      63-64 ATHERYIC LANTERN\nhim. The noble had poor Bovva hung from the shop’s rafters and      When the artefact is activated, it acts as a beacon to the\ngave the boots to the stable boy, who had much success              denizens of the Warp who would feast upon the dead and\nthroughout the rest of his days.                                    dying. The warrior can perform the IGNITE ATHERYRIC\nA warrior with the Boots of Bovva gains +1 Attack dice in close     LANTERN (DOUBLE) action. If they do, any Seriously\ncombat with the following weapon profile:                           Injured warrior (friend or foe) within 12\" must make a\nWeapon                    Range         Str         D        AP     Toughness check or go Out of Action.\nBoots of Bovva            Melee           S         1        +1\nTraits: Magical, Stun                                               65 66 SONNEKLINGE\nThis weapon cannot be disarmed.                                     This flaming sword that was once owned by Lord Karad Von\n                                                                    Carron. His victory over the Goblinoid hordes that attacked the\n55-56 SHADOW CASKET                                                 town of Carroburg is the stuff of legend. Even his death as the\nThe artefact is a gateway to a dark yawning void that the           hands of the Ogre Ratgot Dwarfmangler, when the fatally\nwarrior may open to sap the strength of those around them. The      wounded Ogre manged to slash Karad’s throat wide open,\nwarrior can perform the Unleash the Void (Double) action. If        couldn’t taint his memory.\nthey take this action, all other warriors within 6\" of them can     Sonneklinge is a bastard sword with following weapon profile:\nonly take a single action during their activation.                  Weapon                  Range             Str       AP         D\n                                                                    Sonneklinge              Melee           S+2         -1         1\n                                                                    Traits, Flaming attacks, Magical, Parrying, Unwieldy\n                                                                    A warrior wielding Sonneklinge has +1 Weapon (this can take\n                                                                    the warrior above their maximum characteristic) ."},{"page":143,"text":"The pre-battle sequence\nIn a Campaign, there are additional steps that take place before              scenario is the attacker.\nand after a battle, as listed below. They must be followed in the\norder shown, and must be done while both players are present.        RESCUE MISSIONS\nThe pre-battle sequence has the following steps:                     If one player has Captured another player’s warrior(s), the\n                                                                     Captured warrior’s player may issue a challenge to play the\nTHE PRE-BATTLE SEQUENCE                                              Rescue Mission scenario. If the challenge is accepted, then\n                                                                     the Rescue Mission scenario is automatically used for the\n1.    MAKE A CHALLENGE\n                                                                     battle. If the player holding the Captive refuses the\n2.    BUY ADVANCEMENTS AND RECRUIT HIRED\n                                                                     challenge, they automatically forfeit the Captive.\n      SWORDS\n                                                                     DETERMINING THE ATTACKER AND DEFENDER\n3.    DETERMINE SCENARIO\n                                                                     In the scenarios where there is an attacker and a defender, the\n4.    SET UP THE BATTLEFIELD                                         player with lowest warband rating may choose which he is.\n5.    CHOOSE CREWS\n6.    ANNOUNCE EXPLORATION BOONS                                     HOME TURF ADVANTAGE\n7.    DEPLOYMENT                                                     The scenario being played may indicate that the defender\n                                                                     benefits from the Home Turf Advantage, representing the\n1. MAKE A CHALLENGE                                                  warband fighting furiously to defend their valuable turf from\nFor a battle to be fought, one player must challenge another         attackers. A warband fighting with the Home Turf Advantage\nplayer to play a game.                                               is far less likely to rout and in some cases will fight ferociously\n                                                                     until the last.\n2. BUY ADVANCEMENTS AND RECRUIT HIRED\nSWORDS                                                               4. SET UP THE BATTLEFIELD\nEach player can spend Experience to purchase Advancements            The players now set up the battlefield. Some scenarios have\nfor their warriors. If both players wish to do so, the player with   special instructions for terrain. The more buildings the better,\nthe lower Warband Rating goes first, purchasing any                  so you should place all the terrain you have.\nAdvancements they wish, then the other player does so. If both\nplayers have the same Warband Rating, the winner of a roll-off       5. CHOOSE CREWS\nchooses whether to go first or second.                               After the battlefield has been set up, before warbands can be\nOnce any Advancements have been bought, players can spend            deployed, players must select their starting crews for the battle\ngold crowns to recruit Hired Swords. Again, if both players          ahead. The scenario being played will detail the method of\nwish to do so, the player with the lower Warband Rating goes         selection to be used and how many warriors can be selected.\nfirst.\n                                                                     6. ANNOUNCE EXPLORATION BOONS\n3. DETERMINE SCENARIO                                                Players may have Exploration Boons granted by the\nThe player with the lowest warband rating rolls on the               Exploration chart (e.g. Catacombs). Players should announce\nScenario table to determine which scenario is played. To             which, if any, of their Exploration Boons grant them a bonus\ndetermine which scenario will be used, roll 2D6 on the               that will have an effect on this game at this stage, forewarning\nfollowing table:                                                     their opponent. If a Exploration Boon is not announced, it\n                                                                     cannot be used during the coming game.\n2D6     Result\n2-3     The player with the higher warband rating chooses            7. DEPLOYMENT\n        which scenario to play. If both have the same warband        Many scenarios will provide details of the size and location of\n        rating, the winner of a roll off chooses. If there is an     deployment zones.\n        attacker and defender, the player who chose the\n        scenario is the attacker.\n4-6     Play the Skirmish scenario.\n7-12    The player with the lower warband rating chooses\n        which scenario to play. If both have the same warband\n        rating, the winner of a roll off chooses. If there is an\n        attacker and defender, the player who chose the"},{"page":144,"text":"Post-battle sequence\nThe post-battle sequence has the following steps:                        •    VISIT THE TRADING POST\n                                                                              The warrior visits the Trading Post, increasing the\nTHE POST-BATTLE SEQUENCE                                                      warband’s chances of finding Rare items. This is\n                                                                              resolved in step 6 (below).\n1.     WRAP UP\n2.     RECEIVE REWARDS                                                   •    SELL CAPTIVE\n3.     COLLECT INCOME                                                         Human and Dwarf warbands that capture evil races\n4.     POST-BATTLE ACTIONS                                                    will collect a bounty (and likely execute the enemy\n5.     UPDATE ROSTER                                                          warrior). Non-human and Non-Dwarf warbands will\n6.     REPORT RESULTS                                                         likely sell the captive to Slavers (or eat them. Or turn\n                                                                              them into an undead warrior.) Whether selling to\n1. WRAP UP                                                                    slavers or collecting a bounty, the outcome is the\n                                                                              same.\nEach player checks to see whether any of their Seriously\n                                                                         •    The warrior can sell any number of Captive warriors\nInjured warriors succumb to their injuries (see page 280), and\n                                                                              – as long as the Captive’s warband has had a chance\nwhether they capture any enemy warriors (see page 250). Any\n                                                                              to rescue them. Each captive is worth half their value,\nother events that take place ‘at the end of the battle’ are\n                                                                              rounding up to the nearest 5 -this many gold crowns\ntriggered here. Warriors that were recovering have made a full\n                                                                              are added to this warband’s Stash. The Captive’s\nrecovery and their In Recovery box on the warband roster is\n                                                                              controlling player should be informed as soon as\ncleared, meaning Leaders and Champions become available for\n                                                                              possible, and must delete the captive from their\npost-battle actions once more.\n                                                                              roster.\nPlayers should also consider shaking hands,\ncongratulating/commiserating with their opponent and                     •    MEDICAL ESCORT\nsharing favourite moments from the battle – some would say                    The warrior escorts a critically injured fellow warband\nthis is the most important step!                                              member to the Physician. Pick another warrior in the\n                                                                              warband who suffered a Critical Injury during the\n                                                                              battle and pay 2D6x10 gold crowns from the\n2. RECEIVE REWARDS\n                                                                              warband’s Stash. If the warband does not have\nEach scenario shows a list of rewards which the warbands can\n                                                                              sufficient funds, or does not wish to pay the full\nreceive, based on their performance during the battle. Any\n                                                                              amount, no roll is made and the warrior dies.\nequipment gained is added to the warband's Stash – it can be\n                                                                              Otherwise, roll a D6 on the table below:\ndistributed to warriors in Step 6.\n                                                                                D6 Result\nGAINING AND LOSING REPUTATION\n                                                                                1     Complications. The warrior dies.\nEach scenario contains a number of ways in which a warband\n                                                                                2- Stabilized. Roll a D6 – this is the second dice of\ncan gain or lose Reputation. If a warband both gains and loses\n                                                                                5     a D66 roll, the first is automatically a 5. Apply\nReputation, any gains are applied before any losses.\n                                                                                      the appropriate result from the Lasting Injuries\n                                                                                      table.\n3. COLLECT INCOME AND EXPLORATION                                               6     Full Recovery. The warrior goes into Recovery,\nEach warband rolls on the Exploration chart and determines                            but suffers no lasting effects.\nhow any shards of wyrdstone they have found. They can then\nsell the shards of wyrdstone for gold crowns.\n                                                                     5. UPDATE ROSTER\n                                                                     These steps are carried out in order:\n4. POST-BATTLE ACTIONS                                                         A.        Delete Dead or Retiring Warriors\nEach Leader or Champion in the warband can make one post-                      B.        Visit the Trading Post\nbattle action. Each of these actions is carried out one at a time,             C.        Gains Boons from Exploration\nin an order of the controlling player’s choice. Warriors who are               D.        Distribute Equipment\nin recovery or who have been Captured, cannot make post-                       E.        Update Warband Rating\nbattle actions. Unless otherwise stated, the same action can be\nmade more than once.                                                 In Recovery: if a warrior missed this battle because they were\n                                                                     recovering, their In Recovery box on the warband roster will\n                                                                     have been cleared during the Wrap-up."},{"page":145,"text":"Recruit Hangers-on: The warband can spend gold crowns to\nA. DELETE DEAD OR RETIRING WARRIORS\n                                                                       add a Hanger-on to their roster. Their Reputation must be\nDead warriors are deleted from the roster. Their equipment\n                                                                       sufficient to allow this.\n(except for armour) is added to the warband’s Stash as long as\ntheir warband had at least one warrior on the battlefield at the\n                                                                       Sell Unwanted Equipment: Any equipment in the warband’s\nend of the battle, or if the warrior was taken to the Physician\n                                                                       Stash can be sold. The item is deleted from the Stash, and the\nbut still died (either because the warband could not pay for\n                                                                       warband gains its value in gold crowns, minus D6x10 (to a\ntheir treatment, or there were complications). Otherwise, the\n                                                                       minimum of five).\ndead warrior's equipment is lost.\nAlso, at this point, the controlling player can choose to retire\n                                                                       Purchase Equipment: The warband can purchase any\nwarriors – usually because Lasting Injuries have rendered them\n                                                                       equipment from their Warband Type Equipment List at the\nunfit for battle. These warriors are deleted from the roster, and\n                                                                       price shown, adding it to their Stash. They can also purchase\ntheir equipment is added to the warband’s Stash. Equipment in\n                                                                       Common equipment from the Trading Post, at the price\nthe warband’s Stash can be sold or transferred to a new warrior\n                                                                       shown. They cannot use this action to purchase Rare\nin the next step.\n                                                                       equipment from the Trading Post – that can only be obtained\n                                                                       with the Seek Rare Equipment action, as follows:\nLOSS OF A LEADER\nIf a warband‘s Leader is killed or is retired, a new Leader must\n                                                                       Seek Rare Equipment: This action is only performed once and\nbe nominated from among the warband’s Champions. If it has\n                                                                       is done to determine the availability of Rare items on offer at\nno Champions, the new Leader must be either a Veteran or\n                                                                       the Trading Post or the Black Market. Roll 2D6 to determine\nRaw Recruits. If it has no Veterans or Raw Recruits, the new\n                                                                       the availability of items, adding the following bonuses:\nLeader is a Henchmen.\n                                                                            • +2 if the warband’s Leader is making a Trade post-\nIn any case, the eligible warrior with the best Leadership must\n                                                                                 battle action.\nbe selected as the new leader. If more than one eligible warrior\n                                                                            • +1 for each Champion making a Trade post-battle\nis drawn for best Leadership, use Advancements as a tie-\n                                                                                 action.\nbreaker; it there is still a tie, the controlling player can decide.\n                                                                            • +1 for every full 10 Reputation the warband has (for\nWhen a warrior is promoted in this way, their Type is changed\n                                                                                 example, a warband with Reputation 24 would get\nto Leader on the warband roster, and from now on they count\n                                                                                 +2).\nas a Leader for determining which equipment and skill sets\n                                                                            • +/-X as from a specified special rule.\nthey can access. Their characteristics do not change.\n                                                                       The result is the Availability level – the higher it is, the rarer\nB. VISIT THE TRADING POST                                              the equipment that is on offer. The warband can now purchase\nThe warband can make any of the Trading Post actions                   Rare items from the Trading Post with a Rarity value equal to\ndescribed as follows, allowing them to hire new warriors and           or lower than the Availability level. Any items that are\nbuy or sell equipment. The actions can be taken in any order,          purchased are immediately added to the warband’s Stash.\nand there is no limit to how many times a warband can\nperform each one. Any spent gold crowns are deducted from              C. GAIN BOONS FROM EXPLORATION\nthe warband’s Stash; any gained gold crowns are added to the\n                                                                       Some Exploration results grant a warband additional recruits,\nwarband’s Stash.\n                                                                       Hangers-on, or equipment – see Exploration Chart for details.\n\nHire a Warrior: The warband can hire a new warrior from\n                                                                       D. DISTRIBUTE EQUIPMENT\ntheir Warband Type list, paying for them as they did when\n                                                                       Any equipment in the warband’s Stash, or gained as a\nfounding the warband. No equipment is purchased for them –\n                                                                       Exploration Chart result, can now be distributed among its\nthey receive equipment in the next step.\n                                                                       warriors. Weapon choices must respect the restrictions shown\n                                                                       in the warband's Warband Type list – for example, a Flagellant\nGANG COMPOSITION                                                       could not be equipped with a crossbow. Also, the limit of no\nThe Warband Composition section of the Warband Type List               more than three weapons must be adhered to, with the Two-\nmust be honoured when hiring new warriors. For example, if a           Handed weapon trait taking the space of two.\nwarband with a Reputation of 9 already has two Hangers-on, it          Once any equipment has been added to a Warrior card, the\ncannot hire any more. Similarly, if a warband has fewer                card’s gold crowns value is updated accordingly. If the warrior\nHenchmen (including Veterans) than its total number of                 is equipped with an item that has two different costs – one in\nLeaders, Champions and Raw Recruits, only Henchmen can be              the warrior’s Warband Type Equipment list and the other in\nhired until this is no longer the case."},{"page":146,"text":"the Trading Post – the value in the Warband Type list takes         random and added to the rest of the warband’s Warrior cards\nprecedence.                                                         before any cards are drawn. This means that only one of this\nPlayers are reminded that no warrior can discard a weapon           warrior’s cards can be drawn for the battle, and that the\nonce added to their Warrior cards. Leaders and Champions            controlling player cannot choose which of their equipment sets\nhowever can have multiple equipment sets as described below.        they will be using.\n                                                                    When distributing equipment from the warband’s Stash, it can\nEQUIPMENT SETS                                                      be moved to any or all of a Leader or Champion’s cards, and\nThe senior members of warbands often maintain a cache of            can even be moved to more than one.\nweapons that allows them to equip themselves appropriately\nfor each battle. As such, a warrior with the Tools of the Trade     UPDATING WARBAND RATING\nspecial rule can have multiple Warrior cards, each representing     Recalculate the warband’s Warband Rating, and update the\na different set of equipment. An appropriate model should be        roster accordingly. Note that this is not done until this step,\navailable for each. There is no additional cost for having          meaning that any other references to the Warband Rating in\nmultiple equipment sets; the controlling player can make  